oxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    31→    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    34→    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    37→    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    40→    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    43→    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    46→    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    49→    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    52→    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n    53→\n    54→---\n    55→\n    56→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    57→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50ce05b6-fbb2-48af-b483-350129d29c8d","uuid":"52c9f88e-9cfe-44db-af93-3def24d431b2","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n\nLayout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n\n*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n\n*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n\n*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n\n*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778273169896,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gsn2LmBkaeaim9wJ7ZgtMS","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 1 — Cover\n     2→\n     3→Cover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n    11→*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n    12→*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n    13→*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n    14→*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n    15→*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n    16→*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n    17→*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n    18→*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n    19→*   Private Hydrants: 1\n    20→*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n    25→*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n    26→*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n    27→*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n    28→*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n    29→*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n    30→*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n    31→*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n    32→*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n    33→\n    34→---\n    35→\n    36→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    37→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad5307f2-d9b7-488b-8d54-395eaf0212d6","uuid":"608ab2ba-60fc-4751-8289-f631030fac52","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 1 — Cover\n\nCover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n*   Private Hydrants: 1\n*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
