{"level":30,"time":1778273662689,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jx5U4ZakSfLASp5tHJdgY4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Block 3\n     2→\n     3→## notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter 344 and other specific regulations.\n     4→\n     5→IRRIGATION NOTES:\n     6→AUTOMATIC IRRIGATION SYSTEMS SHALL COMPLY WITH TCEQ CHAPTER 344, AS WELL AS THE FOLLOWING REQUIREMENTS:\n     7→\n     8→1. THESE REQUIREMENTS SHALL BE NOTED ON THE SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT AND SHALL BE IMPLEMENTED AS PART OF THE LANDSCAPE INSPECTION:\n     9→a. THE SYSTEM MUST PROVIDE A MOISTURE LEVEL ADEQUATE TO SUSTAIN GROWTH OF THE PLANT MATERIALS;\n    10→b. THE SYSTEM DOES NOT INCLUDE SPRAY IRRIGATION ON AREAS LESS THAN TEN (10) FEET WIDE (SUCH AS MEDIANS, BUFFER STRIPS, AND PARKING LOT ISLANDS);\n    11→c. CIRCUIT REMOTE CONTROL VALVES HAVE ADJUSTABLE FLOW CONTROLS;\n    12→d. SERVICEABLE IN-HEAD CHECK VALVES AREA ADJACENT TO PAVED AREAS WHERE ELEVATION DIFFERENCES MAY CAUSE LOW HEAD DRAINAGE;\n    13→e. A MASTER VALVE INSTALLED ON THE DISCHARGE SIDE OF THE BACKFLOW PREVENTER;\n    14→f. ABOVE-GROUND IRRIGATION EMISSION DEVICES ARE SET BACK AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES FROM IMPERVIOUS SURFACES;\n    15→g. AN AUTOMATIC RAIN SHUT-OFF DEVICE SHUTS OFF THE IRRIGATION SYSTEM AUTOMATICALLY AFTER MORE THAN A ONE-HALF INCH (1/2\") RAINFALL; AND\n    16→h. NEWLY PLANTED TREES SHALL HAVE PERMANENT IRRIGATION CONSISTING OF DRIP OR BUBBLERS.\n    17→\n    18→2. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL DEVELOP AND PROVIDE AN AS-BUILT DESIGN PLAN TO THE CITY AT THE TIME THE FINAL IRRIGATION INSPECTION IS PERFORMED;\n    19→a. UNLESS FISCAL SECURITY IS PROVIDED TO THE CITY FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE SYSTEM, IT MUST BE OPERATIONAL AT THE TIME OF THE FINAL LANDSCAPE INSPECTION.\n    20→\n    21→3. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL ALSO PROVIDE EXHIBITS TO BE PERMANENTLY INSTALLED INSIDE OR ATTACHED TO THE IRRIGATION CONTROLLER, INCLUDING:\n    22→a. A LAMINATED COPY OF THE WATER BUDGET CONTAINING ZONE NUMBERS, PRECIPITATION RATE, GALLONS PER MINUTE AND THE LOCATION OF THE ISOLATION VALVE; AND AN AS BUILT PLAN.\n    23→\n    24→4. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL PROVIDE A REPORT TO THE CITY ON A FORM PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER CERTIFYING COMPLIANCE WITH SUBSECTION 1. WHEN THE FINAL PLUMBING INSPECTION IS PERFORMED BY THE CITY.\n    25→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90431bd8-bd79-4eb9-bd46-3969546723e7","uuid":"994c3ced-1e1a-4262-a152-e74a9ceb6563","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/block-3.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Block 3\n\n## notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter 344 and other specific regulations.\n\nIRRIGATION NOTES:\nAUTOMATIC IRRIGATION SYSTEMS SHALL COMPLY WITH TCEQ CHAPTER 344, AS WELL AS THE FOLLOWING REQUIREMENTS:\n\n1. THESE REQUIREMENTS SHALL BE NOTED ON THE SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT AND SHALL BE IMPLEMENTED AS PART OF THE LANDSCAPE INSPECTION:\na. THE SYSTEM MUST PROVIDE A MOISTURE LEVEL ADEQUATE TO SUSTAIN GROWTH OF THE PLANT MATERIALS;\nb. THE SYSTEM DOES NOT INCLUDE SPRAY IRRIGATION ON AREAS LESS THAN TEN (10) FEET WIDE (SUCH AS MEDIANS, BUFFER STRIPS, AND PARKING LOT ISLANDS);\nc. CIRCUIT REMOTE CONTROL VALVES HAVE ADJUSTABLE FLOW CONTROLS;\nd. SERVICEABLE IN-HEAD CHECK VALVES AREA ADJACENT TO PAVED AREAS WHERE ELEVATION DIFFERENCES MAY CAUSE LOW HEAD DRAINAGE;\ne. A MASTER VALVE INSTALLED ON THE DISCHARGE SIDE OF THE BACKFLOW PREVENTER;\nf. ABOVE-GROUND IRRIGATION EMISSION DEVICES ARE SET BACK AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES FROM IMPERVIOUS SURFACES;\ng. AN AUTOMATIC RAIN SHUT-OFF DEVICE SHUTS OFF THE IRRIGATION SYSTEM AUTOMATICALLY AFTER MORE THAN A ONE-HALF INCH (1/2\") RAINFALL; AND\nh. NEWLY PLANTED TREES SHALL HAVE PERMANENT IRRIGATION CONSISTING OF DRIP OR BUBBLERS.\n\n2. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL DEVELOP AND PROVIDE AN AS-BUILT DESIGN PLAN TO THE CITY AT THE TIME THE FINAL IRRIGATION INSPECTION IS PERFORMED;\na. UNLESS FISCAL SECURITY IS PROVIDED TO THE CITY FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE SYSTEM, IT MUST BE OPERATIONAL AT THE TIME OF THE FINAL LANDSCAPE INSPECTION.\n\n3. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL ALSO PROVIDE EXHIBITS TO BE PERMANENTLY INSTALLED INSIDE OR ATTACHED TO THE IRRIGATION CONTROLLER, INCLUDING:\na. A LAMINATED COPY OF THE WATER BUDGET CONTAINING ZONE NUMBERS, PRECIPITATION RATE, GALLONS PER MINUTE AND THE LOCATION OF THE ISOLATION VALVE; AND AN AS BUILT PLAN.\n\n4. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL PROVIDE A REPORT TO THE CITY ON A FORM PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER CERTIFYING COMPLIANCE WITH SUBSECTION 1. WHEN THE FINAL PLUMBING INSPECTION IS PERFORMED BY THE CITY.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778273662689,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018UMroYa8DFqs5TojrrMxms","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"That block just has irrigation notes. Let me think about what I need to do:\n\nFrom the vision check, I found that there are trees planted very close to (within 1-2 feet or AT) the overhead electric line on the south and southwest portions of the property. This is a clear violation of the 15-foot minimum clearance requirement.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Identify the specific species of these trees\n2. Verify their utility-compatible status and mature heights\n3. Determine if they meet any exceptions\n\nThe plant schedule from Sheet 35 lists these species being planted:\n- 2x Live Oak (Quercus virginiana)\n- 10x Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia)\n- 2x Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora)\n- 6x Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana)\n- Plus shrubs and groundcovers\n\nNow I need to check the ECM Appendix F to see the utility-compatible status of these species. The grouping guide mentioned that \"Utility-compatible trees\" are marked with \"x\" in the UC column of ECM Appendix F.\n\nLet me search for any ECM Appendix F references in the site plan or look for a way to verify the utility-compatible status of these species. I should also note that I don't have direct access to ECM Appendix F in the workspace, but I may find cross-references in the plan documents.\n\nLet me check if there's any supplementary document that references utility compatibility or if there are any special notes in the plan about this.\n\nActually, let me think about what I know from the grouping guide:\n- Utility-compatible trees are those marked \"UC\" in ECM Appendix F\n- Large trees (mature height 40+ feet) have different requirements\n- Common Austin area species that are typically utility-compatible include: crepe myrtle, Mexican redbud, desert willow, Texas mountain laurel\n\n\n- Species that are typically NOT utility-compatible include: live oak, cedar elm, native oaks\n\nLooking at the planted species: Live Oak and Cedar Elm are both large trees (40-50+ feet at maturity) and not utility-compatible, which creates a significant problem given their proximity to the overhead line. Texas Mountain Laurel and Mexican Redbud are smaller (15-25 feet) and typically marked as utility-compatible in ECM standards. I need to verify this against the actual appendix to confirm the violation severity.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":937,"cache_read_input_tokens":53338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":937},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90431bd8-bd79-4eb9-bd46-3969546723e7","uuid":"dff2f580-eaaf-490f-86d4-b7200fddddbf"}
