ing the presence of bollards at any of these locations on this specific sheet."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b2369d5-d10d-43cc-a9bd-10ac3946c3f9","uuid":"b3123281-a7fe-45e9-b115-195ae73f0e92","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here is the requested information:\n\n**1. Are any of the transformer pads located within 4 feet of parking areas, drive aisles, or vehicle circulation routes?**\n\nYes. There are four locations explicitly labeled with a callout pointing to an **\"Electrical Transformer Pad.\"** Based on the provided scale (Scale 1\" = 20') located in the top right corner, all four of these pads appear to be located immediately adjacent to (well within 4 feet of) the paved drive aisles, parking areas, or vehicle circulation routes.\n\n*   **Pad 1:** Located in the top-left quadrant, situated on the inside curve of the main entrance drive aisle, adjacent to the unit marked \"Bldg. 1\".\n*   **Pad 2:** Located on the mid-left side of the plan, situated immediately adjacent to the drive aisle/parking area edge, near the units marked \"Bldg. 2\" and \"Bldg. 8\".\n*   **Pad 3:** Located on the mid-right side of the plan, situated immediately adjacent to the drive aisle/parking area edge, near the units marked \"Bldg. 5\" and \"Bldg. 4\".\n*   **Pad 4:** Located in the lower-middle section of the plan, situated immediately adjacent to the drive aisle edge, near the units marked \"Bldg. 6\" and \"Bldg. 7\".\n\n**2. If yes, are bollards (protective metal posts) shown and dimensioned around those transformer pads?**\n\n**No.** Upon close inspection of the drafting around all four labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, there are no symbols (such as small circles or squares typically used to denote posts) drawn around the perimeter of the pads. Furthermore, there are no text callouts, labels, or dimensions indicating the presence of bollards at any of these locations on this specific sheet."}]}
