{"level":30,"time":1778273691461,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01ArN7XaCpqKuu7q3dMggcC5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very important! The vision check found that the \"M\" (mitigation) trees on the landscape plan are NOT identified by species on Sheet 31. The system found these trees are near the overhead electric line on the south property line, but there's no species identification for them on the landscape plan itself.\n\nThe plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists the species of trees being planted, but the landscape plan (Sheet 31) doesn't show which specific species correspond to the \"M\" symbols on the drawing.\n\nThis is a deficiency! The grouping requirement EL-2.10 states: \"Plant legend or plant schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities.\"\n\nThe mitigation trees on the landscape plan are near the OHE line but their species are not identified on that plan.\n\nNow let me also check:\n1. If there are large trees (40+ feet) near the overhead lines\n2. Check the utility compatibility of the proposed species\n3. Look for issues with measurement methodology\n4. Check for trees near other electric equipment\n\nLet me continue investigating the plant species and their utility compatibility.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":754,"cache_read_input_tokens":53907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":754},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e1eed96-d749-4c9f-b941-3ae8c1ee87e2","uuid":"8a8a233a-d854-4b02-ada8-02529e4f0e80"}
