{"level":30,"time":1778273701449,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PUdner19RrXB1DpVWhWrH1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan, yes, overhead electric lines and poles are shown. \n\nHere is the description of their routing relative to the proposed buildings and structures:\n\n*   **Visual Representation:** Overhead electric lines are indicated by dashed lines with the label **`--- OHE ---`**. Poles are generally indicated by small circle symbols along these lines.\n*   **Western Routing:** An **`--- OHE ---`** line runs roughly parallel to the western property line (along the street frontage). It routes to the west of **Bldg. 1** and **Bldg. 8**, separated from the buildings by a sidewalk, retaining walls, and a driveway.\n*   **Southern Routing:** The **`--- OHE ---`** line continues and runs along the entire southern property line. It routes to the south of **Bldg. 8** and **Bldg. 7**, separated from the buildings by a driveway and proposed retaining walls. \n*   **Overall Proximity:** The overhead electric lines are routed strictly along the outer perimeter (West and South boundaries) of the site. They do not cross over any of the proposed buildings or internal structures. Utility poles are visible at various points along this perimeter routing, such as near the corners of the property."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d95a2e27-fdb9-4bac-a4d1-7990111a8624","uuid":"23b77b48-b7da-43bc-842d-6748127bc02c","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan, yes, overhead electric lines and poles are shown. \n\nHere is the description of their routing relative to the proposed buildings and structures:\n\n*   **Visual Representation:** Overhead electric lines are indicated by dashed lines with the label **`--- OHE ---`**. Poles are generally indicated by small circle symbols along these lines.\n*   **Western Routing:** An **`--- OHE ---`** line runs roughly parallel to the western property line (along the street frontage). It routes to the west of **Bldg. 1** and **Bldg. 8**, separated from the buildings by a sidewalk, retaining walls, and a driveway.\n*   **Southern Routing:** The **`--- OHE ---`** line continues and runs along the entire southern property line. It routes to the south of **Bldg. 8** and **Bldg. 7**, separated from the buildings by a driveway and proposed retaining walls. \n*   **Overall Proximity:** The overhead electric lines are routed strictly along the outer perimeter (West and South boundaries) of the site. They do not cross over any of the proposed buildings or internal structures. Utility poles are visible at various points along this perimeter routing, such as near the corners of the property."}]}
