ine labeled \"**-W-**\" (water), with the \"**-OHE-**\" line located further south near the boundary.\n*   South of **Bldg. 7**: A dimension of \"**21.3'**\" is shown between the building corner (Unit 705) and the southern property line.\n*   East of **Bldg. 6**: A dimension of \"**21.3'**\" is shown between the building and the eastern property line.\n*   East of **Bldg. 5**: A dimension of \"**19.3'**\" is shown between the building and the eastern property line."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c202df16-5633-43ec-a785-1c53dfb8863e","uuid":"3814c1dc-905b-4388-a827-7dc37c03400a","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan document, here are the details regarding overhead electric lines and utility infrastructure:\n\n**Are overhead electric lines or overhead utility infrastructure shown on the main site plan?**\nYes.\n\n**What is their location relative to the proposed buildings?**\nOverhead utility lines, identified by the line-type label \"**-OHE-**\", are shown running along two primary boundaries of the site relative to the proposed buildings:\n1.  **Southern Boundary:** An **-OHE-** line runs roughly parallel to the southern property line, located south of proposed **Bldg. 8**, **Bldg. 7**, and **Bldg. 6**.\n2.  **Eastern Boundary:** Another **-OHE-** line runs roughly parallel to the eastern property line, located east of proposed **Bldg. 5** and **Bldg. 6**. Utility pole symbols (small circles with connecting lines) are visible along this route, including one near the northeast corner of the site adjacent to the \"Existing Apartment Building\" and another near the southeast corner.\n3.  **Off-site/Street:** There is also an **-OHE-** line shown crossing the street near the top left (northwest) corner of the drawing, near a utility pole labeled \"**AT&T Pole**\".\n\n**What clearances are shown?**\nThere are **no explicit clearance dimensions or zones labeled specifically for the overhead electrical lines** (such as a 