{"level":30,"time":1778274085590,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LxtvP7Z77VKWKjU93hTV3v","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c202df16-5633-43ec-a785-1c53dfb8863e","uuid":"e2e38398-72be-4228-8fc4-5730907d2b18","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778274085590,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Pfe5pMZvY4ifCe49qZCkH4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The Electric Review section explicitly lists the exact code sections that are required for this project:\n- UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n- UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n- UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n\nThis confirms that the grouping is applicable and these are the exact standards I need to verify.\n\nThe Master Comment Report mentions there's a Bluebeam link with Austin Energy's specific comments, but I cannot access external links. However, the fact that they've cited UCM § 1.10.3 (Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities) means they expect the plans to address clearances.\n\nNow let me summarize what I've found so far:\n\n**KEY FINDINGS FROM RESEARCH (Step 3):**\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Lines - EXIST:**\n   - Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey): Shows overhead utility poles and electric lines (marked \"OH\" or \"OHE\")\n   - Located along western boundary (Valley View Road) with service drops crossing into property to existing building\n   - Located along southern and eastern boundaries per Sheet 9\n   - One overhead line on north boundary in adjacent property\n\n2. **Site Plan Shows Overhead Lines:**\n   - Sheet 9 (Site Plan): Shows \"-OHE-\" (overhead electric) lines on southern and eastern boundaries\n   - Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan): Explicitly shows overhead electric lines (OHE) in the drawing\n   - NO explicit clearance dimensions shown\n\n3. **Buildings and Proposed Features:**\n   - 8 new multi-family buildings proposed (Buildings 1-8)\n   - Buildings located 19.3' to 28.8' from property boundaries where overhead lines exist\n   - No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations provided\n   - No profile sections showing vertical clearances from overhead lines to buildings\n\n4. **Critical Missing Documentation:**\n   - NO surveyed conductor elevation data on building elevation sheets\n   - NO measured clearance dimensions from outside conductor to buildings\n   - NO profile views showing vertical clearances\n   - NO clearance verification for building projections (overhangs, roofs, etc.)\n   - NO landscape clearance analysis (trees near overhead lines - though trees shown on landscape plan)\n   - NO driveways shown with overhead clearances marked\n   - NO notification requirement note about 48-hour notification to Austin Energy\n\n5. **Regulatory Requirements Being Checked:**\n   - UCM § 1.10.3 specifies:\n     - 7.5-foot horizontal sky\n\n-to-ground clearance from all primary, neutral, secondary conductors\n     - 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary and neutral conductors\n   - Buildings must maintain these clearances\n   - Building projections must maintain clearances\n   - Driveways must maintain 16-18 feet vertical clearance depending on truck traffic\n\nNow I need to systematically work through each of the 47 checklist items. The site has overhead lines and proposed buildings, so several items apply directly: buildings need 7.5' horizontal clearance from conductors (EL-1.1), customer facilities require 15' radial clearance (EL-1.2), building projections must be verified (EL-1.3), buildings near ROW with overhead lines need documentation (EL-1.6), surveyed conductor elevations must appear on building elevation sheets (EL-1.7), and section views are needed (EL-1.8).\n\nAdditional applicable items include plan exhibits with dimensions from conductor to building edges (EL-1.23), clearance dimensions measured from outside conductor (EL-1.23), registered surveyor documentation of conductor locations (EL-1.31), landscape clearances from overhead lines for trees (EL-1.37), 10-foot radial clearance for construction staging areas (EL-1.45), and 48-hour notification requirement for Austin Energy (EL-1.46).\n\nSeveral items don't apply since they're not proposed: gas pump canopies (EL-1.4), stairs/elevated walkways/platforms (EL-1.5), new fences (EL-1.9), fence posts (EL-1.10), and fence-related items (EL-1.11).\n\nFencing near substations (EL-1.11) and transmission lines (EL-1.12) are inapplicable—no substation or transmission lines exist on site. Vehicle barrier fencing (EL-1.13), emergency access structures (EL-1.16), and roads under transmission lines (EL-1.20) aren't proposed. However, retaining walls are proposed and need verification for proximity to overhead lines (EL-1.14), as do driveways for vertical clearance (EL-1.18) and existing parking areas (EL-1.19). Retaining wall section exhibits apply if walls are near lines (EL-1.17).\n\nMoving forward, poles potentially blocking proposed driveways require checking (EL-1.22), and proposed streetlights need location verification relative to overhead lines (EL-1.24). Sidewalks are planned but their relationship to property line ROW must be confirmed (EL-1.25). Trash area location relative to overhead lines needs assessment (EL-1.26), and proposed water meters and lines require clearance verification (EL-1.28, EL-1.29). Facilities under or over distribution lines are absolutely prohibited (EL-1.27). Building foundations must be checked for the 5-foot property line setback requirement (EL-1.30).\n\nBuildings are positioned 19-28 feet from the boundary, which appears to satisfy setback requirements. New overhead line crossings and secondary line configurations only apply if new lines are being added (EL-1.32, EL-1.33). Marquee signs aren't shown on the plans. New power poles near existing infrastructure need electrical design review (EL-1.35), and decorative lighting placement should be verified against the lighting plan (EL-1.36). Meter locations and potential obstruction must be checked in the electrical and utility plans (EL-1.38). Streetlight proximity to buildings is possible and should be reviewed (EL-1.39). Down guy wires and their anchor easements require survey verification (EL-1.40, EL-1.42), though transmission guy easements don't apply here. Transformer clearances need to be confirmed.\n\nTransformer placement relative to overhead lines and service-mast roof clearances both require review of the electrical plan. I should conduct a detailed evaluation of each item and perform a comprehensive clearance check of the main building areas to better understand the spatial relationships.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":64252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":641},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c202df16-5633-43ec-a785-1c53dfb8863e","uuid":"f64709cb-9b94-4a7d-97c0-1c1968a82b46"}
