{"level":30,"time":1778274219690,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BrhNfJ8Z4n8e74BdpBTJBp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I've successfully completed the site plan review for the Electric/Clearances grouping (Grouping 2 - Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\nMy findings identified:\n- 2 FAIL conditions: EL-2.7 (pad-mounted equipment clearances) and EL-2.9 (root barriers)\n- 6 NOT-VERIFIABLE conditions: EL-2.1, EL-2.6, EL-2.8, EL-2.15\n- 6 PASS conditions: EL-2.3, EL-2.10, EL-2.11, EL-2.12, EL-2.13, EL-2.14\n- 4 N/A conditions: EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5\n\nThe critical violations are the transformer clearances (EL-2.7) where trees are planted too close (4.2 and 6.2 feet from transformers when 10 feet is required), and the lack of root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment (EL-2.9).\n\nThe not-verifiable items primarily stem from missing ECM Appendix F data to confirm utility-compatible designations and missing Austin Energy coordination approval letters.\n\nThe review is now complete and the structured output has been successfully submitted.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8491,"cache_read_input_tokens":69420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8491},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90431bd8-bd79-4eb9-bd46-3969546723e7","uuid":"cb12cef4-cb6a-43db-82cb-9e4b784fdc96"}
{"level":30,"time":1778274219690,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BrhNfJ8Z4n8e74BdpBTJBp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete\n\nI have completed the site plan review for **Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** for the Valley View Townhomes project (SP-2025-0126C).\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**CRITICAL DEFICIENCIES (FAIL):**\n- **EL-2.7**: Two electrical transformer pads are too close to tree plantings:\n  - Transformer west of Building 1: only 6.2 feet from nearest tree (requires 10 feet minimum)\n  - Transformer west of Building 8: only 4.2 feet from nearest tree (requires 10 feet minimum)\n- **EL-2.9**: No root barriers specified for trees planted within 20 feet of underground electrical transformers\n\n**CANNOT VERIFY (NOT-VERIFIABLE):**\n- **EL-2.1**: Trees planted extremely close (0-2 feet) to overhead electric line along south boundary cannot be verified as utility-compatible without ECM Appendix F documentation\n- **EL-2.6**: Utility pole locations not clearly marked on plans; distances cannot be verified\n- **EL-2.8**: Underground equipment clearances not sufficiently documented for all pull boxes and conduits\n- **EL-2.15**: No Austin Energy written approval found for trees planted in restricted clearance zones; cannot verify compliance without utility-compatible designation confirmation\n\n**COMPLIANT ITEMS (PASS):**\n- Plant species are clearly identified in schedule\n- Large trees are differentiated by size\n- Trees are shown in relation to overhead facilities on plans\n- Measurement methodology appears correct\n\nThe structured findings have been submitted for applicant response."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8491,"cache_read_input_tokens":69420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8491},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90431bd8-bd79-4eb9-bd46-3969546723e7","uuid":"1cf3443b-c250-442d-8f8d-fbb3d29a6713"}
{"level":30,"time":1778274219690,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1013333,"duration_api_ms":195513,"num_turns":23,"result":"## Review Complete\n\nI have completed the site plan review for **Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** for the Valley View Townhomes project (SP-2025-0126C).\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**CRITICAL DEFICIENCIES (FAIL):**\n- **EL-2.7**: Two electrical transformer pads are too close to tree plantings:\n  - Transformer west of Building 1: only 6.2 feet from nearest tree (requires 10 feet minimum)\n  - Transformer west of Building 8: only 4.2 feet from nearest tree (requires 10 feet minimum)\n- **EL-2.9**: No root barriers specified for trees planted within 20 feet of underground electrical transformers\n\n**CANNOT VERIFY (NOT-VERIFIABLE):**\n- **EL-2.1**: Trees planted extremely close (0-2 feet) to overhead electric line along south boundary cannot be verified as utility-compatible without ECM Appendix F documentation\n- **EL-2.6**: Utility pole locations not clearly marked on plans; distances cannot be verified\n- **EL-2.8**: Underground equipment clearances not sufficiently documented for all pull boxes and conduits\n- **EL-2.15**: No Austin Energy written approval found for trees planted in restricted clearance zones; cannot verify compliance without utility-compatible designation confirmation\n\n**COMPLIANT ITEMS (PASS):**\n- Plant species are clearly identified in schedule\n- Large trees are differentiated by size\n- Trees are shown in relation to overhead facilities on plans\n- Measurement methodology appears correct\n\nThe structured findings have been submitted for applicant response.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"90431bd8-bd79-4eb9-bd46-3969546723e7","total_cost_usd":0.2481136,"usage":{"input_tokens":116,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53198,"cache_read_input_tokens":821451,"output_tokens":19871,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53198,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":116,"outputTokens":19871,"cacheReadInputTokens":821451,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53198,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2481136,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["south property boundary adjacent to overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees (likely Texas Mountain Laurel and Mexican Redbud per plant schedule) are shown planted 0-2 lateral feet from the overhead electric line on the south property boundary, within the <15-foot distribution clearance zone. While the grouping regulatory overview identifies Texas Mountain Laurel as a utility-compatible species example, the plans do not include independent verification of utility-compatible designation per ECM Appendix F for the specific species shown, nor is any Austin Energy written approval for this proximity provided. Cannot verify compliance without ECM Appendix F confirmation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements of the landscape plan show trees planted 0-2 feet from the OHE line along the south boundary. The plant schedule identifies shade trees (100-gallon container size) and ornamental trees (45-gallon container size) with species including Texas Mountain Laurel and Mexican Redbud.","reasoning":"Trees within 15 feet of distribution conductors are only permitted if utility-compatible per UCM § 1.10.10.4. While the regulatory overview identifies Texas Mountain Laurel as a utility-compatible example, the submitted plans do not provide independent verification of the ECM Appendix F UC designation for the trees shown at this location, making compliance not verifiable from the provided documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead transmission lines (≥60kV) or transmission easements are identified on the submitted site plans or in the project facts. This checklist item applies only when transmission facilities are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan facts document and all plan sheets reviewed show no transmission lines, transmission easements, or transmission voltage infrastructure. All overhead electric infrastructure shown is distribution-level (the OHE line on the south boundary).","reasoning":"Checklist item EL-2.2 is applicability-gated: it applies only when overhead transmission lines are present or proposed. Absence of transmission facilities from all submitted documents constitutes evidence of inapplicability.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["south property boundary near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees planted within 25 feet of the overhead electric distribution line (0-2 feet) are mitigation trees (Texas Mountain Laurel and Mexican Redbud) with mature heights of 20-25 feet and 15-20 feet respectively. Per ECM Appendix F, neither species is classified as a large tree (40+ feet minimum height). No large trees are proposed within the 25-foot distribution clearance zone.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule (Sheet 35) identifies the ornamental trees planted near the south boundary as Texas Mountain Laurel (mature height approximately 20-25 feet) and Mexican Redbud (mature height approximately 15-20 feet). Vision measurements confirm these trees are located 0-2 feet from the OHE line.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) within 25 feet of distribution conductors. The trees shown at this location are not large trees; they are classified as ornamental trees with mature heights well under 40 feet. Therefore, this requirement is satisfied.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead transmission lines are present on the project site. This checklist item is inapplicable when transmission facilities are not proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The facts document and all plan sheets show no transmission-level electrical facilities or transmission easements.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: this requirement applies only when transmission lines are present. The absence of transmission infrastructure from all submissions indicates inapplicability.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement boundaries are depicted on the submitted site plans, and the project facts document indicates no transmission easements are recorded against the property. This requirement applies only when a transmission easement is present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The facts document lists all recorded easements on the property (greenbelt, drainage, wastewater, drainage easements from adjacent platting, utility easements). None are identified as transmission easements. No transmission easement is shown on the grading plan (Sheet 11) or any other plan sheet.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: this requirement is conditional on the presence of a transmission easement. The recorded instruments and plan sheets show no transmission easement, establishing inapplicability.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["property boundary areas where utility poles may be present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While overhead electric poles may be present on or adjacent to the property (consistent with the OHE line shown on the landscape plan), the specific locations of utility poles are not clearly marked or dimensioned on the submitted plans. The distance from proposed trees to any utility pole cannot be verified without explicit pole location identification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows an OHE line label but does not clearly mark individual utility pole locations. The electrical design plan shows underground infrastructure but is labeled as underground service. Utility poles associated with the OHE line may exist but are not explicitly documented with measurements.","reasoning":"Verification requires identifying pole locations on plans and measuring distances from tree symbols to poles. While infrastructure likely exists (OHE line shown), the plans do not provide sufficient documentation of pole locations to measure the required 10-foot clearances.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["area west of Building 1","area west of Building 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical transformer pads (pad-mounted equipment) are proposed within 10 lateral feet of landscaped tree plantings. Transformer west of Building 1 is 6.2 feet from nearest tree symbol; transformer west of Building 8 is 4.2 feet from nearest tree symbol. UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires 10 lateral feet minimum clearance from tree trunks (planting locations) to pad-mounted equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements of the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and cross-reference with landscape plan (Sheet 31) show transformer pads at specific distances from nearest tree symbols: Bldg. 1 transformer at 6.2 feet, Bldg. 8 transformer at 4.2 feet from trees.","reasoning":"Both measured distances fall short of the 10-foot minimum clearance required by UCM § 1.10.10.4. These are deficiencies requiring tree relocation or equipment relocation to achieve the required clearance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["vicinity of electrical equipment on property"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformers and pull boxes as underground electrical infrastructure. While measurements confirm trees are within 5-10 feet of transformers, the exact locations and clearances to other underground equipment (pull boxes, conduit locations) are not sufficiently detailed in the submitted plans to verify complete compliance with the 5-foot underground equipment clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electrical infrastructure including transformers, pull boxes, and underground lines, but the landscape plan does not overlay this infrastructure with sufficient clarity to independently verify all clearance measurements from trees to all underground equipment locations.","reasoning":"Complete verification would require either cross-referenced utility overlay drawings or explicit clearance dimensions on the landscape plan. The available documents show transformers at 4-6 feet but do not provide comprehensive documentation of all underground equipment locations relative to all proposed plantings.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["area west of Building 1","area west of Building 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical transformers (at 4.2 and 6.2 feet per measured distances). UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from underground equipment) for trees within this zone. The landscape calculations and plant schedule (Sheet 35) do not include specifications for root barriers for trees in proximity to transformers.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show transformers at 4.2 and 6.2 feet from tree plantings. The comprehensive plant schedule on Sheet 35, including landscape construction notes and special construction techniques, does not reference root barrier installation for protection of underground electrical equipment.","reasoning":"The regulatory requirement is clear: trees within 20 feet of underground equipment require specified root barriers. The submitted plans do not include this required detail. Absence of root barrier specifications in the landscape plan represents a deficiency in meeting the requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["landscape plan and plant schedule sheets"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The plant schedule on Sheet 35 provides complete identification of all proposed trees near electric facilities with both common names and botanical names. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) includes a legend with tree symbols defined. No deficiency in species identification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule lists all shade trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) and ornamental trees (Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) with common and botanical names clearly identified. Sheet 31 legend defines tree symbols (SY, PL, P, M designations).","reasoning":"The requirement for plant legend and schedule completeness is satisfied by the presence of comprehensive species identification and symbol definitions across both sheets.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["landscape plan and plant schedule sheets"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees and small trees are clearly differentiated in the plant schedule by container size (100-gallon shade trees vs. 45-gallon ornamental trees). Mature heights are specified for each species, allowing clear identification of large trees (40+ feet) versus smaller trees.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule (Sheet 35) organizes trees into two categories: Shade Trees (100-gallon minimum) including Live Oak and Cedar Elm, and Ornamental Trees (45-gallon) including Texas Mountain Laurel and Mexican Redbud. Container sizes directly correlate with mature tree size classifications.","reasoning":"The requirement that large trees be differentiated from other trees for clearance verification is met by the explicit size classifications and container sizes provided in the schedule.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["south property boundary","transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance measurements shown or implied in the plans are measured from utility infrastructure locations (OHE line, transformer pads) rather than from pole centerlines. This is the correct measurement methodology per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements of the landscape plan measure distances from the OHE line (shown conductor location) to trees, not from pole centerline. Measurements of transformers similarly measure from the pad-mounted equipment location.","reasoning":"The correct methodology is to measure from outside conductor location or from equipment pad location. The plans and measurements available do not demonstrate measuring from pole centerline, which would be incorrect.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscape plan trees near utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree clearances shown on the landscape plan appear to be measured from tree trunk centerline (planting location indicated by tree symbol) rather than from projected canopy edge. This is the correct methodology per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows trees as discrete symbols (circles with various markings for SY, PL, P, M designations). Distance measurements from these symbols to utilities appear to originate from the symbol center (trunk location), not from an assumed canopy perimeter.","reasoning":"Correct methodology measures from planting location (trunk centerline), not from projected canopy edge. The submitted plans' use of discrete symbols as planting locations supports correct measurement methodology.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["south and southeast property boundary areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) clearly shows tree locations in relation to the overhead electric line (OHE) marked on the drawing. Both trees and utility infrastructure are visible and can be cross-referenced for clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 drawing (Block 2) includes both tree symbols (M designations for mitigation trees) and the utility line marked as OHE along the south property boundary. The features are shown on the same drawing at the same scale, enabling visual and measured comparison.","reasoning":"The requirement that trees be shown in relation to overhead facilities for clearance verification is satisfied by the presence of both features on the landscape plan drawing.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["south property boundary where trees are planted 0-2 feet from overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed 0-2 feet from the overhead electric distribution line, which is within the <15-foot clearance zone where only utility-compatible trees are permitted. Verification of compliance requires confirmation that trees are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F, or production of Austin Energy written approval for non-compatible species. Neither confirmation nor approval documentation is provided with the submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Trees at 0-2 feet from OHE line are within a clearance restriction zone per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The submitted plans do not include Austin Energy approval letters or documentation confirming utility-compatible designation per ECM Appendix F for the specific tree species shown.","reasoning":"Compliance with restricted-zone tree placement requires either: (1) independent verification of utility-compatible status per ECM Appendix F, or (2) explicit Austin Energy written approval for restricted placement. The submitted documents do not provide either verification method, making compliance determination not verifiable from the available materials.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"34dec48a-fdfa-4f1e-8c96-b68c0483fe14"}
