{"level":30,"time":1778274502421,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01TNNgPMt1bRGkHwmFWBTps6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key findings so far:\n1. Overhead electric (OHE) lines ARE shown on the site plans\n2. They route along the western and southern property boundaries\n3. NO clearance dimensions are shown from the conductors to buildings or structures\n4. NO surveyed conductor elevations or vertical clearance profiles are shown\n\nThis is a major deficiency. According to the grouping:\n- EL-1.1: Requires buildings to maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal clearance\n- EL-1.8: Requires section and plan view exhibits showing dimensions from conductor to buildings\n- EL-1.23: Requires clearance dimensions measured from outside conductor (not pole centerline)\n- EL-1.31: Requires surveyed conductor elevations and pole locations when vertical clearances are questionable\n\nSince overhead electric facilities are shown on the plans, the applicability conditions are met for many items. Let me now systematically go through all items and evaluate each one.\n\nLet me check if there are any building elevation sheets or detail sheets that might show clearance information.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1103,"cache_read_input_tokens":54891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1103},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d95a2e27-fdb9-4bac-a4d1-7990111a8624","uuid":"b76b1e98-180b-42a4-8b5b-37e2014d3e74"}
