{"level":30,"time":1778274502421,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T84YYmAV5yLfL4PfC97YZK","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 20 — Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile\n     2→\n     3→Utility tap public plan and profile for townhomes project.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the public plan and profile for a proposed utility tap (Water Line A) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the connection to an existing AC water main, the transition to new DI pipe, and the installation of a new fire demand meter, vault, and fire hydrant.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→* Proposed Pipe Segments: 47.0 lf of 8\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 5.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ -0.00% slope), 12.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 3.0 lf of 6\" C900, 5.0 lf of 6\" C900\n    11→* Flowline Elevations: FL 8\" = 674.33', FL In 6\" = 674.42', FL Out 6\" = 674.42'\n    12→* Restraints: 52' of restraints required from Sta 0+00 to Sta 0+52\n    13→* Benchmarks: BM #1 = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n    14→* Pressure Reducing Valve (PRV) Threshold: 65 psi\n    15→* Geologist Inspection Trench Depth Threshold: > 5 feet\n    16→\n    17→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    18→\n    19→* **Block 1**: drawing — Profile View of Water Line A (Wtr-Ln-A). Shows the vertical alignment of the proposed water line from station 0+00 to 0+75, including the transition from AC to DI pipe, reducers, and the meter vault. Use VISION to examine the pipe slopes and relationship to the existing/proposed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\n    20→* **Block 2**: drawing — Plan View of Utility Tap. Top-down layout showing the proposed connection to the existing 6\" water line, the new fire hydrant, vault, and various utility crossings. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the proposed infrastructure and intersections with existing easements and lines.\n    21→* **Block 3**: notes — Restrained Joints Specification. Details the requirement to restrain all bends, tees, and valves using specific SPL standards (WW-27F or WW-27A). READ the block content for the approved mechanical joint restraint standards.\n    22→* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n    23→* **Block 5**: notes — Water Tap Note. Contains instructions for replacing the existing AC pipe with DI pipe. READ the block content for strict asbestos handling and disposal requirements.\n    24→* **Block 6**: notes — Legend. Defines linetypes and symbols used in the plan view. READ the block content to accurately interpret the utility lines (Water, Wastewater, Storm, Electric) in Block 2.\n    25→* **Block 7**: notes — PRV Note. READ the block content for the specific pressure threshold (65 psi) that requires the installation of a pressure reducing valve.\n    26→* **Block 9**: notes — Void and Water Flow Mitigation. READ the block content for the trenching depth threshold (> 5 feet) that triggers a mandatory inspection by a licensed geologist.\n    27→* **Blocks 8, 10, 11, 12, 13**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Includes the legal description, standard disclaimers regarding existing utility locations, general verification notes, the PE Seal for Jason K. Rodgers, and the Texas 811 logo. READ the block content only if verifying administrative details, legal descriptions, or standard utility coordination notes.\n    28→\n    29→---\n    30→\n    31→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    32→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d95a2e27-fdb9-4bac-a4d1-7990111a8624","uuid":"006f307c-1b4b-4eec-b48f-863dfb34ab6c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 20 — Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile\n\nUtility tap public plan and profile for townhomes project.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the public plan and profile for a proposed utility tap (Water Line A) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the connection to an existing AC water main, the transition to new DI pipe, and the installation of a new fire demand meter, vault, and fire hydrant.\n\n**Key values:**\n* Proposed Pipe Segments: 47.0 lf of 8\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 5.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ -0.00% slope), 12.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 3.0 lf of 6\" C900, 5.0 lf of 6\" C900\n* Flowline Elevations: FL 8\" = 674.33', FL In 6\" = 674.42', FL Out 6\" = 674.42'\n* Restraints: 52' of restraints required from Sta 0+00 to Sta 0+52\n* Benchmarks: BM #1 = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n* Pressure Reducing Valve (PRV) Threshold: 65 psi\n* Geologist Inspection Trench Depth Threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n* **Block 1**: drawing — Profile View of Water Line A (Wtr-Ln-A). Shows the vertical alignment of the proposed water line from station 0+00 to 0+75, including the transition from AC to DI pipe, reducers, and the meter vault. Use VISION to examine the pipe slopes and relationship to the existing/proposed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\n* **Block 2**: drawing — Plan View of Utility Tap. Top-down layout showing the proposed connection to the existing 6\" water line, the new fire hydrant, vault, and various utility crossings. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the proposed infrastructure and intersections with existing easements and lines.\n* **Block 3**: notes — Restrained Joints Specification. Details the requirement to restrain all bends, tees, and valves using specific SPL standards (WW-27F or WW-27A). READ the block content for the approved mechanical joint restraint standards.\n* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n* **Block 5**: notes — Water Tap Note. Contains instructions for replacing the existing AC pipe with DI pipe. READ the block content for strict asbestos handling and disposal requirements.\n* **Block 6**: notes — Legend. Defines linetypes and symbols used in the plan view. READ the block content to accurately interpret the utility lines (Water, Wastewater, Storm, Electric) in Block 2.\n* **Block 7**: notes — PRV Note. READ the block content for the specific pressure threshold (65 psi) that requires the installation of a pressure reducing valve.\n* **Block 9**: notes — Void and Water Flow Mitigation. READ the block content for the trenching depth threshold (> 5 feet) that triggers a mandatory inspection by a licensed geologist.\n* **Blocks 8, 10, 11, 12, 13**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Includes the legal description, standard disclaimers regarding existing utility locations, general verification notes, the PE Seal for Jason K. Rodgers, and the Texas 811 logo. READ the block content only if verifying administrative details, legal descriptions, or standard utility coordination notes.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778274502421,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FHhSpznRZtk3y8QnVbiLxv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N169Fhb2muaEyAFsB4YVpv","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/guide.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1583,"cache_read_input_tokens":55994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1583},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d95a2e27-fdb9-4bac-a4d1-7990111a8624","uuid":"d703c609-bd83-44e8-9dd1-561a247394ea"}
{"level":30,"time":1778274502421,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N169Fhb2muaEyAFsB4YVpv","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n     2→\n     3→Plan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n    11→* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n    12→* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n    13→* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n    14→* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n    15→* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n    16→* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n    17→* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n    18→* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n    19→* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n    20→* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    23→\n    24→* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n    25→* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n    26→* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n    27→* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n    28→* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n    29→* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n    30→* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n    31→* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d95a2e27-fdb9-4bac-a4d1-7990111a8624","uuid":"8eaab1f9-4f5f-48d5-a1f5-5478108a924c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n\nPlan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n\n**Key values**:\n* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
