{"level":30,"time":1778274504446,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018CXXrBYD6du2WDfULVfM5D","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 16\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing water main has adequate capacity for the proposed Valley View Townhomes project.\n     4→\n     5→AW\n     6→City of Austin | Austin Water\n     7→6310 Wilhelmina Delco Drive, Suite 3100\n     8→Austin, Texas 78752\n     9→http://www.austintexas.gov/SER\n    10→SER@austintexas.gov\n    11→\n    12→Mr. Jason Rodgers, P.E.\n    13→Bleyl Engineering\n    14→7701 San Felipe Blvd Ste 200\n    15→Austin, Texas 78729\n    16→\n    17→Re: Letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\n    18→3759 Valley View Townhomes Service Extension Request for Water (SER-6324)\n    19→3759 Valley View, Austin, Texas 78704\n    20→\n    21→Dear Mr. Rodgers:\n    22→\n    23→Austin Water has reviewed your submittal for the above referenced Service Extension Request (SER) project and is issuing this letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service in keeping with all current rules and regulations.\n    24→\n    25→Submitted project specifications:\n    26→39 Condo Units (6 to 24 Units/Acre)\n    27→Living Unit Equivalent (LUE): 28\n    28→Subject Tract Area: 3.59 Acres\n    29→Water Demand (Estimated Peak Hour): 60 gpm\n    30→Sprinkled Fire flow requirement of 1,500 gpm and water demand submitted in the engineering calculations received from Jason Rodgers, P.E. of Bleyl Engineering on 10/20/2025.\n    31→\n    32→Based on the submitted project specifications and the results of the Service Extension Request review, it has been determined that the existing 8-inch water main (Drawn. No. 74-0050) in Valley View Rd. is suitable and sufficient to provide service to the subject tract.\n    33→\n    34→Due to the existing suitable and sufficient water main at the subject tract, a water main extension/improvement is not required for this project.\n    35→\n    36→Water service for this project can be provided based upon plan approval within the Austin Water plan review process. It is suggested that this letter be submitted with your site development plans.\n    37→\n    38→This letter will automatically expire 180 days after its date of issue unless a development application has been accepted by the Development Services Department (DSD). If a development application has been accepted by DSD, then this letter expires on the date the development application, or its approval, expires.\n    39→\n    40→If we can provide additional information, please call me at (512) 972-0035.\n    41→\n    42→Sincerely,\n    43→[Signature]\n    44→Christine Perez, P.E.\n    45→Austin Water\n    46→Utility Development Services Division\n    47→\n    48→DATE: 12/10/2025\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d95a2e27-fdb9-4bac-a4d1-7990111a8624","uuid":"8c251766-cc1e-469a-a67f-dcc9dcf27546","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-16.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 16\n\n## text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing water main has adequate capacity for the proposed Valley View Townhomes project.\n\nAW\nCity of Austin | Austin Water\n6310 Wilhelmina Delco Drive, Suite 3100\nAustin, Texas 78752\nhttp://www.austintexas.gov/SER\nSER@austintexas.gov\n\nMr. Jason Rodgers, P.E.\nBleyl Engineering\n7701 San Felipe Blvd Ste 200\nAustin, Texas 78729\n\nRe: Letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\n3759 Valley View Townhomes Service Extension Request for Water (SER-6324)\n3759 Valley View, Austin, Texas 78704\n\nDear Mr. Rodgers:\n\nAustin Water has reviewed your submittal for the above referenced Service Extension Request (SER) project and is issuing this letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service in keeping with all current rules and regulations.\n\nSubmitted project specifications:\n39 Condo Units (6 to 24 Units/Acre)\nLiving Unit Equivalent (LUE): 28\nSubject Tract Area: 3.59 Acres\nWater Demand (Estimated Peak Hour): 60 gpm\nSprinkled Fire flow requirement of 1,500 gpm and water demand submitted in the engineering calculations received from Jason Rodgers, P.E. of Bleyl Engineering on 10/20/2025.\n\nBased on the submitted project specifications and the results of the Service Extension Request review, it has been determined that the existing 8-inch water main (Drawn. No. 74-0050) in Valley View Rd. is suitable and sufficient to provide service to the subject tract.\n\nDue to the existing suitable and sufficient water main at the subject tract, a water main extension/improvement is not required for this project.\n\nWater service for this project can be provided based upon plan approval within the Austin Water plan review process. It is suggested that this letter be submitted with your site development plans.\n\nThis letter will automatically expire 180 days after its date of issue unless a development application has been accepted by the Development Services Department (DSD). If a development application has been accepted by DSD, then this letter expires on the date the development application, or its approval, expires.\n\nIf we can provide additional information, please call me at (512) 972-0035.\n\nSincerely,\n[Signature]\nChristine Perez, P.E.\nAustin Water\nUtility Development Services Division\n\nDATE: 12/10/2025\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
