sed strictly on the provided image (Sheet 28).*\n\n**Are overhead electric lines (OHE) clearly shown and cross-referenced with the tree locations?**\nYes, overhead electric lines are clearly shown on this plan. Near the bottom edge of the site plan area, there is a distinct line running horizontally across the width of the property labeled **\"- OHE -\"**. \n\n**Are the overhead electric lines and tree symbols visible on the same plan sheet such that clearances could be verified?**\nYes. Along that same bottom edge (southern boundary, based on the north arrow), numerous tree canopy symbols (represented by large overlapping circles with center-point crosses) are drawn directly over and adjacent to the **\"- OHE -\"** line. \n\nBecause both the utility line and the proposed/existing tree locations are mapped together on this single landscape plan sheet, a reviewer would be able to visually assess the spatial relationship and potential clearances between the tree canopies and the overhead electric lines."}]}
