{"level":30,"time":1778274524036,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AKVNDVPgzxLKir6L5DJYG6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a precise visual analysis of the provided Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan), here are the findings:\n\n**Overhead Electric Utility Poles:**\nYes, indications of overhead electric utilities are present. \n*   **Location:** Running along the far western boundary (the left side of the drawing, outside the main property line near the street/sidewalk area), there is a continuous dashed line explicitly labeled **`---OHE---`**. \n*   Spaced intermittently along this `---OHE---` line from the top-left down to the bottom-left are small circular symbols that are standard representations for utility poles. \n\n**Pad-Mounted Transformer Boxes and Other Electric Equipment:**\nYes, the plan shows a comprehensive underground electrical layout highlighted in blue, including transformer pads and other equipment. The document explicitly includes the following exact labels:\n\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: There are multiple instances of this exact callout pointing to square blue boxes on the plan (e.g., between Bldg. 1 & 2, near Bldg. 4 & 5, and near Bldg. 7 & 8).\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: There are numerous callouts pointing to smaller circular/square blue symbols scattered throughout the site.\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: There are multiple callouts pointing to rectangular boxes attached to the various buildings (e.g., on Bldg. 1, Bldg. 3, Bldg. 5, etc.).\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Callouts with this text point to the network of solid and dashed blue lines connecting the transformers, pull boxes, and meters throughout the property."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da8d4f94-c433-44b6-bc3f-ac89c89d21c6","uuid":"0d8c76e5-6a5c-43e2-94ba-adfe