nywhere on this document.**\n\nSpecifically regarding the areas adjacent to the transformer pads, I have examined the three locations explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**:\n\n1.  **West side (near Bldg. 2):** Adjacent features include a sidewalk, a curb, an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**, and an **\"Underground Electric Line\"**. There are no stairs or fire escapes visible.\n2.  **East side (between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 5):** Adjacent features include the building footprint, an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**, a sidewalk labeled \"SD\", and an **\"Underground Electric Line\"**. There are no stairs or fire escapes visible.\n3.  **South side (near Bldg. 8 and Bldg. 7):** Adjacent features include a sidewalk, an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**, and an **\"Underground Electric Line\"**. There are no stairs or fire escapes visible.\n\nWhile the building footprints show internal divisions (e.g., \"Unit 801\", \"Unit 802\") and some hatched interior spaces, there is no linework or text indicating exterior stairwells or fire escapes attached to the buildings or located anywhere on the site layout shown on this specific electrical sheet."}]}
