{"level":30,"time":1778274552775,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0182ZzX8KjfkaaZ1HTJLgNr7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"EXCELLENT! Now I have found critical information:\n\nFrom Block 13 (Electric Transmission Notes) - These are for TRANSMISSION lines (the overhead lines I saw on the survey):\n- No trees within transmission easement or within 25 feet of transmission structure base\n- No digging/grading within 25 feet of transmission structures\n- Pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy 48 hours before construction (OSHA requires 20' clearance from energized transmission lines)\n- Various other transmission facility requirements\n\nFrom Block 19 (Electric Notes) - General electric notes:\n- \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment.\"\n- \"Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained.\"\n\nCRITICAL FINDING: \n- Block 19, Note 3 mentions \"the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the **proposed overhead electric facilities** designed to provide electric service to this project.\"\n- Block 19, Note 4 explicitly states clearances must be maintained per NESC, OSHA, and local rules.\n\nHowever:\n1. **NO SPECIFIC 48-HOUR NOTIFICATION NOTE** has been found on the plans for work near high-voltage overhead lines (per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003). The block mentions a pre-construction safety meeting but not the 48-hour notification requirement specifically.\n\n2. The notes mention \"proposed overhead electric facilities\" - but Block 19 mentions tree pruning within 10 feet of these. This is interesting because it's about the NEW electric service lines to be installed, not the existing overhead distribution lines.\n\n3. The transmission notes (Block 13) do NOT include a 48-hour notification requirement either - they mention a pre-construction safety meeting.\n\n\nNow I need to assess what's actually documented versus what's missing. I've searched extensively and cannot locate building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor heights, profile sections showing vertical clearances to the structure, dimension annotations from outer conductors to building edges, registered surveyor clearance data, or section details for retaining walls that verify clearances from overhead lines. The wall details exist but don't address clearance verification from the transmission lines.\n\nThe landscape plan only shows generic \"M\" mitigation tree labels without species identification, and there are no vertical clearance markings for driveways or parking areas. The statutory 48-hour notification requirement from Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 isn't documented—only a transmission safety meeting is mentioned. Specific clearance analysis documentation is absent throughout the set.\n\nThis means several checklist items will not pass: EL-1.1 lacks both surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions; EL-1.2 has no documented 15-foot radial clearances; EL-1.3 provides no clearance documentation for building projections; and EL-1.7 is missing surveyed conductor elevations on the building elevation itself.\n\nSeveral items don't apply because they're not part of the proposal: gas pump canopies aren't included, stairs and elevated walkways aren't proposed, there's no substation on the property, no new fencing is being added adjacent to transmission lines despite easement restrictions being noted, transmission roads aren't present, and no highway or freeway is involved.\n\nFor verification, I need to confirm whether retaining walls fall under overhead lines, check if any driveways have vertical clearance issues with overhead infrastructure, investigate the tree species near the OHE line that's already visible, determine if down guy conflicts appear on the survey, and verify the notification requirements.\n\nI'm noticing an important distinction here—the overhead lines visible on Sheet 4 appear to be service drops serving the existing building that's being demolished, separate from the transmission lines referenced in the notes. Let me clarify what infrastructure is actually present on the property.\n\nThe existing overhead electric service lines currently feed the building scheduled for demolition, while the proposed work involves underground electric service to the eight new buildings shown on Sheet 21. The clearance standards apply to any overhead lines that will remain after demolition and those serving adjacent properties. Since I've identified overhead lines on Sheets 4, 9, and 31 along the site boundaries, this grouping is relevant to the project.\n\nThe main gaps I'm seeing are the absence of measured clearances between the overhead lines and proposed buildings, no building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor heights, missing profile views showing vertical clearances, and no 48-hour notification documentation.\n\nNow I need to work through the remaining items in my evaluation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2492,"cache_read_input_tokens":75104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2492},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c202df16-5633-43ec-a785-1c53dfb8863e","uuid":"34c89f1f-6511-40e6-b40d-e6e3c6cd882d"}
{"level":30,"time":1778274552775,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0182ZzX8KjfkaaZ1HTJLgNr7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research, I now have enough information to evaluate all checklist items. Let me document my key findings and then provide the structured assessment.\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY — Step 3 Complete\n\n**Applicability Confirmed:** The site has existing overhead electric lines shown on:\n- Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey): Overhead utility poles and service drop lines serving existing building\n- Sheet 9 (Site Plan): Overhead electric lines marked \"-OHE-\" along southern and eastern boundaries  \n- Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan): Overhead electric lines depicted with mitigation trees nearby\n- Sheets 3 (General Notes): Extensive transmission easement restrictions documented\n\n**Proposed Site Features Subject to Clearances:**\n- 8 new multi-family buildings (Buildings 1-8)\n- New driveways and parking areas\n- New sidewalks\n- Retaining walls (pond and perimeter)\n- Landscape plantings including trees\n- Underground electrical service lines\n\n**CRITICAL NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n1. Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations\n2. Vertical clearance profile sections from conductors to buildings\n3. Clearance dimension annotations from outside conductor to building faces/edges\n4. Registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey data\n5. Building projection clearance documentation (overhangs, roofs, balconies)\n6. Retaining wall section exhibits with overhead line clearances\n7. Landscape tree species identification for trees near overhead lines\n8. Driveway/parking vertical clearance dimensions\n9. 48-hour notification note to Austin Energy per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752.003\n10. Formal clearance verification analysis/exhibits\n\nNow I'll provide the complete findings assessment:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2492,"cache_read_input_tokens":75104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2492},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c202df16-5633-43ec-a785-1c53dfb8863e","uuid":"c8c36437-c742-4fa8-bf66-264b845ebca8"}
