{"level":30,"time":1778274739419,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QjEExTujmuA5DTZDdyameo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ayz1GkouQvxe22VR3EK8PW","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building locations near Valley View Road and southern boundary overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings and permanent structures are proposed near existing overhead electric lines shown on Sheets 4 and 9, but building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions from outer conductor to building faces are not provided. Horizontal sky-to-ground clearance compliance cannot be verified without elevation data and dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing overhead electric lines are shown on the site plan (Sheet 4 shows poles/conductors along Valley View Road and southern boundary; Sheet 9 shows OHE line labeled along southern boundary). Buildings 7 and 8 are proposed near the southern OHE line. However, no building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor locations or clearance dimension annotations are present in the submittal.","reasoning":"While the site plan shows the presence of overhead lines and building locations, UCM 1.10.3 requires surveyed elevations of conductors with labeled clearance dimensions to demonstrate compliance. Without elevation data, conductor positions, or dimension annotations showing the specific clearance from the outermost conductor to building faces, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Customer facilities and buildings near overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities shown on site plan but voltage classification not labeled (cannot determine if distribution <60kV or transmission ≥60kV). Site plan shows buildings and facilities but no 15-foot radial clearance dimensions labeled. Profile plans with radial clearance verification from outside conductor to facility locations not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and survey (Sheet 4) depict overhead electric lines near buildings, but no voltage information is labeled on any plan. No clearance dimensions annotating 15-foot radial distances from outer conductor to building locations are shown on site plan or utilities plan.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radial clearance applies only to distribution conductors (<60kV). The plans do not label the voltage class, making it impossible to confirm which clearance standard applies. Even if distribution is confirmed, the site plan does not show the 15-foot radial clearance dimensions required by UCM 1.10.3, preventing verification of compliance.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building projections near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations with projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks) and surveyed overhead conductor elevations not provided. Section views showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to building projections not included. Compliance with both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets or section views showing building projections and their relationship to overhead electric lines are included in the submittal. The site plan shows building footprints but not architectural projections.","reasoning":"Verification of clearances for building projections requires both elevation views of the projections and surveyed elevation data for the conductors, along with dimension annotations showing clearances. These are not present in the submittal.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan sheets (Sheet 9, Sheet 31) shows no gas pump canopies proposed anywhere on the development site.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies only when gas pump canopies are proposed. Since none are shown, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms are proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows walkways at grade level and no elevated structures beyond standard building construction with entries.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies only when elevated walkways or platforms are proposed. Standard building entries and roof structures are not within the scope of this deficiency.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near Valley View Road right-of-way"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are proposed adjacent to Valley View Road where overhead electric lines exist in the right-of-way. No clearance dimensions (7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial) are labeled on site plan or utility plan to demonstrate compliance with permanent clearance requirements per UCM 1.10.3.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings proximate to Valley View Road right-of-way, and the existing conditions survey shows overhead electric lines along this boundary. However, no clearance dimension annotations are present on the site plan showing distances from the outer conductor to the buildings.","reasoning":"Even if buildings appear to be at adequate distance, compliance must be documented with explicit clearance dimensions measured from the outer conductor, not from the property line or pole center. Without these dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building elevations showing proximity to overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimension annotations are not included in the submittal. Registered surveyor data showing pole and conductor locations required to verify vertical clearance requirements is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Submitted plans contain no building elevation sheets. The preliminary electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed underground facilities but not surveyed existing overhead line elevations.","reasoning":"UCM 1.10.3 requires surveyed elevations of overhead conductors on building elevation sheets with dimension annotations showing clearances. This documentation is essential for verifying compliance and is entirely absent from the submittal.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building locations near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits showing dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings and building projections are not provided. Clearance verification cannot be completed without these detailed section views with dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings near overhead lines (OHE labeled on southern boundary per vision check), but no detail sections or enlarged plan details are included showing clearance dimensions from the outer conductor to building edges.","reasoning":"Detailed section views with clearance dimension lines originating from the outer conductor are required to demonstrate compliance. The absence of these exhibits prevents verification.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Fences near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on the site plan near overhead electric lines, but no clearance dimensions annotating 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from outer conductor are labeled. Dimension annotations must originate from conductor position, not pole center or property line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows property-line fences, and overhead electric lines are present along the property boundaries (visible on Sheets 4 and 9). However, no clearance dimensions are annotated on the plan.","reasoning":"Even if visual inspection suggests adequate distance, compliance requires explicit clearance dimensions measured from the outer conductor. Without these dimensions, compliance cannot be verified per UCM 1.10.3.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence posts near electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on site plan near existing overhead electric poles (visible on Sheets 4 and 9 along Valley View Road and southern boundary). Specific dimensions showing 10-foot horizontal clearance from fence posts to pole centerlines are not annotated on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing electric poles are marked on the survey (Sheet 4) and fences are shown on the site plan (Sheet 9) near property boundaries where poles exist. No horizontal dimensions from fence posts to poles are labeled.","reasoning":"Compliance requires explicit horizontal dimension annotations from fence post locations to pole centerlines, showing the 10-foot minimum clearance. These are not present on the plans.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation is shown on or adjacent to the property. Fences connecting to or near substation fences are not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan sheets (4, 9, 31) and facts.md shows no mention of an Austin Energy substation on or immediately adjacent to the property. Substation facilities are not depicted on the survey or site plan.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies only when a substation fence exists adjacent to or connected with proposed fencing. Since no substation is present, this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Fencing near transmission facilities (if present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan indicates electric transmission structures exist (Sheet 3, Block 13 lists extensive transmission requirements), but overhead electric line voltage is not labeled on site plan. Cannot determine whether fencing beneath transmission lines is required without confirmation of transmission voltage (≥60kV). If transmission lines are present, fencing material specifications and grounding details are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 13 references 'electric transmission lines and structures' and includes 16 notes about transmission easements, suggesting transmission infrastructure exists on or near the property. However, no voltage labels are present on the actual utility plans (Sheets 4, 9, 21) to confirm 69kV, 138kV, or 345kV transmission.","reasoning":"The distinction between distribution (<60kV) and transmission (≥60kV) is critical. While transmission notes exist, the plans do not label the facilities as transmission with specific voltages. If transmission is confirmed, fence material specifications and grounding details would be required but are not provided.","tools_used":["Read","vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier fencing or posts beneath overhead electric lines are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows standard perimeter property line fencing but no vehicle barrier posts or protective fencing designed to prevent vehicle contact with overhead utilities.","reasoning":"Vehicle barrier fencing is a specific type of protective structure. Standard property-line fencing does not meet the definition of vehicle barrier fencing in this context, and no vehicle barriers are shown.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are shown on site plan (Sheets 38-39) and overhead electric lines exist on property (Sheets 4, 9). However, no clearance dimensions showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from outermost electric line to retaining wall faces are annotated on the site plan or wall sections. Measurement from conductor position (not pole) is not confirmed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows existing stone retaining wall on southern boundary where overhead electric line is present. Wall plan sheets (38-39) show wall details but no clearance dimension annotations from the overhead line to the wall face.","reasoning":"Compliance requires explicit clearance dimensions measured from the outer conductor to the wall face. Without these dimensions on the plan or section views, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No retaining walls are proposed adjacent to an Austin Energy substation. Substation property is not shown on site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No Austin Energy substation is identified on the property or in adjacent areas per site plan review and facts.md.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies only to retaining walls adjacent to substation walls. Without an adjacent substation, this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) are proposed on the site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows standard pedestrian walkways and no elevated emergency access bridges or platforms.","reasoning":"This deficiency applies only to emergency access structures. Standard building access is not within scope.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall section views (Sheets 38-39) do not include dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall face. Section exhibits showing clearance verification from conductor (not pole) are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Wall detail sheets 38-39 show cross-sections but no overlay or annotation showing the relationship to overhead electric conductors or clearance dimensions from conductors.","reasoning":"UCM 1.10.3 requires section views with dimensions originating from the outer conductor. The wall sections do not include this clearance verification.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways beneath overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":17}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways are proposed on site plan, and overhead electric lines exist along southern boundary (Sheets 4, 9). However, no clearance dimension annotations showing vertical clearance from lowest point of overhead electric facilities to driveway finished grades are labeled on grading plan or section views. Mid-span clearance verification and truck traffic determination not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan show driveway locations, and overhead electric line is present along southern boundary. However, no vertical clearance dimensions (requiring 16 feet for parking without trucks or 18 feet with truck traffic) are annotated on the grading plan or cross-sections.","reasoning":"Compliance requires: (1) determination of whether truck traffic is expected (establishing 16-foot vs. 18-foot minimum), and (2) verified mid-span clearance data. Neither is documented on the plans.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are proposed beneath overhead electric lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking within garages and surface parking areas not located beneath overhead electric lines (OHE is shown along southern boundary away from parking area).","reasoning":"No applicable vehicle display areas on concrete pads are shown beneath overhead lines, so this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Roads and driveways beneath transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 Block 13 indicates transmission facilities and structures are present on or near the property. However, transmission line voltage is not labeled on site or grading plans (cannot confirm 69kV, 138kV, or 345kV). If transmission lines exist, grading plan does not show vertical clearance dimensions verifying 30-foot minimum clearance from ground to transmission line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"General notes reference transmission structures and easements (Sheet 3 Block 13), but utility plans do not label transmission facility voltages. Grading plan shows driveway grades but no vertical clearance dimensions referenced to transmission facilities.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on confirmation of transmission voltage (≥60kV). While transmission references exist in notes, the actual facility classification is not labeled on the utility plans, making compliance verification impossible.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Highways/freeways with distribution underbuilt"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows local development on surface streets (Valley View Road classified as local street per facts.md, not highway/freeway). 40-foot vertical clearance requirement for distribution underbuilt on transmission structures does not apply to this project's street context.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md indicates Valley View Road is classified as a Local Street (ASMP Street Level 1), not a highway or freeway. Site development is a local townhome project, not a highway project.","reasoning":"This deficiency applies only to highways and freeways. The project involves local street frontage only, making this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways near existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing electric poles are shown on survey along Valley View Road. Site plan shows driveways and access, but no dimension annotations confirming whether driveways are in conflict with pole locations or whether poles are relocated minimum 30 feet from driveway edges. Relocation notes not provided if conflict exists.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey (Sheet 4) shows electric poles along Valley View Road with x-y coordinates. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows driveway layout. However, no explicit dimension annotations verify the distance relationship between pole locations and driveway edges.","reasoning":"Compliance requires either: (1) confirming driveways are not within 30 feet of existing poles, or (2) providing relocation notes for affected poles. Neither verification nor relocation documentation is present.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric facilities shown on site plans"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are shown on the site plan and existing conditions survey using schematic lines labeled 'O.H. ELECTRIC' or 'OHE', but clearance dimensions are completely absent from all sheets. The critical deficiency is not measurable clearance from the outer conductor—dimensions must originate from outer conductor location, not pole centerline.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead lines are depicted on Sheets 4 and 9 as schematic dashed lines labeled 'O.H. ELECTRIC LINE' or 'OHE' with pole symbols shown. The vision check confirmed no clearance dimension annotations are present anywhere on the site plan, grading plan, or section views.","reasoning":"UCM 1.10.3 explicitly requires dimensions measured from the 'outside conductor' to verify clearances. The complete absence of any clearance dimensions on the plans represents a fundamental documentation failure. Even if buildings appear adequately spaced visually, compliance cannot be demonstrated without explicit dimension annotations originating from outer conductor positions.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Streetlight pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan (Sheet 10 Fire Protection Plan) may show streetlight locations. Without explicit photometric plan or enlarged site plan showing streetlight pole locations overlaid on overhead electric line routing, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 is the Fire Protection Plan, which may include lighting. However, without visual confirmation that streetlight pole locations are not directly beneath overhead electric lines, compliance cannot be determined.","reasoning":"Verification requires comparison of streetlight pole positions to overhead line routing shown on the site plan. This analysis was not completed due to lack of dedicated photometric plan in the submittal.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks at property limits along right-of-way"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing power poles are shown on survey along Valley View Road right-of-way. Site plan shows sidewalk alignment at property limits. Specific dimension annotations confirming sidewalk clearances from existing power poles at each end of property are not provided on the plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Poles exist on survey (Sheet 4) along Valley View Road. Site plan shows sidewalk routing but no specific dimensions from pole locations to sidewalk alignment at property corners/ends.","reasoning":"Compliance requires either confirmed adequate clearance or relocation of poles. Without dimension annotations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Enclosed trash areas or trash receptacles are shown on site plan (Block 54 on Sheet 9 references trash collection notes), but they are not located beneath overhead electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows trash enclosures near buildings and parking areas, which are not positioned beneath the overhead electric lines shown along the southern boundary.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies only when trash areas are beneath overhead lines. Since trash facilities are not under the OHE, this does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Structures within electric easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows plat-dedicated electric easements (5' easements ×2 and 7.5' PUE per facts.md), but easement boundaries are not clearly depicted or dimension-verified on Sheet 9. Structures, features, or site improvements within easement boundaries lack dimension verification showing 7.5-foot clearance from outer conductor if items are proposed within easement areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md confirms two 5-foot electric easements and one 7.5-foot PUE are plat-dedicated on the property. Sheet 2 (Plat) should show easement boundaries, and Sheet 9 should relate proposed improvements to these boundaries. However, no specific notation was observed confirming whether structures fall within or outside the easement areas.","reasoning":"The prohibition on structures under/over distribution facilities is absolute per UCM 1.10.3, regardless of clearance. If any structures, parking, or pavement are within the electric easement boundaries, verification that they maintain 7.5-foot clearance from outer conductor is required. This verification is not evident from review of Sheets 2 and 9.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No water meters are shown on the utility plan at locations where overhead electric service drops exist.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows underground electric service, not overhead service drops. No overhead service drop conductors are labeled on utility plans.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies only when water meters are located near overhead service drops. If service is provided underground, overhead service-drop clearances do not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"New water lines are shown on the utility plan but are routed beneath underground facilities, not beneath overhead electric distribution facilities per Sheet 21.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows private water and sewer branches as underground utilities. No conflict with overhead electric lines is apparent from the plan layout.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies only to water lines near overhead distribution facilities. Underground water service does not trigger this requirement.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Permanent structure foundations near property line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are proposed on site, but specific dimension annotations showing setbacks from property lines where structures are located within 5 feet are not clearly labeled. Electric facilities exist in adjacent ROW (Valley View Road), but clearance space adequacy for electric facility access and maintenance cannot be verified without explicit dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building locations with setbacks from Valley View Road ROW. Electric poles exist along the ROW (Sheet 4). However, no specific dimensions annotate whether any building foundations fall within 5 feet of the property line or confirm adequate clearance for utility access.","reasoning":"Compliance requires confirming that permanent foundations do not encroach within 5 feet of the property line (or if they do, that adequate clearance space for utility facility access is maintained). Without explicit dimension annotations, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Site areas where proposed features may not meet minimum vertical clearances from overhead facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are shown on site plan (Sheet 9 labels 'OHE' along southern boundary) near proposed buildings and driveways. No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is provided showing pole locations with surveyed elevations of overhead conductors. Without surveyor data, vertical clearance from overhead lines to building features, roof projections, and driveway grades cannot be verified as meeting required minimums (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 16-18 feet for driveways).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines are depicted on site plan (Sheet 9 shows 'OHE' label along southern boundary). No registered surveyor report or mid-span clearance data is included showing: (1) surveyed pole locations, (2) surveyed conductor elevations at mid-span and near poles, or (3) clearance dimensions from conductors to proposed site features. Vision check confirmed no clearance dimensions appear anywhere on the site plan or section views.","reasoning":"UCM 1.10.3 explicitly requires surveyor data for pole and conductor locations when vertical clearances may be marginal. The complete absence of surveyor mid-span clearance data is a critical documentation deficiency preventing verification of vertical clearance compliance.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new overhead electric lines are being installed as part of this project. Sheet 21 shows proposed underground electric service only.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 Preliminary Electrical Design Plan depicts proposed underground electric lines, transformers, and pull boxes. No new overhead line construction is shown.","reasoning":"This deficiency applies only to new overhead lines being installed. Since the project proposes underground service, the line-crossing requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new overhead electric lines of any type are being installed. Only underground electric lines are proposed per Sheet 21.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) shows only underground electric facilities.","reasoning":"Secondary/primary line crossing deficiency applies only to new overhead lines. This project proposes only underground service.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows no signage structures or marquee installations.","reasoning":"Marquee sign clearance requirements apply only when marquee signs are proposed. None are shown.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed. Sheet 21 shows underground electric service design only.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan does not show new pole installations. Existing poles are to remain or be relocated, but no specifications for new underground service conversion poles are present.","reasoning":"This deficiency applies only to new poles proposed for service conversion. The project does not include new pole installations for this purpose.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No decorative lighting fixtures are proposed beneath or near existing overhead electric lines per landscape and photometric plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows general landscaping. Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) may show functional lighting. No decorative lighting fixtures are indicated beneath the overhead electric line along the southern boundary.","reasoning":"Decorative lighting under overhead lines would require clearance verification. Since no such fixtures are shown in conflict, this does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near overhead electric facilities, particularly southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed on landscape plan (Sheet 31) in areas with overhead electric lines. Plant schedule lists Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, and Texas Mountain Laurel, but compliance with ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible (marked 'UC') species list is not documented. Vision check measured tree distances from OHE line but species verification against utility-compatible list not confirmed. Grading near transmission structures not verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed trees, and overhead electric line is marked 'OHE' on the drawing. Vision measurement showed trees at various distances from the line (85-148 feet for most trees, well above the 10-foot distribution or 50-foot transmission thresholds). Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists species but does not indicate whether they are marked 'UC' (utility compatible) in ECM Appendix F.","reasoning":"Compliance requires: (1) tree species verification against ECM Appendix F utility-compatible list, and (2) confirmation of lateral distances. While measured distances appear adequate, species documentation is missing. Without explicit notation that species meet the 'UC' designation or mature height ≤20 feet requirement, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows meter locations, but enlarged plan details with specific obstruction analysis (fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, building projections) conflicting with meter access are not provided. Working clearance verification (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) is not documented on the plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows meter locations on the general site plan but no enlarged detail views showing potential obstructions or working clearance space around meters.","reasoning":"Compliance requires verification that meters have adequate working space. Without enlarged detail views annotating working clearances and obstruction analysis, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No existing streetlight poles are identified in the project vicinity on the site plan or survey.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey (Sheet 4) and site plan (Sheet 9) do not indicate existing streetlight poles on or immediately adjacent to the property.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies only when existing streetlights are present. Without identified streetlight poles, clearance requirements do not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Accessible paths and driveways near electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing electric poles are shown on survey (Sheet 4) along Valley View Road and southern boundary. Down guy wires (support cables from distribution poles to ground anchors) may exist but are not explicitly labeled or shown on the site plan. Accessible path and driveway alignments shown on site plan but potential guy wire conflicts are not verified or resolved with notation regarding relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles marked with symbols but down guy wires (guy anchors) are not explicitly labeled in the legend or called out on the drawing. Site plan shows accessible routes and driveways, but no dimension verification confirms clearance from guy wire locations.","reasoning":"Down guy wires are frequently omitted from site plans despite existing in the field. Without explicit labeling or dimension verification that accessible routes and driveways do not conflict with guy wires, compliance cannot be confirmed. If conflicts exist, relocation notes are required.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No angled guy anchors from transmission structures are shown on site plan. Easement exhibit on Sheet 2 does not indicate transmission guy easements requiring the 10-foot either-side and 50-foot extension dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat (Sheet 2) shows easement dedications but no transmission guy easement boundaries are depicted. General notes (Sheet 3 Block 13) reference transmission structures but not angled guy arrangements requiring dedicated easements.","reasoning":"This deficiency applies only when transmission guy anchors with dedicated easements are required. Since none are shown, this does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations from distribution poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing distribution poles are shown on survey (Sheet 4) along Valley View Road with guy wires labeled 'O.H. GUY WIRE', indicating down guys exist. However, down guy anchor locations and dedicated easement boundaries are not clearly depicted on Plat (Sheet 2) or site plan (Sheet 9). Easement requirements showing 10-foot width and 5-foot extension beyond anchor ground entry point are not verified on easement exhibit.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey (Sheet 4) labels 'O.H. GUY WIRE' near poles, confirming down guys exist. However, the plat (Sheet 2) and easement exhibit do not show detailed down guy anchor easement boundaries with specific dimensions.","reasoning":"Down guy easements require specific dimensional boundaries (10-foot wide, extending 5 feet past where the guy enters the ground). Without detailed easement boundaries showing these dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers are shown directly exposed beneath overhead electric lines in the submittal. Sheet 21 shows proposed transformers on pads but they are located at ground level in service areas, not beneath overhead conductors above the transformer.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations on the site plan. No overhead electric lines are shown routing directly above these pad-mounted transformers.","reasoning":"The deficiency applies when overhead lines pass above transformer equipment. Since transformers are not positioned under overhead conductors, this does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service configurations with transformers or switchgears covered by structures or canopies are proposed. Transformers shown on Sheet 21 are pad-mounted in open locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows pad-mounted transformers in open-air locations, not in niche (covered/recessed) configurations.","reasoning":"Niche configuration requirements apply only to covered or recessed transformer/switchgear installations. This project does not propose such configurations.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas and equipment operation zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":6}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows erosion control plan (Sheet 5) with construction phasing, but construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, and work platform locations are not detailed with 10-foot radial clearance verification from energized overhead lines. Construction logistics and crane swing radius not explicitly dimensioned relative to overhead electric facilities per OSHA requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Erosion control sheets show general construction areas but do not detail staging zone boundaries with specific 10-foot radial clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"OSHA regulations and Texas law require 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines during construction. This requirement must be documented on construction logistics plans with explicit dimension annotations. Without such documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet and general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on the site adjacent to Valley View Road and along the southern boundary (Sheets 4, 9). Sheet 3 Block 13 includes transmission-specific notes requiring a '48-hour pre-construction safety meeting' with Austin Energy, but no general note is present stating that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead distribution lines as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. The transmission safety meeting note does not constitute the required general notification requirement for all overhead lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 13 includes a 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting requirement specific to transmission structures. However, a separate, general 48-hour notification requirement for work near overhead distribution lines (required by Texas Health & Safety Code 752.003) is not present anywhere on the cover sheet or general notes sheets.","reasoning":"Texas Health & Safety Code § 752.003 requires property owners/contractors to notify utilities 48 hours before work near high-voltage lines. UCM 1.10.2 incorporates this requirement. While Block 13 addresses transmission safety, it does not address the general distribution-line notification requirement. This is a separate, mandatory note that must be included on plans whenever overhead lines are present.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No service-mast through-roof installations are shown on building elevations. Underground service is proposed per Sheet 21.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) indicates underground electric service. No building elevation sheets showing roof-penetrating service masts are provided.","reasoning":"Service-mast clearance requirements apply only to through-roof installations. Since underground service is proposed, this does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2480,"cache_read_input_tokens":67008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2480},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad5307f2-d9b7-488b-8d54-395eaf0212d6","uuid":"77c9f066-7fe2-4831-a2c5-9fb48efcbb8c"}
