dard circle with an 'X', a 'UP' label, or any specific symbol defined in the Key Notes/legend) depicted along this \"- OHE -\" line or elsewhere on this specific plan sheet.\n3.  **Trees:** Because specific individual pole locations are not explicitly marked, it is not possible to determine if trees are within exactly 10 feet of a *pole*. However, it is important to note that there are several trees, specifically those marked with an **\"M\"** (which the Key Notes define as \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"), located directly adjacent to the overhead line. The center trunk symbols (indicated by a '+') of at least two \"M\" trees on the bottom right are depicted virtually on top of or immediately next to the \"- OHE -\" line, with their drawn canopies overlapping the line."}]}
