{"level":30,"time":1778275165092,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0114Dcpu4DMzudA9wzhRjm37","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is critical! The overhead electric lines are NOT identified with voltage levels or classification (distribution vs transmission). This means:\n\n1. I cannot definitively determine if they are distribution (<60kV) or transmission (≥60kV)\n2. Without voltage classification, I cannot apply the correct clearance rules\n3. The default assumption per the grouping guidance would be \"typical overhead lines are distribution\" but this should be verified\n\nHowever, the grouping guidance states: \"Most overhead facilities on typical development sites are distribution unless explicitly labeled as transmission or located within transmission easements.\"\n\nFacts.md also confirms: \"No transmission easement\" on site (checked easements, only found 5' electric easements which are distribution).\n\nSo the reasonable assumption is that the OHE lines shown are DISTRIBUTION lines, not transmission.\n\nNow, let me also check if there's any reference in the supplementary documents (like the application or engineer's letter) that might clarify the voltage level or utility information.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":785,"cache_read_input_tokens":57728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":785},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da8d4f94-c433-44b6-bc3f-ac89c89d21c6","uuid":"53c82f9a-0817-4867-a119-3c613fa6c902"}
