{"level":30,"time":1778275579069,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EqC8gMvpSVcihMuzpxvUYX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided electrical and site plan:\n\n**Are easement boundaries shown?**\nYes, easement boundaries are clearly shown and labeled throughout the plan. Examples include:\n*   \"Wastewater Easement\" (northwest area)\n*   \"5' P.U.E.\" (Public Utility Easement, along the northern boundary)\n*   \"25' Drainage Easement\" (along the eastern boundary)\n*   \"15' Water & Wastewater Easement\" (along the eastern boundary)\n*   \"15' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" (along the southern boundary)\n*   \"Sidewalk Easement\" (multiple locations on the western side)\n\n**Do any transformer pads appear to fall within drainage easements, water easements, sewer easements, or electrical easements marked on the plan?**\nNo. Based on the labels and boundary lines drawn on the plan, the structures explicitly labeled as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** do not appear to fall within the marked drainage, water, sewer (wastewater), or electrical easements. \n\nThere are four labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations on the plan:\n1.  West of Building 2 (near Unit 201)\n2.  West of Building 8 (near Unit 801)\n3.  East of Building 4 (near Unit 404)\n4.  East of Building 7 (near Unit 703/704)\n\nThe pads on the western side (near Buildings 2 and 8) are located adjacent to or slightly overlapping areas marked as a \"Sidewalk Easement,\" but they are well outside the \"Wastewater Easement,\" \"15' Elec. & Tele. Easement,\" and other utility easements on the perimeter. The pads centrally located between the buildings (east of Buildings 4 and 7) do not intersect any drawn easement boundaries."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b2369d5-d10d-43cc-a9bd-10ac3946c3f9","uuid":"ef672865-a3d2-4a8f-be2b-19b3bfcffbef","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided electrical and site plan:\n\n**Are easement boundaries shown?**\nYes, easement boundaries are clearly shown and labeled throughout the plan. Examples include:\n*   \"Wastewater Easement\" (northwest area)\n*   \"5' P.U.E.\" (Public Utility Easement, along the northern boundary)\n*   \"25' Drainage Easement\" (along the eastern boundary)\n*   \"15' Water & Wastewater Easement\" (along the eastern boundary)\n*   \"15' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" (along the southern boundary)\n*   \"Sidewalk Easement\" (multiple locations on the western side)\n\n**Do any transformer pads appear to fall within drainage easements, water easements, sewer easements, or electrical easements marked on the plan?**\nNo. Based on the labels and boundary lines drawn on the plan, the structures explicitly labeled as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** do not appear to fall within the marked drainage, water, sewer (wastewater), or electrical easements. \n\nThere are four labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations on the plan:\n1.  West of Building 2 (near Unit 201)\n2.  West of Building 8 (near Unit 801)\n3.  East of Building 4 (near Unit 404)\n4.  East of Building 7 (near Unit 703/704)\n\nThe pads on the western side (near Buildings 2 and 8) are located adjacent to or slightly overlapping areas marked as a \"Sidewalk Easement,\" but they are well outside the \"Wastewater Easement,\" \"15' Elec. & Tele. Easement,\" and other utility easements on the perimeter. The pads centrally located between the buildings (east of Buildings 4 and 7) do not intersect any drawn easement boundaries."}]}
