{"level":30,"time":1778275938523,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01XLiCz5r6KSRin4bGwovmmQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete\n\nI have completed a comprehensive site plan review for **Grouping 1: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Summary of Findings:\n\n**Total Checklist Items Evaluated:** 47\n\n**Deficiency Status Breakdown:**\n- **FAIL** (requirement not met): 14 items\n- **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (cannot determine from available documents): 15 items  \n- **PASS** (evidence supports compliance): 3 items\n- **N/A** (not applicable to project): 15 items\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**Critical Gaps Identified:**\n1. **No clearance dimensions shown** - Despite overhead electric (OHE) lines being clearly depicted on site plans routing along western and southern property boundaries, no clearance dimensions are provided from conductors to any site features (buildings, fences, retaining walls, driveways, parking areas)\n\n2. **Missing surveyed conductor data** - No registered surveyor field survey showing pole locations, conductor elevations, or mid-span clearances is provided\n\n3. **Trees non-compliant** - Multiple landscape trees are positioned within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (some as close as 1.6-3 feet), but tree species are not identified or verified to be utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F\n\n4. **Vertical clearances undocumented** - No vertical clearance dimensions shown where driveways on the western boundary cross utility pole alignments (16-foot or 18-foot minimum required)\n\n5. **Transformer clearances not verified** - Transformers shown on electrical plan lack section views demonstrating 7.5-foot vertical clearance from overhead lines\n\n6. **48-hour notification note missing** - Despite transmission line references and Austin Energy requirements in general notes, the mandatory 48-hour notification requirement per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752 is not included\n\n7. **Construction staging not documented** - No construction logistics plan shows required 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines for staging areas and equipment operation zones\n\n**Applicable Infrastructure Confirmed:**\n- Overhead electric (OHE) distribution lines shown on site\n- Transmission line facilities referenced in General Notes (Sheet 3)\n- Electric easements (5-foot electric, 7.5-foot PUE) documented on property\n- Buildings, parking, driveways, retaining walls, sidewalks, and landscaping all proposed near OHE facilities\n\nThe structured output has been returned with complete details on each finding, including code citations, applicable areas, sheet references, and agent reasoning traces."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15458,"cache_read_input_tokens":74472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15458},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d95a2e27-fdb9-4bac-a4d1-7990111a8624","uuid":"669a609f-1414-4b62-a443-ceda1b0b23b4"}
{"level":30,"time":1778275938524,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":2569552,"duration_api_ms":238741,"num_turns":30,"result":"## Review Complete\n\nI have completed a comprehensive site plan review for **Grouping 1: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Summary of Findings:\n\n**Total Checklist Items Evaluated:** 47\n\n**Deficiency Status Breakdown:**\n- **FAIL** (requirement not met): 14 items\n- **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (cannot determine from available documents): 15 items  \n- **PASS** (evidence supports compliance): 3 items\n- **N/A** (not applicable to project): 15 items\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**Critical Gaps Identified:**\n1. **No clearance dimensions shown** - Despite overhead electric (OHE) lines being clearly depicted on site plans routing along western and southern property boundaries, no clearance dimensions are provided from conductors to any site features (buildings, fences, retaining walls, driveways, parking areas)\n\n2. **Missing surveyed conductor data** - No registered surveyor field survey showing pole locations, conductor elevations, or mid-span clearances is provided\n\n3. **Trees non-compliant** - Multiple landscape trees are positioned within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (some as close as 1.6-3 feet), but tree species are not identified or verified to be utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F\n\n4. **Vertical clearances undocumented** - No vertical clearance dimensions shown where driveways on the western boundary cross utility pole alignments (16-foot or 18-foot minimum required)\n\n5. **Transformer clearances not verified** - Transformers shown on electrical plan lack section views demonstrating 7.5-foot vertical clearance from overhead lines\n\n6. **48-hour notification note missing** - Despite transmission line references and Austin E