78950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are shown routing along western and southern property boundaries adjacent to proposed buildings. However, no clearance dimensions are provided to demonstrate that buildings maintain the required minimum 7 feet 6 inches horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor. Section and elevation exhibits with clearance dimensions from outside conductor to building faces must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of site plans (Sheets 9, 31) confirmed overhead electric (OHE) lines are depicted with dashed lines labeled '-- OHE --' running parallel to western and southern property boundaries. No dimension callouts, clearance annotations, or distance measurements from the OHE line to any building edge are shown on any plan sheet.","reasoning":"The deficiency requires evidence that buildings maintain the 7.5-foot clearance; absent explicit clearance dimensions or calculated clearances from plan geometry, the requirement cannot be verified as met. Burden of proof is on applicant to demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["western and southern property boundaries near all buildings and parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities are shown on site. However, no distinction is made between distribution primary/neutral conductors (requiring 15-foot radial clearance) and secondary conductors. Without conductor voltage labeling and clearance dimensions, compliance with the 15-foot radial clearance requirement for distribution facilities cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"OHE lines are shown on plans with label '-- OHE --' but no voltage designation (distribution vs. transmission) or conductor type labeling is visible. No radial clearance dimensions (in any direction from conductor) are shown on the plans.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radial clearance is specific to distribution primary and neutral conductors. Without conductor voltage identification on plans and without clearance dimensions shown, the applicability and compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all proposed buildings adjacent to OHE on western and southern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed buildings are shown near overhead electric lines. However, no building elevation sheets or detail sections are provided showing overhangs, awnings, balconies, or other projections and their clearances (both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial) from outside conductors. Building elevation drawings with clearance dimensions are required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building footprints near OHE, but no building elevation sheets with horizontal overhangs or vertical projections are visible in the provided sheet index. No section views showing clearances from conductors to building edges or projections are shown.","reasoning":"Building projections are a specific element required to maintain clearances. Without elevation or section views showing the location of projections and dimensions to conductors, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Gas pump canopies are not proposed on this site plan. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of si