electric facilities exist in adjacent ROW, buildings must maintain documented permanent clearances. Absence of clearance dimensions means compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all proposed buildings within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities on western and southern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities are shown on site plan. However, no building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and mid-span clearance data from registered surveyor are provided. Registered surveyor field survey of pole locations, conductor elevations, and measured mid-span clearances must be provided on building elevation drawings.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and site plan (Sheet 9) show OHE routing but contain no surveyed elevation data, pole locations with coordinates, or conductor heights. No reference to survey data or surveyor credentials is provided.","reasoning":"Code requires surveyed elevation data to verify clearances. None is shown on any submitted sheet.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all proposed buildings and structures within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No section or plan view exhibits with dimension lines extending from the outside electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings and building features are shown on any submitted plan. Detailed section exhibits with clearance dimensions from outer conductor to all building edges, overhangs, and projections must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of site plan (Sheet 9) found no dimension callouts showing clearance distances from overhead electric lines to buildings. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) also lacks clearance dimensions. No detail sections provided on subsequent sheets.","reasoning":"Clearance dimensions must be shown graphically from conductor to building edges. Total absence of such dimensions indicates non-compliance with documentation requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["wooden privacy fences shown on site plan near overhead electric facilities on western and southern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences (shown as H.6 symbol on landscape plan) are proposed near overhead electric facilities. However, no clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to the fence structure are shown. Dimension callouts must demonstrate minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from conductor to fence face.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows fence symbols (H.6 pattern) along property boundaries where OHE is routed, but no clearance dimensions between fence and OHE conductor are provided.","reasoning":"Without dimension callouts, compliance with clearance requirement cannot be verified from plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["wooden privacy fences shown on site plan where electric utility poles exist along property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on site plan and utility poles are depicted along western and southern property boundaries. However, no specific dimension annotations showing the minimum 10-foot clearance from fence post locations to pole locations are provided. Fence post locations must be dimensioned to verify the 10-foot clearance from poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks of site plans (Sheets 9, 31) show OHE poles are depicted along property boundaries and fences are shown, but no dimension lines between fence post locations and pole locations are visible.","reasoning":"Without specific dimension callouts to fence posts, horizontal separation cannot be verified from plan scale alone.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation is shown on or adjacent to the site. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan, facts.md, and easement documentation shows electric easements but no mention of a substation facility on the property or on immediately adjacent properties.","reasoning":"Applicability requires an existing substation adjacent to site. None is shown or documented.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["areas near transmission line facilities if fencing is proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan notes reference transmission structures and facilities. However, no detail sheets showing fence material specifications (non-conductive material requirement) or grounding details are provided for fencing near transmission lines. If fencing is proposed in transmission easement or beneath transmission lines, fence material specifications (non-conductive) and proper grounding detail drawings must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"General Notes (Sheet 3, Block 13) explicitly reference transmission lines and facilities with multiple clearance requirements. Landscape plan shows fencing on site perimeter where OHE is routed (potentially transmission). No fence material specification or grounding detail sheets are provided.","reasoning":"Transmission line proximity may require non-conductive fencing with grounding. Without material specs and grounding details, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier posts or fencing specifically designed as vehicle barriers beneath overhead electric lines are proposed on this site. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows standard fencing and retaining walls but no explicit vehicle barrier posts or anti-ram barriers beneath overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"Item is conditional on vehicle barrier fencing being proposed. None is shown.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["retaining walls shown on site plan perimeter near overhead electric facilities on western and southern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are proposed on site perimeter (Sheet 38-39) in locations where overhead electric facilities are present along property boundaries. However, no clearance dimensions from the outside electric conductor to the outermost face of the retaining wall are shown. Dimension callouts demonstrating minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from conductor to wall face must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Wall plan (Sheets 38-39) shows retaining wall details and plan locations. Site plan (Sheet 9) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) show walls aligned with perimeter where OHE exists. No dimension callouts from OHE conductor to wall faces are visible.","reasoning":"Retaining walls are permanent structures requiring clearance documentation. Absence of clearance dimensions indicates non-compliance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation exists on or is adjacent to the site. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review and facts.md confirm no substation facility is shown or referenced.","reasoning":"Applicability gate requires substation adjacency. Not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms for emergency access) are proposed on this site. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows standard residential townhome development with surface parking and driveways. No elevated emergency access structures are indicated.","reasoning":"Item applies only to specific emergency access structures. None proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["retaining walls on western and southern property boundaries where overhead electric facilities exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are proposed on site perimeter within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities. However, no section view exhibits with dimension lines from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of the retaining wall are provided. Detailed section views showing clearance dimensions from conductor to wall face must be included.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Wall plan (Sheets 38-39) provides structural sections and details of wall construction, footings, and reinforcement, but no clearance dimensions from OHE conductors are shown on any section.","reasoning":"Code requires section view clearance exhibits. None provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["western property boundary where proposed driveways cross utility pole alignments"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed driveways on the western boundary are shown crossing or passing adjacent to overhead electric utility pole alignments. However, no vertical clearance dimensions are shown to demonstrate the minimum 16-foot clearance (for parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot clearance (for roads with truck traffic) from the lowest point of overhead electric facilities. Vertical profile sections with clearance dimensions from overhead conductors/lines to the finished driveway surface must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Grading Plan (Sheet 11) identified two driveway entrances on western boundary crossing utility pole alignments but found no vertical clearance dimension callouts anywhere on the plan where driveways approach the utility alignments.","reasoning":"Vertical clearance verification is required when driveways pass under or adjacent to overhead lines. Absence of clearance dimensions indicates non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["parking areas on site plan if located beneath overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Parking areas are shown on the site plan. If any parking is located beneath overhead electric facilities, vertical clearance dimensions must be provided demonstrating the required minimums (12 feet for residential pedestrian areas, 16 feet for parking without trucks, 18 feet with truck traffic). Based on the site plan, parking areas appear to be primarily internal and not directly beneath the perimeter OHE routing, but clearance verification must be documented if any parking is in question.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking areas are primarily in interior of site away from perimeter OHE. However, no explicit vertical clearance annotations are shown for any parking area relative to overhead lines.","reasoning":"Without clearance dimensions shown and uncertain parking-to-OHE relationship, compliance cannot be fully verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["if final road/driveway grades are positioned beneath transmission line facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"General notes reference transmission structures and facilities on site. If roads or driveways will be located beneath transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV), grading plans must show final grade elevations with vertical clearance dimensions demonstrating the minimum 30-foot clearance from ground surface to electric transmission lines. No such profile sections are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 13 explicitly references transmission lines, structures, and clearance requirements. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows driveway and road elevations but no clearance dimensions relative to transmission line height/clearance zones.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on whether driveways are beneath transmission (unknown from plans). Compliance documentation is not provided regardless.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This is a townhome/residential development project, not a highway or freeway. The requirement for 40-foot vertical clearance does not apply. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Project is Valley View Townhomes (39 residential condo units). No highway or freeway grading is proposed.","reasoning":"Applicability is specific to highway/freeway projects. Not applicable here.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["western property boundary if existing electric poles are in conflict with proposed driveway locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric poles are shown on the site plan along the property boundaries. If any proposed driveways conflict with or pass within 30 feet of existing electric pole locations, the pole relocation or the driveway alignment change must be documented. No pole relocation notes or driveway adjustment details are provided on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check identified driveway entrances on western boundary crossing utility pole alignments. However, no note or detail indicates whether poles will be relocated, moved, or whether driveway alignment will adjust.","reasoning":"If conflict exists, resolution is not documented. Compliance status unclear from submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all locations where overhead electric facilities are shown on site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on the site plans. However, the code requirement states that where clearance dimensions ARE shown, they must be measured from the outside conductor (not from pole centerline or pole structure). Since no clearance dimensions are shown at all, this deficiency cannot be evaluated, but this also indicates that required clearance documentation is missing. All clearance dimensions must originate from the outside conductor location, not from pole center.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of all sheet blocks found zero clearance dimension callouts or annotations on any plan sheet. Vision checks confirmed absence of dimension lines showing clearances from conductors to any structures.","reasoning":"Code requires clearance dimensions be measured from conductor. Complete absence of clearance dimensions indicates this specific measurement methodology cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["site perimeter and parking areas if streetlight poles are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) and site plan were reviewed to locate streetlight pole positions. The Fire Protection Plan did not show overhead electric lines or streetlight poles. If new streetlight poles are proposed elsewhere on the site, their locations relative to overhead electric lines must be documented to verify they are not positioned directly beneath OHE conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) found no streetlight pole symbols or overhead electric line routing shown. Site plan (Sheet 9) was not specific about streetlight locations.","reasoning":"Streetlight locations cannot be specifically verified without clear identification on a lighting or fire protection plan. Applicability unclear.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["western and southern property boundaries where sidewalks meet property lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are shown on site plan along property boundaries where overhead electric poles exist. The sidewalk routing does not appear to conflict with or be directly aligned with pole locations at the property line intersections. The sidewalk appears to be cleared from the pole locations at both ends of the property along the ROW frontage.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of site plans (Sheets 9, 31) shows sidewalks routed along property boundaries in proximity to OHE poles, but visual inspection indicates sidewalk paths do not intersect or directly coincide with pole locations at property line transitions.","reasoning":"While not explicitly dimensioned, spatial relationship from plan view suggests sidewalks are adequately separated from pole locations. Geometry supports compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["trash enclosure/receptacle locations if located beneath overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan notes mention trash containers and collection requirements. However, specific trash enclosure or receptacle locations are not clearly identified on the site plan in relation to the overhead electric facilities. If trash enclosures are proposed beneath OHE, clearance verification showing minimum 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from conductor to the top of raised/serviced trash bins must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9, Block 7) references trash collection notes requiring that 'trash containers shall not be left at curbside unattended,' but no detailed trash enclosure location plan is provided showing proximity to OHE.","reasoning":"Trash enclosure locations relative to OHE are not specifically documented. Clearance verification cannot be completed without locating these features on plans relative to conductors.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all site features shown within overhead distribution electric easement boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution electric facilities are shown on site plans. Site features including buildings, parking, driveways, sidewalks, fences, and retaining walls are proposed in proximity to or within electric easement boundaries. The code prohibits placing customer facilities under or over Austin Energy distribution facilities, separate from the clearance distance requirement. Verification must be provided that all proposed features maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor and do not create violations of NESC code. No such verification exhibits are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows OHE routing along property boundaries with 5' electric easements marked. Multiple site features (buildings, walls, parking, sidewalks) are shown near these easement boundaries. No clearance dimensions or exhibits demonstrate compliance with the prohibition on structures under/over distribution facilities and the 7.5-foot clearance minimum.","reasoning":"Two separate requirements: (1) absolute prohibition on structures under/over distribution lines, and (2) 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor. Neither is documented as met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["water meter locations if adjacent to overhead electric service drops"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and utility tap plan (Sheet 19) were reviewed for water meter locations. Meters may be shown but their clearances from existing overhead electric service drops are not documented. If water meters are proposed, clearance dimensions demonstrating minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor of service drops must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plans reviewed but water meter locations relative to proposed overhead electric service drops are not specifically dimensioned for clearance verification.","reasoning":"Without specific dimension callouts from service drop conductors to meter locations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["water utility lines routed on site plan near overhead electrical distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on utility plan (Sheet 19). However, clearance dimensions from water line routing to overhead electrical distribution poles and conductors are not shown. Clearance verification dimensions must demonstrate that water lines maintain adequate clearance from OHE facilities during normal operation and maintenance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility tap plan (Sheet 19) shows water line routing but does not provide clearance dimensions to OHE conductors or poles.","reasoning":"Without clearance dimension callouts, compliance cannot be determined from plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["building foundations shown on site plan within 5 feet of property line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are proposed on site. However, no specific foundation location data is provided to verify that permanent structure foundations within 5 feet of property line allow necessary clearance space for existing or planned electric facilities in adjacent ROW or properties. Foundation setback verification from property lines and coordination with electric facility clearance requirements must be demonstrated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building layouts but does not provide specific foundation setback dimensions from property lines or clearance space analysis for electric facilities in adjacent ROW.","reasoning":"Without specific setback dimensions and clearance coordination documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["western and southern property boundaries where overhead electric facilities may not meet vertical clearance requirements relative to proposed buildings and driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities are shown on site in proximity to proposed buildings and driveways. Vertical clearances between overhead conductors and site features appear marginal or cannot be determined from available plan data. A registered surveyor must provide pole locations, conductor elevations, and mid-span clearance measurements to verify that minimum vertical clearances (7.5-foot sky-to-ground for general, 16-18 feet for driveways/parking) are maintained. No surveyor field data is provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan show OHE routing and proposed features but contain no surveyed elevation data, pole heights, or conductor height information. Without surveyor data, vertical clearances cannot be calculated or verified.","reasoning":"When clearances are marginal or cannot be determined, surveyor field data is mandatory. Absence of this data indicates non-compliance with documentation requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["overhead electric line routing relative to roadways if lines cross roads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines on the site plan are routed parallel to property boundaries (western and southern). They do not cross perpendicular to roadways or driveways in an angular orientation. The OHE routing shown is substantially parallel to the site perimeter, which satisfies the conventional practice of crossing roads at 90-degree angles (by not crossing at angles).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of site plans confirmed OHE routing along property perimeter boundaries parallel to Valley View Road and southern property line. No diagonal or angled crossings of road alignments visible.","reasoning":"OHE does not cross roads at non-90-degree angles. Geometry supports compliance with the convention.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Only overhead electric distribution lines are shown on the site plan. No secondary and primary line crossing condition is evident. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and utility plans shows only OHE referenced, with no indication of multiple overhead line types crossing.","reasoning":"Applicability requires both secondary and primary overhead lines to be shown crossing. Only single overhead line routing is shown.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on this site plan. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows townhome buildings with no mention of marquee signs or large commercial signage.","reasoning":"Applicability requires marquee signs. Not proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground service with transformers and pull boxes. No new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed. The existing overhead lines will remain, and service to buildings will be underground. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) explicitly shows underground electric lines to buildings, transformers (pad-mounted), and pull boxes. No mention of new poles for service conversion.","reasoning":"Applicability requires new poles to be proposed for underground conversion. Service is already proposed underground.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["decorative lighting fixtures if proposed under overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) and site plan (Sheet 9) reference lighting fixtures and exterior lighting requirements (full cut-off, fully shielded per Subchapter E). However, specific decorative lighting fixture locations relative to overhead electric lines and clearance verification exhibits are not provided. If decorative lighting is proposed under OHE, clearance dimensions must demonstrate 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9, Block 1) specifies all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded, but specific fixture locations on lighting or landscape plans relative to OHE are not clearly identified with clearance callouts.","reasoning":"Without specific location identification and clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscape areas along western and southern property boundaries where trees are proposed within 10 feet (distribution) or 50 feet (transmission) of overhead electric conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows tree plantings near overhead electric lines. Distance measurements from landscape plan indicate multiple trees are positioned within 10 lateral feet of OHE (distribution) or 50 lateral feet (transmission): trees measured at 1.6 feet, 2.6 feet, 3 feet, 9.1 feet, 13.9 feet, 19.6 feet, 21.4 feet, and 27.4 feet from OHE conductors. However, tree species are not identified on the plans, and there is no verification that trees within these clearance zones are from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, marked 'UC', generally with mature height ≤20 feet). All trees within 10 feet of distribution or 50 feet of transmission conductors must be confirmed as utility-compatible species.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement analysis of landscape plan (Sheet 31) calculated 9 tree-to-conductor distance measurements, with multiple trees (at 1.6, 2.6, 3, 9.1 feet) clearly within the 10-foot distribution threshold. Trees are labeled with designations 'SY', 'M', 'P', 'PL' but no species names or ECM Appendix F utility-compatible references are shown.","reasoning":"Deficiency explicitly requires verification that trees within clearance zones are utility-compatible. Absence of species identification and 'UC' confirmation indicates trees cannot be verified as meeting requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["electrical meter locations shown on site plans"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer locations and pull boxes. However, individual electric meter locations for each unit are not clearly identified on the site plan with reference to obstructions. Meter locations must be verified to be unobstructed by buildings, fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, or other features that would prevent access, installation, or required working clearances (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan shows general electrical routing and transformers but does not provide detailed meter location plans showing each unit meter location relative to buildings, fences, and landscape features.","reasoning":"Without detailed meter location exhibits, obstruction verification cannot be completed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["buildings and structures proposed adjacent to existing streetlight poles if streetlights exist on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are shown on the site plan. No streetlight poles appear to be in immediate conflict with building locations based on site plan geometry. Buildings are adequately separated from any potential streetlight pole locations shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review did not identify streetlight poles positioned directly adjacent to or in conflict with building footprints. Building setbacks from property lines and internal spacing suggest adequate separation.","reasoning":"Spatial relationships shown on site plan support separation compliance. No conflicts evident.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wires from existing distribution poles are not shown or mentioned on the site plan. No down guy conflicts with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or site features are evident. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of all site plan sheets, including utility plans and general notes, found no reference to or depiction of down guy wires (ground-anchored support cables from distribution poles).","reasoning":"Applicability requires down guy conflicts to exist. None shown or documented.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Angled guy anchors and associated guy easements from transmission structures are not identified on site plans. If transmission line facilities with angled guy anchors exist, they would require 10-foot-wide easements extending 50 feet beyond anchor points. No such easements are noted. This item may not be applicable or easements are not required if no angled transmission guy anchors exist.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of easement documentation (facts.md) and site plan does not identify angled transmission guy wire facilities requiring dedicated guy easements.","reasoning":"Applicability requires angled guy anchors from transmission. Not documented as existing.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchors from distribution poles are not shown or referenced on site plans. If down guy anchors exist or will exist, 10-foot-wide easements extending 5 feet past the ground entry point would be required. No such down guy anchor easements are noted. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No down guy anchor features or associated easement requirements are identified on site plans.","reasoning":"Applicability requires down guy anchors. None documented.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["pad-mounted or pole-mounted transformers shown on electrical design plan if overhead electric lines exist above or adjacent"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer locations on the site. Overhead electric facilities are shown on site plan (Sheets 9, 31) along property boundaries. However, no vertical section views or clearance dimensions are provided demonstrating that transformers maintain the minimum 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric lines that may be above or adjacent to transformer locations. Section views with clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to the top of transformer equipment must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pad locations but does not provide section views or vertical clearance dimensions relative to overhead lines. OHE shown on site plan may be above transformer locations along perimeter.","reasoning":"Without vertical clearance section views and dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformers shown on electrical design plan (Sheet 21) are pad-mounted or pole-mounted in open configuration, not in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations below grade or within structures). The 35-foot vertical clearance requirement for niche installations does not apply. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan indicates transformer locations as pad-mounted (surface installations), not niche configurations.","reasoning":"Applicability requires niche service configurations. Not proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, and work platforms during project construction near overhead electric facilities on western and southern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":6}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities exist on the site adjacent to construction areas. However, no site logistics plan, construction sequence plan, or construction staging plan is provided that demonstrates construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platforms will maintain the minimum 10-foot radial clearance (all directions) from energized overhead electric lines as required by OSHA and Texas law. A construction logistics/phasing plan showing staging areas with 10-foot clearance radii from OHE must be provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Erosion control plan (Sheets 5-7) and general construction notes (Sheet 3) were reviewed but no detailed construction staging or logistics plan showing equipment laydown zones with clearance verification from OHE is provided.","reasoning":"Construction working clearances are mandatory safety requirement. Absence of construction logistics plan showing 10-foot clearances indicates non-compliance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["cover sheet or general notes if construction near high-voltage overhead lines is proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities (distribution and transmission) exist on the site and construction is proposed. However, the site plan notes do not include the required note that the owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines (as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003). This note must be added to the cover sheet or general notes to inform all contractors and site personnel of the notification requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of Sheet 1 (Cover) and Sheet 3 (General Notes) and all blocks thereof found extensive notes about transmission line clearances, tree work, and Austin Energy requirements, but no explicit note requiring 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752.","reasoning":"Required safety note is absent. Even though general Electric Transmission Notes discuss pre-construction coordination, the specific 48-hour notification requirement mandated by state law is not stated in plan notes.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground service connections to buildings with transformers and pull boxes located on site. No through-roof service-mast installations are proposed. Service to buildings is provided via underground cable. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan explicitly shows underground electric service with pad-mounted transformers and pull boxes, not overhead service masts through roofs.","reasoning":"Applicability requires service-mast through-roof installations. Service is proposed underground.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f02ca9c1-9db7-4afc-ab4e-fb5343b7cc1c"}
