{"level":30,"time":1778275956883,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BKEZCZC9T1LAS7V3LcAxAM","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 21 (titled \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\"), here are the precise details regarding the electrical transformer pads and access points:\n\n**1. Transformer Pad Labels**\nThe transformer locations are NOT explicitly labeled with the exact phrases \"above-ground pad-mounted\" or \"underground installation points.\" Instead, they are labeled exactly as:\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**\n\nThere are four distinct locations on the plan bearing this exact label, typically pointing to a dashed square symbol:\n*   Near the northwest entrance curve.\n*   On the western edge near the \"Sidewalk Easement\" (west of Bldg. 2).\n*   In the east-central area (between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 5).\n*   In the south-central area (between Bldg. 6 and Bldg. 7).\n\n*Note:* While the transformer pads themselves are not labeled as underground, the utility lines connecting to them are explicitly labeled as **\"Underground Electric Line\"** in at least two locations (one near the western boundary and one near the east-central transformer pad).\n\n**2. Surface-Level Access Doors or Boxes**\nYes, there are numerous surface-level access boxes visible and explicitly labeled on the plan. They are identified with the exact text:\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**\n\nThese \"Electrical Pull Box\" labels point to smaller square symbols and are located frequently along the underground electrical routes, often positioned directly adjacent to or nearby the \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, as well as near the \"Electrical Meters\" banks for the buildings."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da8d4f94-c433-44b6-bc3f-ac89c89d21c6","uuid":"96991bde-2e48-4865-92ef-ef9d456