{"level":30,"time":1778275971051,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J5MDZ1UV5kzT1wRWKZDgv4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cfb3d30-a54c-43db-bd21-983850252c35","uuid":"af7c93f0-0659-45c8-a379-7a5453be3d17","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778275974296,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012g9gLRpBK28zAGLnVT3pUn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good information. There are overhead electric lines (OHE) on the western boundary/right-of-way side, but they are separated from the transformer pads by distance. However, no dimension callouts show the specific clearance distance.\n\nNow I have enough information to evaluate all 39 checklist items. Let me organize my findings:\n\n**SUMMARY OF FINDINGS FROM RESEARCH:**\n\n1. **5 Transformer Pads identified:**\n   - West of Bldg. 1, West of Bldg. 2, West of Bldg. 8, Between Bldg. 4-5, Between Bldg. 6-7\n\n2. **FAIL Items Identified:**\n   - EL-13.12: Fire hydrant clearance (2.6 ft measured vs. 5 ft required) - FAIL\n   - EL-13.38: Bollards missing around pads within 4 feet of parking/vehicle circulation - FAIL\n\n3. **NOT-VERIFIABLE Items Identified:**\n   - EL-13.21, 13.22, 13.23: Underground utility clearances (W, WW, SD) - utilities shown but no dimension callouts - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n   - EL-13.25: Underground utility clearances (12-inch minimum) - no dimensions shown - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n   - EL-13.32: Oil-filled equipment drainage - transformers not identified as oil-filled or dry-type on plans - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n   - EL-13.27, 13.28: Overhead line clearances - overhead lines shown but no dimension callouts - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n   - EL-13.37: Transformer pad dimensions - no details shown matching AE Design specifications - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n   - EL-13.13, EL-13.14, EL-13.15: Tree clearances and species verification - trees near transformers shown but no specific spatial correlation documented - Partially verifiable but need cross-reference\n   \n4. **PASS Items:**\n   - EL-13.1: Building clearance (all ≥ 10.2 ft vs. 5 ft min) - PASS\n   - EL-13.33: Property location (all 34.4+ ft from boundaries) - PASS\n   - EL-13.34: Easement avoidance (not in prohibited easements) - PASS\n\n5. **N/A Items (Applicability checking):**\n   - EL-13.2: Retaining walls - need to check if retaining walls exist\n   - EL-13.3: Fences - need to check if fences are adjacent\n   - EL-13.4\n\n: Reduced clearances (3 ft to buildings) - none shown on plans\n   - EL-13.5: Balconies/overhangs - need to verify on building elevations\n   - EL-13.6: Windows/doors/ventilating ducts - need to verify\n   - EL-13.7: Sidewalks - need to verify\n   - EL-13.8: Stairwells as fire exits - need to verify\n   - EL-13.9: Fire escapes - need to verify (only 1 fire hydrant shown, no fire escapes mentioned)\n   - EL-13.10: Hot-stick 10-ft access - depends on transformer orientation/access door location\n   - EL-13.11: 15-ft clearance for confined space - need to check if any niches exist\n   - EL-13.16-13.20: Site features like dumpsters, bike racks, light poles, and fire lanes across multiple pads require verification. EL-13.24 calls for checking gas service availability, while EL-13.26 needs confirmation on transformer placement relative to utilities. Easements and electrical routing on private property (EL-13.35, EL-13.36) should be confirmed, along with whether customer facilities exist over overhead lines (EL-13.39). Niches and cross-sections appear not applicable unless overhead structures are present.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":67170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":784},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b2369d5-d10d-43cc-a9bd-10ac3946c3f9","uuid":"ada5f84c-d305-4c3f-a6df-96cb6f2a0db6"}
