{"level":30,"time":1778275995618,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01X3etBb1Y1BY2ycheaTAqkj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've reached the end of the sheet 31 blocks. The notes section (Block 4 and Block 5) contain the landscape key notes and general notes I already reviewed. There are no notes specifically addressing electric utility clearances or tree clearance from overhead lines.\n\nNow let me compile my final findings. I have thoroughly researched the project:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY:\n\n**Infrastructure Present:**\n1. Overhead electric (OHE) lines - shown on both electrical plan (Sheet 21, western boundary) and landscape plan (Sheet 31, southern boundary)\n2. Voltage/classification: NOT SPECIFIED - default assumption is distribution (<60kV) based on grouping guidance\n3. Underground electric lines and pull boxes - shown on electrical plan\n4. Poles indicated on electrical plan (small circles along OHE line on western boundary)\n5. NO transmission easement exists\n6. NO above-ground pad-mounted transformers identified (electrical infrastructure is underground)\n\n**Trees Proposed:**\n1. Total 20 trees proposed: 2 Live Oak, 10 Cedar Elm, 2 Texas Mountain Laurel, 6 Mexican Redbud\n2. Near OHE line: Several trees marked \"M\" (Mitigation) and \"P\" (Parking Buffer Point) shown near southern boundary OHE line\n3. Species NOT identified for trees near OHE - only symbol designations (M, P) shown\n4. Mature heights NOT shown for any trees on landscape plan or in notes\n5. Utility compatibility NOT verified for any species\n\n**Dimensioning/Documentation:**\n1. NO clearance distances dimensioned on plans\n2. NO reference to Austin Energy approval or variances\n3. Trees shown graphically overlapping or in close proximity to OHE line but not dimensioned\n4. Plant schedule provided but does not clearly map species to symbol types\n5. NO notes addressing electric utility clearances\n\n**Key Deficiencies:**\n1. Trees near utilities are not identified by species (EL-2.10)\n\n\n2. Mature heights unavailable to verify large tree requirements (EL-2.11)\n3. Clearance distances not dimensioned anywhere on the plans (EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.14, EL-2.6, EL-2.8)\n4. Trees positioned near or overlapping the OHE line cannot be verified for compliance without species identification and mature height data\n\nNow evaluating each checklist item:\n\n**EL-2.1: Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution conductor**\n- Applicability: YES (OHE distribution lines present, trees proposed near them)\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: Trees near OHE line are shown but lack species identification and mature height documentation needed to determine compatibility\n\n; actual lateral distances from tree trunks to the outside conductor cannot be measured; compliance cannot be verified without this information.\n\n**EL-2.2: Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission**\n- Applicability: NO\n- Status: n/a\n- Reason: No transmission lines present on site\n\n**EL-2.3: Large trees (40+ ft) within 25 ft of distribution**\n- Applicability: YES (distribution lines present, trees proposed near them)\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: Mature heights not provided; cannot identify which trees will reach 40+ feet without species data; distances cannot be verified\n\n**EL-2.4: Large trees (40+ ft) within 50 ft of transmission**\n- Applicability: NO\n- Status: n/a\n- Reason: No transmission lines present\n\n**EL-2.5: Trees within transmission easement**\n- Applicability: NO\n- Status: n/a\n- Reason: No transmission easement present on site\n\n**EL-2.6: Trees within 10 ft of pole**\n- Applicability: YES (poles shown on electrical plan)\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: Poles appear on Sheet 21 but the landscape plan doesn't show them; without overlaying the sheets, I can't determine which trees are near which poles; distances aren't dimensioned\n\n**EL-2.7: Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment**\n- Applicability: QUESTIONABLE or NO\n- Status: n/a or NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: The \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations on Sheet 21 appear connected to underground lines, suggesting subsurface installations rather than above-ground equipment; no above-ground pad-mounted transformers are clearly shown; distances aren't provided on the landscape plan anyway\n\n**EL-2.8: Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment**\n- Applicability: YES (underground electric equipment present)\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: Underground lines and equipment are shown on the electrical plan but not on the landscape plan; tree locations relative to underground utilities cannot be determined without cross-referencing the sheets; no clearance distances are dimensioned\n\n**EL-2.9: Root barriers for trees within 20 ft of underground equipment**\n- Applicability: CONDITIONAL\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: Can't identify which trees fall within the 20 ft zone; landscape notes don't specify root barrier details for trees near electrical infrastructure\n\n**EL-2.10: Plant legend/schedule doesn't identify species near electric facilities**\n- Applicability: YES\n- Status: FAIL\n- Reason: Trees near overhead lines are marked only with symbols (M and P) rather than species names, even though the plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists the actual species available\n\n. The schedule doesn't clarify which species corresponds to which symbol on the landscape plan, making species identification impossible without cross-referencing.\n\n**EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated on plans**\n- Applicability: YES\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: The landscape plan doesn't distinguish large trees (40+ ft mature height per ECM Appendix F); while the plant schedule lists species, it lacks mature height data, so I can't determine which proposed trees meet the \"large tree\" threshold.\n\n**EL-2.12: Clearances measured from pole instead of conductor**\n- Applicability: NO\n- Status: n/a\n- Reason: No clearance dimensions appear on the plans, so this requirement only applies when clearances are actually dimensioned.\n\n**EL-2.13: Clearances measured from canopy instead of trunk**\n- Applicability: NO\n- Status: n/a\n- Reason: No clearances are dimensioned on any plans.\n\n**EL-2.14: Trees not shown in relation to overhead facilities**\n- Applicability: YES\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: Sheet 31 shows both trees and the OHE line, but without dimensions or scale verification, I cannot determine actual clearances; trees appear graphically close to or overlapping the line, but lateral distances remain unverified.\n\n**EL-2.15: Trees without Austin Energy approval in restricted zones**\n- Applicability: YES\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: Proposed trees near OHE may fall within restricted zones (15 ft distribution, 10 ft from poles), but I cannot verify without species identification and clearance measurements; no Austin Energy approval documentation was provided.\n\nThe applicant needs to submit either clearance measurements confirming compliance, an Austin Energy approval letter for any plantings that don't meet restrictions, or species identification to verify utility compatibility.\n\n**Items to Flag as FAIL:**\n- EL-2.10: Plant legend/schedule missing species identification near electric facilities\n\n**Items to Flag as NOT-VERIFIABLE:**\n- EL-2.1: Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft (species not identified)\n- EL-2.3: Large trees within 25 ft of distribution (heights not provided)\n- EL-2.6: Trees within 10 ft of pole (poles not shown in relation to trees on landscape plan)\n- EL-2.\n\n8: Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment (equipment not shown on landscape plan)\n- EL-2.9: Root barriers for trees near underground equipment (depends on EL-2.8 verification)\n- EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated (heights not provided)\n- EL-2.14: Trees not shown in relation to overhead facilities (relationship not dimensioned)\n- EL-2.15: Trees without Austin Energy approval (no approval found, distances cannot be verified)\n\n**Items to Mark as n/a:**\n- EL-2.2: Transmission lines (not present)\n- EL-2.4: Large trees from transmission (not present)\n- EL-2.5: Trees in transmission easement (not present)\n- EL-2.7: Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment (no above-ground pad-mounted equipment identified)\n- EL-2.12: Clearances from pole (no clear pole locations shown)\n- EL-2.13: Clearances from canopy (no clearances dimensioned)\n\n**Items to Mark as PASS:**\n- None identified.\n\nI need to structure the output to include every checklist item with its corresponding status, providing citations and specific details for each finding.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":61664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da8d4f94-c433-44b6-bc3f-ac89c89d21c6","uuid":"a29225f2-d1dd-4f05-9e9f-93f076e59598"}
{"level":30,"time":1778275995618,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01X3etBb1Y1BY2ycheaTAqkj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the site plan, I have completed the evaluation of all checklist items in this grouping. Let me now compile my findings into the structured format.\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY:**\n\nI have examined:\n- Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) - Shows underground electrical infrastructure, transformer pads, pull boxes, and overhead electric (OHE) lines along the western boundary\n- Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) - Shows proposed trees with symbols (M, SY, PL, P) and OHE lines along the southern boundary\n- Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations/Plant Schedule) - Lists 4 tree species (2 Live Oak, 10 Cedar Elm, 2 Texas Mountain Laurel, 6 Mexican Redbud) with quantities but does not map species to specific symbol types on the plan\n- Grading Plan (Sheet 11) - Shows electric and telephone easements but no transmission easement\n- Facts.md - Confirms no transmission easement present on property\n\n**KEY FINDINGS:**\n1. **Overhead Electric Lines Present**: YES - OHE lines run along property boundaries\n2. **Voltage Classification**: NOT SPECIFIED on plans (default assumption: distribution per grouping guidance)\n3. **Trees Near OHE Lines**: YES - Several trees marked \"M\" (Mitigation) and \"P\" (Parking Buffer Point) shown near southern boundary OHE line\n4. **Species Identification**: Trees near utilities are only designated by symbols; NO species names provided on landscape plan\n5. **Mature Heights**: Not provided for any proposed trees\n6. **Clearance Measurements**: No distances dimensioned on plans\n7. **Austin Energy Approval**: No documentation found in submitted materials"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":61664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da8d4f94-c433-44b6-bc3f-ac89c89d21c6","uuid":"46ff75c3-ada2-4720-9cd6-118b8306a33d"}
{"level":30,"time":1778275995618,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015yvhCd8oScjg2sCdR7sDhb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Based on the README, the sheets are:\n- Sheet 29: Addressing Plan (building layouts)\n- No specific elevation sheets mentioned by name\n\nThe project appears to be preliminary architectural plans only. Let me now systematically evaluate the 39 checklist items based on what I've gathered.\n\nKEY FINDINGS SUMMARY:\n1. Transformer pads ARE shown on Sheet 21 (5 pads located)\n2. Located on private property (all within property boundaries)\n3. NO pad dimensions shown\n4. NO Austin Energy Design detail references\n5. ~4 pads within 4 feet of parking/drive aisles - NO bollards shown\n6. NO fire escapes identified on site\n7. NO transformer specifications (oil-filled vs. dry, single vs. three-phase)\n8. Transformers NOT shown on grading plan (so drainage direction cannot be evaluated)\n9. Transformers NOT shown on landscape plan (so vegetation clearances cannot be verified)\n10. Transformers NOT shown on utility plan with utility crossings\n11. NO transformer easements shown\n12. Service routing is shown but pad-specific dimensions and clearances not documented\n\nNow I'll evaluate each item. Let me be systematic and thorough, going through each checklist item and determining: pass, fail, not-verifiable, or n/a.\n\nITEMS TO EVALUATE:\n1. EL-13.1: 5-foot clearance from buildings - VISION showed pads are \"near buildings\" but no specific measurements\n2. EL-13.2: 5-foot clearance from retaining walls - retaining walls are shown on plans, need to check proximity\n3. EL-13.3: Clearance from fences (5ft for operator sides, 3ft for non-operator) - fences shown, need access door orientation\n4. EL-13.4: 3-foot reduced clearance with AE Design approval - no such clearances documented\n5. EL-13.5: 5-foot lateral clearance from balconies/overhangs - no balconies/overhangs explicitly shown near pads\n\n\n6. EL-13.6: 12-foot clearance from windows/doors (oil-filled equipment) - building elevations not provided, so I can't verify this requirement\n7. EL-13.7: 2-foot clearance from back of sidewalks - sidewalks are shown on plans\n8. EL-13.8: Clearance from stairwells serving as fire exits - no stairwells identified as fire exits on the drawings\n9. EL-13.9: 20-foot clearance from fire escapes (oil-filled) - no fire escapes shown on site\n10. EL-13.10: 10-foot hot-stick clearance for access door side - access door orientation not shown on pad details\n11. EL-13.11: 15-foot clearance when facing confined space - site plan doesn't indicate confined spaces. Fire hydrants are shown on Sheet 10 with a required 5-foot separation. Trees within 10 feet need to be utility-compatible, but transformer locations aren't on the landscape plan, making this difficult to verify. Same issue with shrub placement requirements at 10 feet from the access door and 5 feet from other sides. Root barriers for trees within 20 feet also can't be confirmed without transformer placement. Dumpsters aren't shown (residential trash collection isn't visible), bike racks appear on the landscape plan with a 5-foot clearance needed, and light poles also require 5-foot separation.\n\nFire lanes shown on Sheet 10 need 15-foot clearance. Five transformer pads exist but their distances from each other aren't documented. Water, wastewater, and storm drain lines all require 5-foot horizontal clearance, yet transformers aren't positioned on the utility plan. Gas service isn't indicated in the project, so the 24-36 inch clearance requirement doesn't apply. Other utilities need 12-inch clearance and transformers shouldn't be placed over or under them, but again, transformer locations aren't shown on utility plans. Overhead distribution lines would be on the utility plan and require 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance.\n\nOverhead distribution conductors need a 15-foot radius clearance. No niche configuration exists, so the 35-foot vertical clearance and 3-hour fire rating requirements for niches don't apply. Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances above transformers are missing. Oil-filled transformers need drainage away from the building, but transformer placement isn't shown on the grading plan. The location is confirmed on private property per the vision check. Easement exhibits need review to verify no prohibited easements exist, and transformer easements haven't been shown yet.\n\nElectrical routing from the transformer to meters must be verified as entirely on private property. Pad dimensions don't match the architectural design details. Four pads are within 4 feet of parking areas but no bollards are indicated. Need to confirm proposed structures won't be positioned under any overhead distribution lines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1337,"cache_read_input_tokens":63206,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1337},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cfb3d30-a54c-43db-bd21-983850252c35","uuid":"20ee9d6f-19f9-49d7-91c4-067505c216c6"}
