{"level":30,"time":1778276070137,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015m7FdD9KurzRcSgKezNTbB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UecTzVVLfRo54LzijkbU8d","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["South property line along overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees (marked M) are shown on landscape plan within 0.1-3.2 feet of the overhead electric distribution line. However, these trees are not identified by species on Sheet 31. While Sheet 35 provides a plant schedule listing proposed species, the specific species corresponding to the mitigation trees near the OHE line cannot be determined from the landscape plan. Without species identification, utility compatibility status (required per ECM Appendix F UC column) cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Mitigation trees marked with 'M' symbols on the landscape plan are positioned 0.1 to 3.2 feet from the OHE line. Vision analysis found the trees are not identified by species on Sheet 31, and the Key Notes only indicate 'M - MITIGATION TREE' without species reference.","reasoning":"The grouping requires verification against ECM Appendix F utility compatibility (UC) column. The mitigation trees near the distribution conductor lack species identification on the landscape plan, preventing determination of whether they are utility-compatible. This makes compliance with the 15-foot minimum clearance requirement for non-utility-compatible trees unverifiable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead transmission lines (60kV or higher) are shown or referenced in the site plan. The project shows only distribution-level overhead electric infrastructure. This requirement applies only when transmission facilities are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric line shown on landscape plan is labeled 'OHE' with typical distribution voltage characteristics for a townhome development. No transmission easements, transmission-specific labels, or facilities characteristic of high-voltage transmission (69kV, 138kV, 345kV) are depicted.","reasoning":"Transmission clearance requirements apply only when transmission facilities (60kV or greater) are present on the project. Evidence indicates distribution-only infrastructure, so this item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["South property line along overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on the landscape plan within 0.1-3.2 feet of the overhead distribution conductor. The plant schedule lists Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) and Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) as shade trees with 100-gallon containers, which typically indicates mature heights of 40+ feet. However, the landscape plan does not differentiate trees by mature height or identify which of the mitigation trees near the OHE line are large trees. Without species and size identification on the landscape plan, compliance with the 25-foot minimum clearance for large trees cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows multiple trees very close to the OHE line (0.1-3.2 feet) but provides no species or height differentiation. Sheet 35 lists proposed species including Live Oak and Cedar Elm (typically 40+ feet mature height), but their specific locations relative to the OHE line cannot be determined.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) within 25 feet of distribution conductors. The trees shown near the OHE line (0.1-3.2 feet) are far less than 25 feet away. If any of these proximate trees are Live Oak or Cedar Elm, they would violate this requirement. However, species identification on the landscape plan is missing, making verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead transmission facilities (60kV or higher) are shown on the site plan. This requirement applies only when transmission lines are present on the project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Only distribution-level overhead electric infrastructure is depicted on the plans; no transmission lines, transmission easements, or transmission facility characteristics are evident.","reasoning":"Transmission clearance requirements do not apply when only distribution facilities are present.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is depicted on the grading plan, site plan, or plat (Sheet 2). This requirement applies only when a transmission easement is present on the property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan, plat, and grading plan shows no transmission easement boundaries. Easements referenced in facts.md are drainage and wastewater easements, not transmission.","reasoning":"The categorical prohibition against trees in transmission easements applies only when such easements exist. No transmission easement is shown on submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric infrastructure locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric utility poles are NOT explicitly marked or identified on the landscape plan. The overhead electric line is shown (OHE), but specific pole locations are not indicated. Without pole locations identified on the landscape plan, the 10-foot clearance requirement from individual poles cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan found no distinct utility pole symbols or labels. While an overhead electric line is marked 'OHE' running along the south property line, individual pole locations are not depicted or labeled.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies 10 feet lateral distance from 'overhead electric utility pole.' Without pole locations shown on the landscape plan, tree proximity to poles cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Pad-mounted electrical equipment locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pad-mounted electric equipment is not depicted or cross-referenced on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). While the electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground transformers and electrical infrastructure, there is no overlay or cross-reference to allow verification of tree proximity to pad-mounted equipment on the landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan found no symbols, labels, or legend entries for pad-mounted electrical equipment. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) contains this information, but it is not transposed to or referenced on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment. Without equipment locations identified on the landscape plan or cross-referenced between plans, proximity cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Underground electric equipment locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electric equipment (transformers, pull boxes, vaults) is shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21) but is NOT depicted on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). Without underground equipment locations identified on or cross-referenced to the landscape plan, the 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified. The two plans must be overlaid to determine if any proposed trees are within 5 feet of underground equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan found no symbols or references to underground electrical equipment. The electrical plan shows transformers and pull boxes, but these locations are not transposed to or cross-referenced on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies trees within 5 lateral feet of underground electric equipment. Equipment locations on Sheet 21 cannot be cross-referenced to tree locations on Sheet 31 due to lack of overlay or cross-reference notation, making verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barrier requirements cannot be verified because: (1) tree locations relative to underground equipment cannot be determined (see EL-2.8); (2) no root barrier details or specifications are shown on the landscape plan or detail sheets. Without knowing which trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment, the requirement for 4-foot-deep root barriers positioned 5 feet from equipment cannot be evaluated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan does not show underground equipment locations or identify trees that might require root barriers. Review of landscape detail sheet (Sheet 37) found no root barrier specifications referenced for trees near electrical equipment.","reasoning":"Root barrier requirements apply only to trees within 20 feet of underground equipment. Without equipment locations cross-referenced to the landscape plan, affected trees cannot be identified, and barrier specifications cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["South property line along overhead electric line; entire landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed on the landscape plan are identified only by function (SY - Street Yard, PL - Parking Lot, P - Parking Buffer Point, M - Mitigation Tree), not by species. The mitigation trees (M) positioned near the overhead electric line on the south property line have no species identification on Sheet 31. While a plant schedule with species is provided on Sheet 35, the landscape plan does not reference it or identify which specific species correspond to each tree location. For electric utility compliance verification, all trees must be identified by species.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan Key Notes found tree designations limited to: 'SY - STREET YARD TREE,' 'PL - PARKING LOT TREE,' 'P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE,' and 'M - MITIGATION TREE.' No species names (common or scientific) appear anywhere on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"The grouping guide specifies that tree species identification is required to verify utility compatibility, mature height, and other electrical safety requirements. The absence of species names on the landscape plan near electric facilities violates the requirement for complete documentation.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Entire landscape plan; south property line where trees are near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees on the landscape plan are not differentiated by mature height or size class. All trees are represented by similar circular canopy symbols without notation indicating whether they are large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F), medium trees, or small trees. The plant schedule on Sheet 35 indicates that proposed shade trees include Live Oak and Cedar Elm (both typically 40+ feet mature height) and ornamental trees including Texas Mountain Laurel and Mexican Redbud (20-30 feet). However, on the landscape plan, there is no visual or textual differentiation to identify which trees are 40+ feet. This prevents verification of the 25-foot clearance requirement for large trees near overhead distribution lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows all trees with the same general canopy symbol style (circles with center points), categorized only by functional use (SY, PL, P, M). No size classes, height ranges, caliper designations, or mature height categories are indicated on the plan.","reasoning":"Verification of compliance with large-tree clearance requirements (EL-2.3) depends on being able to identify which trees meet the 40+ foot mature height threshold. The landscape plan provides no mechanism to distinguish large trees from smaller ones, making compliance verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No tree clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan or site plan. Because no clearances are dimensioned, the requirement to measure from outer conductor (not pole centerline) does not apply. This requirement becomes applicable only if and when clearances are dimensioned on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan found no dimension lines, distance annotations, or clearance callouts for trees relative to the overhead electric line or any other utilities.","reasoning":"The requirement governs the measurement methodology for clearances that have been dimensioned. Since no clearances are shown, the measurement-reference-point requirement is not triggered.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No tree clearance dimensions are shown on the plans. Because no clearances are dimensioned, the requirement to measure from tree trunk location (not canopy edge) does not apply. This requirement becomes applicable only if and when clearances are dimensioned.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No dimension lines or clearance annotations are present on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies how to measure clearances when they are dimensioned. Absence of dimensional callouts makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["South property line along overhead electric infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees and overhead electric facilities are shown on the same landscape plan sheet. The OHE line is clearly marked along the south property line, and tree symbols (including mitigation trees) are visible on the same plan, allowing visual identification of spatial relationships. However, the lack of species identification (EL-2.10) and size differentiation (EL-2.11) limits the utility of this visual relationship for full compliance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Both the OHE line (labeled '- OHE -') and proposed tree symbols are depicted on Sheet 31 landscape plan. Tree and utility line locations are spatially visible together.","reasoning":"The requirement that trees be 'shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities' is satisfied when both elements appear on the same plan. While additional information is needed for full compliance verification, the basic requirement to show spatial relationships is met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["South property line where mitigation trees are shown near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees are shown on the landscape plan within 0.1-3.2 feet of the overhead electric distribution conductor, which is well within prohibited clearance zones (<15 feet for non-utility-compatible trees). However, without species identification, it cannot be determined whether these trees are utility-compatible or non-compatible. If any are non-utility-compatible large trees, or if they violate other clearance requirements, Austin Energy written approval would be required. No Austin Energy approval documentation is evident in the site plan package. Cannot verify compliance with this requirement without first determining tree species and applicability of clearance restrictions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Mitigation trees are positioned at 0.1-3.2 feet from the OHE line—distances that would trigger the need for Austin Energy approval if clearance requirements are violated. No approval letters or correspondence from Austin Energy are included in the site plan package.","reasoning":"Trees within prohibited clearance zones require explicit written Austin Energy approval per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Without species identification, compliance with clearance thresholds cannot be determined, and therefore the applicability and status of Austin Energy approval cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":65029,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e1eed96-d749-4c9f-b941-3ae8c1ee87e2","uuid":"058ff7e7-447e-4582-9c54-b1a1b11158be"}
