{"level":30,"time":1778276070137,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QF9J2j4fVbjLtN7AuuR8c2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've successfully completed the evaluation of all 15 checklist items for grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\nLet me summarize what I found:\n\n**FINDINGS SUMMARY:**\n\n**FAILS (2 items):**\n- EL-2.10: Plant species not identified on landscape plan (trees identified only by function, not species)\n- EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated on landscape plan (no size/height indication)\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE (7 items):**\n- EL-2.1: Species utility compatibility cannot be determined\n- EL-2.3: Large tree status and clearances cannot be verified\n- EL-2.6: Utility pole locations not shown\n- EL-2.7: Pad-mount equipment not shown on landscape plan  \n- EL-2.8: Underground equipment not cross-referenced to landscape plan\n- EL-2.9: Root barrier requirements cannot be verified\n- EL-2.15: Austin Energy approval status cannot be verified\n\n**N/A (4 items):**\n- EL-2.2: No transmission lines\n- EL-2.4: No transmission lines  \n- EL-2.5: No transmission easement\n- EL-2.12: No clearances dimensioned\n- EL-2.13: No clearances dimensioned\n\n**PASS (1 item):**\n- EL-2.14: Trees and OHE shown on same plan\n\n**CRITICAL ISSUES IDENTIFIED:**\n1. Trees are shown within 0.1-3.2 feet of the overhead electric line on the south property line\n2. These trees lack species identification on the landscape plan\n3. Proposed species include large trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) that may violate 25-foot clearance requirements\n4. Underground electrical equipment shown on Sheet 21 is not cross-referenced on the landscape plan\n5. No utility poles, pad-mounts, or underground equipment are shown on or referenced from the landscape plan\n\n\n6. Clearance dimensions and Austin Energy approvals are missing from the documentation\n\nThis grouping applies fully given the overhead distribution lines present on the site, and the identified deficiencies will need to be addressed by the applicant.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6425,"cache_read_input_tokens":65691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6425},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e1eed96-d749-4c9f-b941-3ae8c1ee87e2","uuid":"02824de3-17a8-4244-aeb7-c94cf994843f"}
{"level":30,"time":1778276070137,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QF9J2j4fVbjLtN7AuuR8c2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines (Grouping 2)\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for electric utility tree clearance requirements (grouping 2). Here's a summary of my findings:\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**APPLICABILITY CONFIRMED:** This grouping is fully applicable. Overhead electric distribution lines are clearly shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) along the south property line, with multiple trees proposed in close proximity (0.1-3.2 feet).\n\n**CRITICAL DEFICIENCIES IDENTIFIED:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10 (FAIL):** Tree species are NOT identified on the landscape plan. Trees are labeled only by function (M=Mitigation, SY=Street Yard, etc.) without species names. While Sheet 35 lists proposed species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud), there is no cross-reference on the landscape plan to match species to specific locations.\n\n2. **EL-2.11 (FAIL):** Large trees (40+ feet mature height) are not differentiated on the landscape plan. All trees are shown with identical symbols, making it impossible to identify which are large trees that require 25-foot clearances from distribution conductors.\n\n3. **Multiple NOT-VERIFIABLE items:** Tree clearances cannot be verified because:\n   - Species identification is missing (EL-2.1, EL-2.3)\n   - Utility pole locations are not marked (EL-2.6)\n   - Underground equipment shown on Sheet 21 is not cross-referenced to the landscape plan (EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9)\n   - No Austin Energy approvals are documented (EL-2.15)\n\n**PASS:** EL-2.14 - Trees and OHE are shown on the same plan sheet, though species identification prevents full verification.\n\n**N/A:** EL-2.2, 2.4, 2.5 (no transmission lines/easements); EL-2.12, 2.13 (no clearances dimensioned).\n\n### Required Actions:\nThe applicant must provide:\n- Species identification for all proposed trees on the landscape plan, especially mitigation trees near the overhead electric line\n- Size/height differentiation for large trees (40+ feet)\n- Cross-reference of underground electrical equipment locations from Sheet 21 to the landscape plan\n- Verification of utility compatibility per ECM Appendix F for all proposed species\n- Documentation of Austin Energy approval if trees are proposed in prohibited clearance zones"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6425,"cache_read_input_tokens":65691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6425},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e1eed96-d749-4c9f-b941-3ae8c1ee87e2","uuid":"58a88f39-4525-4f7b-bec1-065a63d396b6"}
{"level":30,"time":1778276070137,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":2870350,"duration_api_ms":161672,"num_turns":23,"result":"## Review Complete: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines (Grouping 2)\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for electric utility tree clearance requirements (grouping 2). Here's a summary of my findings:\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**APPLICABILITY CONFIRMED:** This grouping is fully applicable. Overhead electric distribution lines are clearly shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) along the south property line, with multiple trees proposed in close proximity (0.1-3.2 feet).\n\n**CRITICAL DEFICIENCIES IDENTIFIED:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10 (FAIL):** Tree species are NOT identified on the landscape plan. Trees are labeled only by function (M=Mitigation, SY=Street Yard, etc.) without species names. While Sheet 35 lists proposed species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud), there is no cross-reference on the landscape plan to match species to specific locations.\n\n2. **EL-2.11 (FAIL):** Large trees (40+ feet mature height) are not differentiated on the landscape plan. All trees are shown with identical symbols, making it impossible to identify which are large trees that require 25-foot clearances from distribution conductors.\n\n3. **Multiple NOT-VERIFIABLE items:** Tree clearances cannot be verified because:\n   - Species identification is missing (EL-2.1, EL-2.3)\n   - Utility pole locations are not marked (EL-2.6)\n   - Underground equipment shown on Sheet 21 is not cross-referenced to the landscape plan (EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9)\n   - No Austin Energy approvals are documented (EL-2.15)\n\n**PASS:** EL-2.14 - Trees and OHE are shown on the same plan sheet, though species identification prevents full verification.\n\n**N/A:** EL-2.2, 2.4, 2.5 (no transmission lines/easements); EL-2.12, 2.13 (no clearances dimensioned).\n\n### Required Actions:\nThe applicant must provide:\n- Species identification for all proposed trees on the landscape plan, especially mitigation trees near the overhead electric line\n- Size/height differentiation for large trees (40+ feet)\n- Cross-reference of underground electrical equipment locations from Sheet 21 to the landscape plan\n- Verification of utility compatibility per ECM Appendix F for all proposed species\n- Documentation of Austin Energy approval if trees are proposed in prohibited clearance zones","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4e1eed96-d749-4c9f-b941-3ae8c1ee87e2","total_cost_usd":0.23047525000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":47403,"cache_read_input_tokens":860405,"output_tokens":17012,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":47403,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":121,"outputTokens":17012,"cacheReadInputTokens":860405,"cacheCreationInputTokens":47403,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.23047525000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["South property line along overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees (marked M) are shown on landscape plan within 0.1-3.2 feet of the overhead electric distribution line. However, these trees are not identified by species on Sheet 31. While Sheet 35 provides a plant schedule listing proposed species, the specific species corresponding to the mitigation trees near the OHE line cannot be determined from the landscape plan. Without species identification, utility compatibility status (required per ECM Appendix F UC column) cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Mitigation trees marked with 'M' symbols on the landscape plan are positioned 0.1 to 3.2 feet from the OHE line. Vision analysis found the trees are not identified by species on Sheet 31, and the Key Notes only indicate 'M - MITIGATION TREE' without species reference.","reasoning":"The grouping requires verification against ECM Appendix F utility compatibility (UC) column. The mitigation trees near the distribution conductor lack species identification on the landscape plan, preventing determination of whether they are utility-compatible. This makes compliance with the 15-foot minimum clearance requirement for non-utility-compatible trees unverifiable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead transmission lines (60kV or higher) are shown or referenced in the site plan. The project shows only distribution-level overhead electric infrastructure. This requirement applies only when transmission facilities are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric line shown on landscape plan is labeled 'OHE' with typical distribution voltage characteristics for a townhome development. No transmission easements, transmission-specific labels, or facilities characteristic of high-voltage transmission (69kV, 138kV, 345kV) are depicted.","reasoning":"Transmission clearance requirements apply only when transmission facilities (60kV or greater) are present on the project. Evidence indicates distribution-only infrastructure, so this item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["South property line along overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on the landscape plan within 0.1-3.2 feet of the overhead distribution conductor. The plant schedule lists Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) and Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) as shade trees with 100-gallon containers, which typically indicates mature heights of 40+ feet. However, the landscape plan does not differentiate trees by mature height or identify which of the mitigation trees near the OHE line are large trees. Without species and size identification on the landscape plan, compliance with the 25-foot minimum clearance for large trees cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows multiple trees very close to the OHE line (0.1-3.2 feet) but provides no species or height differentiation. Sheet 35 lists proposed species including Live Oak and Cedar Elm (typically 40+ feet mature height), but their specific locations relative to the OHE line cannot be determined.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) within 25 feet of distribution conductors. The trees shown near the OHE line (0.1-3.2 feet) are far less than 25 feet away. If any of these proximate trees are Live Oak or Cedar Elm, they would violate this requirement. However, species identification on the landscape plan is missing, making verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead transmission facilities (60kV or higher) are shown on the site plan. This requirement applies only when transmission lines are present on the project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Only distribution-level overhead electric infrastructure is depicted on the plans; no transmission lines, transmission easements, or transmission facility characteristics are evident.","reasoning":"Transmission clearance requirements do not apply when only distribution facilities are present.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is depicted on the grading plan, site plan, or plat (Sheet 2). This requirement applies only when a transmission easement is present on the property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan, plat, and grading plan shows no transmission easement boundaries. Easements referenced in facts.md are drainage and wastewater easements, not transmission.","reasoning":"The categorical prohibition against trees in transmission easements applies only when such easements exist. No transmission easement is shown on submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric infrastructure locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric utility poles are NOT explicitly marked or identified on the landscape plan. The overhead electric line is shown (OHE), but specific pole locations are not indicated. Without pole locations identified on the landscape plan, the 10-foot clearance requirement from individual poles cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan found no distinct utility pole symbols or labels. While an overhead electric line is marked 'OHE' running along the south property line, individual pole locations are not depicted or labeled.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies 10 feet lateral distance from 'overhead electric utility pole.' Without pole locations shown on the landscape plan, tree proximity to poles cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Pad-mounted electrical equipment locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pad-mounted electric equipment is not depicted or cross-referenced on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). While the electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground transformers and electrical infrastructure, there is no overlay or cross-reference to allow verification of tree proximity to pad-mounted equipment on the landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan found no symbols, labels, or legend entries for pad-mounted electrical equipment. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) contains this information, but it is not transposed to or referenced on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment. Without equipment locations identified on the landscape plan or cross-referenced between plans, proximity cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Underground electric equipment locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electric equipment (transformers, pull boxes, vaults) is shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21) but is NOT depicted on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). Without underground equipment locations identified on or cross-referenced to the landscape plan, the 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified. The two plans must be overlaid to determine if any proposed trees are within 5 feet of underground equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan found no symbols or references to underground electrical equipment. The electrical plan shows transformers and pull boxes, but these locations are not transposed to or cross-referenced on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies trees within 5 lateral feet of underground electric equipment. Equipment locations on Sheet 21 cannot be cross-referenced to tree locations on Sheet 31 due to lack of overlay or cross-reference notation, making verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barrier requirements cannot be verified because: (1) tree locations relative to underground equipment cannot be determined (see EL-2.8); (2) no root barrier details or specifications are shown on the landscape plan or detail sheets. Without knowing which trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment, the requirement for 4-foot-deep root barriers positioned 5 feet from equipment cannot be evaluated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan does not show underground equipment locations or identify trees that might require root barriers. Review of landscape detail sheet (Sheet 37) found no root barrier specifications referenced for trees near electrical equipment.","reasoning":"Root barrier requirements apply only to trees within 20 feet of underground equipment. Without equipment locations cross-referenced to the landscape plan, affected trees cannot be identified, and barrier specifications cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["South property line along overhead electric line; entire landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed on the landscape plan are identified only by function (SY - Street Yard, PL - Parking Lot, P - Parking Buffer Point, M - Mitigation Tree), not by species. The mitigation trees (M) positioned near the overhead electric line on the south property line have no species identification on Sheet 31. While a plant schedule with species is provided on Sheet 35, the landscape plan does not reference it or identify which specific species correspond to each tree location. For electric utility compliance verification, all trees must be identified by species.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan Key Notes found tree designations limited to: 'SY - STREET YARD TREE,' 'PL - PARKING LOT TREE,' 'P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE,' and 'M - MITIGATION TREE.' No species names (common or scientific) appear anywhere on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"The grouping guide specifies that tree species identification is required to verify utility compatibility, mature height, and other electrical safety requirements. The absence of species names on the landscape plan near electric facilities violates the requirement for complete documentation.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Entire landscape plan; south property line where trees are near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees on the landscape plan are not differentiated by mature height or size class. All trees are represented by similar circular canopy symbols without notation indicating whether they are large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F), medium trees, or small trees. The plant schedule on Sheet 35 indicates that proposed shade trees include Live Oak and Cedar Elm (both typically 40+ feet mature height) and ornamental trees including Texas Mountain Laurel and Mexican Redbud (20-30 feet). However, on the landscape plan, there is no visual or textual differentiation to identify which trees are 40+ feet. This prevents verification of the 25-foot clearance requirement for large trees near overhead distribution lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows all trees with the same general canopy symbol style (circles with center points), categorized only by functional use (SY, PL, P, M). No size classes, height ranges, caliper designations, or mature height categories are indicated on the plan.","reasoning":"Verification of compliance with large-tree clearance requirements (EL-2.3) depends on being able to identify which trees meet the 40+ foot mature height threshold. The landscape plan provides no mechanism to distinguish large trees from smaller ones, making compliance verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No tree clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan or site plan. Because no clearances are dimensioned, the requirement to measure from outer conductor (not pole centerline) does not apply. This requirement becomes applicable only if and when clearances are dimensioned on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan found no dimension lines, distance annotations, or clearance callouts for trees relative to the overhead electric line or any other utilities.","reasoning":"The requirement governs the measurement methodology for clearances that have been dimensioned. Since no clearances are shown, the measurement-reference-point requirement is not triggered.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No tree clearance dimensions are shown on the plans. Because no clearances are dimensioned, the requirement to measure from tree trunk location (not canopy edge) does not apply. This requirement becomes applicable only if and when clearances are dimensioned.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No dimension lines or clearance annotations are present on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies how to measure clearances when they are dimensioned. Absence of dimensional callouts makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["South property line along overhead electric infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees and overhead electric facilities are shown on the same landscape plan sheet. The OHE line is clearly marked along the south property line, and tree symbols (including mitigation trees) are visible on the same plan, allowing visual identification of spatial relationships. However, the lack of species identification (EL-2.10) and size differentiation (EL-2.11) limits the utility of this visual relationship for full compliance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Both the OHE line (labeled '- OHE -') and proposed tree symbols are depicted on Sheet 31 landscape plan. Tree and utility line locations are spatially visible together.","reasoning":"The requirement that trees be 'shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities' is satisfied when both elements appear on the same plan. While additional information is needed for full compliance verification, the basic requirement to show spatial relationships is met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["South property line where mitigation trees are shown near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees are shown on the landscape plan within 0.1-3.2 feet of the overhead electric distribution conductor, which is well within prohibited clearance zones (<15 feet for non-utility-compatible trees). However, without species identification, it cannot be determined whether these trees are utility-compatible or non-compatible. If any are non-utility-compatible large trees, or if they violate other clearance requirements, Austin Energy written approval would be required. No Austin Energy approval documentation is evident in the site plan package. Cannot verify compliance with this requirement without first determining tree species and applicability of clearance restrictions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Mitigation trees are positioned at 0.1-3.2 feet from the OHE line—distances that would trigger the need for Austin Energy approval if clearance requirements are violated. No approval letters or correspondence from Austin Energy are included in the site plan package.","reasoning":"Trees within prohibited clearance zones require explicit written Austin Energy approval per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Without species identification, compliance with clearance thresholds cannot be determined, and therefore the applicability and status of Austin Energy approval cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c70caa9c-193b-46e3-9d49-b99eb65cabe7"}
{"level":30,"time":1778276070138,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01X3etBb1Y1BY2ycheaTAqkj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018DXXMegVPmWgPssExQm1F5","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near OHE line where trees marked M and P are located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed near overhead electric distribution line (southern boundary) are marked only with symbols (M, P) and are not identified by species name on the landscape plan. Without species identification, utility compatibility status cannot be verified. Plant schedule lists species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but does not clearly map which species are used for trees near the OHE line. Actual lateral distances from tree trunks to outside conductor are not dimensioned.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows several tree symbols (M and P) near the overhead electric line on the southern boundary, but these trees are identified only by their designation symbols, not by species names. The plant schedule lists four proposed tree species with quantities but does not indicate which species correspond to which locations or symbols on the plan.","reasoning":"The reviewer cannot verify compliance with utility-compatible tree requirements because the species identity is unknown. Without species identification, it is impossible to cross-reference against ECM Appendix F to determine utility compatibility designation. Additionally, the submitted plans do not dimension the lateral distances from tree trunks to the outside conductor, preventing verification of the 15-foot minimum clearance requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines are present or proposed on the site. Facts.md confirms no transmission easement exists on the property. The overhead electric lines shown on the plans are not identified as transmission facilities and, per grouping guidance, are assumed to be distribution lines typical of development sites. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of facts.md and easement documentation reveals only 5-foot electric easements (typical of distribution) and no transmission easement on the property. The overhead electric lines shown on the electrical and landscape plans are not labeled with voltage levels or identified as transmission infrastructure.","reasoning":"Since no transmission infrastructure is present on the site, this requirement is not applicable. The applicability gate established in the grouping guidance indicates this item applies only when transmission facilities are present.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed near the overhead electric distribution line cannot be verified as compliant with the 25-foot clearance requirement for large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) because: (1) trees near the OHE line are not identified by species on the landscape plan; (2) mature heights are not provided for any proposed trees in the plant schedule or landscape notes; (3) actual lateral distances from tree trunks to outside conductor are not dimensioned. Without this information, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule lists proposed tree species and quantities but does not provide mature height information for any species. The landscape plan shows tree symbols near the OHE line but does not identify which species these trees are or provide height designations to distinguish large trees (40+ feet) from smaller specimens.","reasoning":"Verification of compliance with the large tree clearance requirement requires identifying which proposed trees have a mature height of 40 feet or greater per ECM Appendix F, and then measuring the lateral distance from those trees to the outside conductor. Since species are not identified on the landscape plan and heights are not provided, this verification is not possible from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines are present on the site. This requirement applies only when transmission infrastructure is present. See EL-2.2 for basis of inapplicability.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transmission easement or transmission-voltage infrastructure is identified in the site plan documents or facts.md.","reasoning":"This item is conditional on the presence of transmission facilities, which do not exist on this property.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is present on the site. Facts.md confirms absence of transmission infrastructure. This requirement applies only when transmission easement boundaries are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of facts.md, grading plan, and site plan shows no transmission easement. Only 5-foot electric easements and other drainage/utility easements are identified.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditional on the presence of a transmission easement boundary. Since no such easement exists, the requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric poles on western boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility poles are indicated on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) as small circles spaced along the overhead electric line on the western boundary. However, the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not show pole locations. Without pole locations depicted on the landscape plan in relation to proposed trees, the 10-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified. Actual lateral distances from tree trunks to poles are not dimensioned on either plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical design plan shows utility pole symbols along the OHE line, but the landscape plan does not indicate pole locations. The two plans use the same scale (1\" = 20') but cannot be directly compared without an overlay analysis, which is not available.","reasoning":"Verification of compliance requires that pole locations be clearly shown on the landscape plan (or cross-referenced) in relation to proposed trees, with actual distances dimensioned. The absence of pole locations on the landscape plan means compliance cannot be verified from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical design plan shows locations labeled as 'Electrical Transformer Pad' connected to 'Underground Electric Lines.' These appear to be underground utility installations rather than above-ground pad-mounted transformers. No above-ground pad-mounted equipment with visible enclosures and access doors (as described in the code requirement) is identified on the plans. This requirement applies only when above-ground pad-mounted equipment is present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan labels show 'Electrical Transformer Pad' locations connected to 'Underground Electric Lines,' which indicates these are subsurface installations accessed via above-ground pull boxes rather than typical above-ground pad-mounted transformers.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 restrictions on trees near pad-mounted equipment typically refer to the above-ground metal enclosures visible on the surface. The submitted plans show only underground installations with surface access points (pull boxes), which are not pad-mounted equipment in the traditional sense. Therefore, this requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Locations of underground electrical equipment shown on electrical plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric lines, pull boxes, and transformer pad locations. However, the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not show these underground equipment locations in relation to proposed trees. Without underground equipment locations depicted on the landscape plan, and without dimensioned distances, compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Underground electrical infrastructure is shown on the electrical plan but is not depicted or referenced on the landscape plan. The two plans cannot be directly correlated to determine proximity of proposed trees to underground equipment.","reasoning":"The landscape plan must either show underground equipment locations (often depicted with dashed lines or access point symbols) or must provide written coordination notes addressing clearances from underground utilities. Without this information, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Locations of underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement is conditional on trees being proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment (EL-2.8). Because compliance with EL-2.8 cannot be verified (underground equipment locations not shown on landscape plan), EL-2.9 cannot be evaluated. Additionally, the landscape plan notes do not specify root barrier requirements for trees near electrical equipment. Plans must either demonstrate trees are beyond 20 feet of underground equipment, or must show root barrier details (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) on the landscape plan or details sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan and notes do not show underground equipment locations or specify root barrier requirements. No details are provided for root barriers in the reviewed landscape notes or detail sheets.","reasoning":"Without knowing which trees, if any, are within 20 feet of underground equipment, and without any root barrier specifications provided, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric line on southern boundary (marked M and P symbols)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed near the overhead electric line on the southern boundary are identified only by category symbols (M for Mitigation Tree, P for Parking Buffer Point Tree) and are NOT identified by species name on the landscape plan. While a plant schedule is provided on Sheet 35 listing species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) and quantities, the schedule does not clearly indicate which species are used for trees at the M and P locations on the landscape plan. Species identification on or adjacent to tree symbols on the landscape plan is required to allow verification of utility compatibility and clearance compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows tree symbols (M and P) near the overhead electric infrastructure but does not label these trees with species names. The plant schedule provides a list of species with quantities but does not map specific species to specific locations or symbol types on the plan.","reasoning":"Species identification is essential for verifying compliance with utility compatibility requirements (ECM Appendix F UC column) and for determining mature heights needed to assess clearance requirements. The absence of species names on the landscape plan for trees near electric facilities is a deficiency. The applicant must either add species labels to trees on the landscape plan or provide a clear key/legend that maps plant schedule species to landscape plan symbol locations.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) are not differentiated on the landscape plan. The plant schedule lists species names but does not provide mature height information for any trees. Without height designations on the landscape plan or in the plant schedule, the reviewer cannot identify which proposed trees are large trees (40+ feet) and therefore cannot verify the 25-foot clearance requirement for large trees from distribution lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule provides species names and quantities but lacks mature height information. The landscape plan does not indicate which trees (if any) are large trees (40+ feet mature height). Common landscape practice shows large trees with distinctive symbols or size notations.","reasoning":"To verify compliance with large tree clearance requirements, the plans must clearly indicate which proposed trees will reach a mature height of 40 feet or greater per ECM Appendix F. This information is not provided in the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance distances are dimensioned on any submitted plans. This requirement applies only when tree clearances from electric conductors are shown with dimension lines and measurements on the plans. Since no such dimensions are provided, this deficiency cannot apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"A review of the landscape plan, electrical design plan, and grading plan shows no dimension lines or distance callouts measuring clearances from trees to electric conductors or poles.","reasoning":"This is a measurement-methodology deficiency that only applies when clearances have been dimensioned on plans. Since no clearances are shown, there is no measurement reference to evaluate.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance distances are dimensioned on any submitted plans. This requirement applies only when tree clearances are dimensioned on the plans. Since no clearances are dimensioned, this deficiency cannot apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No dimension lines or distance measurements are shown on the landscape plan for tree clearances from electric facilities.","reasoning":"This is a measurement-methodology deficiency applicable only when clearances are dimensioned. Since no clearances are shown, there is no measurement reference to evaluate.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary where overhead electric line runs and trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While trees are shown on the landscape plan and the overhead electric line is shown on the same plan, their relationship is not documented with actual clearance measurements or cross-references. The landscape plan shows tree symbols (M, P) in close proximity to or overlapping the depicted OHE line, but without dimensioned lateral distances from tree trunks to the outside conductor, and without species identification, the actual clearance relationship cannot be verified. Proposed trees and overhead facilities must be shown with sufficient clarity and documentation to verify compliance with minimum clearance requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows both trees (via symbols) and overhead electric line (labeled OHE) on the same drawing. Visually, some tree symbols appear to be very close to or overlapping the depicted OHE line. However, no dimension lines, distance callouts, or cross-reference notes clarify the actual clearances.","reasoning":"To satisfy this requirement, either the plans must clearly show (without guesswork) that trees are outside restricted clearance zones, or dimension lines must document the actual lateral distances. Graphics alone are insufficient—documented measurements are needed. The apparent proximity of trees to the OHE line, combined with the lack of dimensioning, means the relationship cannot be verified as compliant.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric line on southern boundary (M and P symbols)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed near overhead electric facilities in locations that may fall within restricted clearance zones (15 feet for distribution, 10 feet from poles, etc.). However, without species identification and dimensioned clearance measurements, it cannot be determined whether these trees comply with clearance requirements or require Austin Energy approval. No written approval letters or variance documentation from Austin Energy are included in the submitted materials. If any proposed trees will be located within the restricted clearance zones, explicit written approval from Austin Energy must be provided, or the applicant must revise the planting plan to move trees outside restricted zones and re-submit with documented clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Visually, trees marked M and P near the OHE line appear to be in close proximity, potentially within restricted clearance zones. No Austin Energy approval documentation is present in the submitted materials. Species and distances cannot be verified from the plans.","reasoning":"The burden is on the applicant to either (1) demonstrate through measured distances and identified species that all trees comply with clearance requirements, or (2) provide written Austin Energy approval authorizing any non-compliant plantings. Since clearances cannot be verified and no approval is provided, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":61664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da8d4f94-c433-44b6-bc3f-ac89c89d21c6","uuid":"4b9814b0-2004-4e2c-a210-c124777a4bb5"}
