{"level":30,"time":1778276070138,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012k4fivnTQ1ssqpq9Ny6a5j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for **Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**1 FAIL Item:**\n- **EL-2.10** — Plant legend/schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities. Trees near the overhead electric line on the southern boundary are marked only with symbols (M = Mitigation Tree, P = Parking Buffer Point) but are not identified by species name on the landscape plan.\n\n**9 NOT-VERIFIABLE Items:**\n- **EL-2.1** — Trees near overhead distribution lines cannot be verified as utility-compatible without species identification\n- **EL-2.3** — Large trees cannot be verified without mature height information  \n- **EL-2.6** — Utility poles shown on electrical plan but not on landscape plan; distances not dimensioned\n- **EL-2.8** — Underground equipment shown on electrical plan but not referenced on landscape plan\n- **EL-2.9** — Root barrier compliance cannot be assessed (depends on EL-2.8); no specifications provided\n- **EL-2.11** — Large trees not differentiated; mature heights not provided\n- **EL-2.14** — Tree/overhead facility relationship not documented with clearance measurements\n- **EL-2.15** — Trees appear to be in restricted zones but compliance cannot be verified; no Austin Energy approval documentation found\n\n**5 N/A Items:**\n- **EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5** — No transmission infrastructure present\n- **EL-2.7** — No above-ground pad-mounted equipment identified\n- **EL-2.12, EL-2.13** — No clearances dimensioned on plans\n\n### Critical Issues:\n\n1. **Species Non-Identification** — The most significant deficiency is that proposed trees near overhead electric lines are not identified by species on the landscape plan, preventing verification of utility compatibility and mature height requirements.\n\n2. **Missing Measurements** — Actual lateral distances from tree trunks to conductors are not dimensioned on any plan, making it impossible to verify compliance with clearance zones (15 ft for distribution, 10 ft from poles).\n\n3. **Incomplete Plan Coordination** — The landscape plan and electrical design plan are not coordinated to show the relationship between trees and electric infrastructure with sufficient clarity for compliance verification."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7550,"cache_read_input_tokens":62335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7550},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da8d4f94-c433-44b6-bc3f-ac89c89d21c6","uuid":"3a07d0d6-afc3-4e8d-9cf3-1a979732756a"}
