 Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but does not clearly map which species are used for trees near the OHE line. Actual lateral distances from tree trunks to outside conductor are not dimensioned.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows several tree symbols (M and P) near the overhead electric line on the southern boundary, but these trees are identified only by their designation symbols, not by species names. The plant schedule lists four proposed tree species with quantities but does not indicate which species correspond to which locations or symbols on the plan.","reasoning":"The reviewer cannot verify compliance with utility-compatible tree requirements because the species identity is unknown. Without species identification, it is impossible to cross-reference against ECM Appendix F to determine utility compatibility designation. Additionally, the submitted plans do not dimension the lateral distances from tree trunks to the outside conductor, preventing verification of the 15-foot minimum clearance requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines are present or proposed on the site. Facts.md confirms no transmission easement exists on the property. The overhead electric lines shown on the plans are not identified as transmission facilities and, per grouping guidance, are assumed to be distribution lines typical of development sites. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of facts.md and easement documentation reveals only 5-foot electric easements (typical of distribution) and no transmission easement on the property. The overhead electric lines shown on the electrical and landscape plans are not labeled with voltage levels or identified as transmission infrastructure.","reasoning":"Since no transmission infrastructure is present on the site, this requirement is not applicable. The applicability gate established in the grouping guidance indicates this item applies only when transmission facilities are present.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed near the overhead electric distribution line cannot be verified as compliant with the 25-foot clearance requirement for large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) because: (1) trees near the OHE line are not identified by species on the landscape plan; (2) mature heights are not provided for any proposed trees in the plant schedule or landscape notes; (3) actual lateral distances from tree trunks to outside conductor are not dimensioned. Without this information, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule lists proposed tree species and quantities but does not provide mature height information for any species. The landscape plan shows tree symbols near the OHE line but does not identify which species these trees are or provide height designations to distinguish large trees (40+ feet) from smaller specimens.","reasoning":"Verification of compliance with the large tree clearance requirement requires identifying which proposed trees have a mature height of 40 feet or greater per ECM Appendix F, and then measuring the lateral distance from those trees to the outside conductor. Since species are not identified on the landscape plan and heights are not provided, this verification is not possible from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines are present on the site. This requirement applies only when transmission infrastructure is present. See EL-2.2 for basis of inapplicability.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transmission easement or transmission-voltage infrastructure is identified in the site plan documents or facts.md.","reasoning":"This item is conditional on the presence of transmission facilities, which do not exist on this property.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is present on the site. Facts.md confirms absence of transmission infrastructure. This requirement applies only when transmission easement boundaries are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of facts.md, grading plan, and site plan shows no transmission easement. Only 5-foot electric easements and other drainage/utility easements are identified.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditional on the presence of a transmission easement boundary. Since no such easement exists, the requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric poles on western boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility poles are indicated on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) as small circles spaced along the overhead electric line on the western boundary. However, the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not show pole locations. Without pole locations depicted on the landscape plan in relation to proposed trees, the 10-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified. Actual lateral distances from tree trunks to poles are not dimensioned on either plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical design plan shows utility pole symbols along the OHE line, but the landscape plan does not indicate pole locations. The two plans use the same scale (1\" = 20') but cannot be directly compared without an overlay analysis, which is not available.","reasoning":"Verification of compliance requires that pole locations be clearly shown on the landscape plan (or cross-referenced) in relation to proposed trees, with actual distances dimensioned. The absence of pole locations on the landscape plan means compliance cannot be verified from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical design plan shows locations labeled as 'Electrical Transformer Pad' connected to 'Underground Electric Lines.' These appear to be underground utility installations rather than above-ground pad-mounted transformers. No above-ground pad-mounted equipment with visible enclosures and access doors (as described in the code requirement) is identified on the plans. This requirement applies only when above-ground pad-mounted equipment is present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan labels show 'Electrical Transformer Pad' locations connected to 'Underground Electric Lines,' which indicates these are subsurface installations accessed via above-ground pull boxes rather than typical above-ground pad-mounted transformers.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 restrictions on trees near pad-mounted equipment typically refer to the above-ground metal enclosures visible on the surface. The submitted plans show only underground installations with surface access points (pull boxes), which are not pad-mounted equipment in the traditional sense. Therefore, this requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Locations of underground electrical equipment shown on electrical plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric lines, pull boxes, and transformer pad locations. However, the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not show these underground equipment locations in relation to proposed trees. Without underground equipment locations depicted on the landscape plan, and without dimensioned distances, compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Underground electrical infrastructure is shown on the electrical plan but is not depicted or referenced on the landscape plan. The two plans cannot be directly correlated to determine proximity of proposed trees to underground equipment.","reasoning":"The landscape plan must either show underground equipment locations (often depicted with dashed lines or access point symbols) or must provide written coordination notes addressing clearances from underground utilities. Without this information, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Locations of underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement is conditional on trees being proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment (EL-2.8). Because compliance with EL-2.8 cannot be verified (underground equipment locations not shown on landscape plan), EL-2.9 cannot be evaluated. Additionally, the landscape plan notes do not specify root barrier requirements for trees near electrical equipment. Plans must either demonstrate trees are beyond 20 feet of underground equipment, or must show root barrier details (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) on the landscape plan or details sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan and notes do not show underground equipment locations or specify root barrier requirements. No details are provided for root barriers in the reviewed landscape notes or detail sheets.","reasoning":"Without knowing which trees, if any, are within 20 feet of underground equipment, and without any root barrier specifications provided, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric line on southern boundary (marked M and P symbols)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed near the overhead electric line on the southern boundary are identified only by category symbols (M for Mitigation Tree, P for Parking Buffer Point Tree) and are NOT identified by species name on the landscape plan. While a plant schedule is provided on Sheet 35 listing species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) and quantities, the schedule does not clearly indicate which species are used for trees at the M and P locations on the landscape plan. Species identification on or adjacent to tree symbols on the landscape plan is required to allow verification of utility compatibility and clearance compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows tree symbols (M and P) near the overhead electric infrastructure but does not label these trees with species names. The plant schedule provides a list of species with quantities but does not map specific species to specific locations or symbol types on the plan.","reasoning":"Species identification is essential for verifying compliance with utility compatibility requirements (ECM Appendix F UC column) and for determining mature heights needed to assess clearance requirements. The absence of species names on the landscape plan for trees near electric facilities is a deficiency. The applicant must either add species labels to trees on the landscape plan or provide a clear key/legend that maps plant schedule species to landscape plan symbol locations.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) are not differentiated on the landscape plan. The plant schedule lists species names but does not provide mature height information for any trees. Without height designations on the landscape plan or in the plant schedule, the reviewer cannot identify which proposed trees are large trees (40+ feet) and therefore cannot verify the 25-foot clearance requirement for large trees from distribution lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule provides species names and quantities but lacks mature height information. The landscape plan does not indicate which trees (if any) are large trees (40+ feet mature height). Common landscape practice shows large trees with distinctive symbols or size notations.","reasoning":"To verify compliance with large tree clearance requirements, the plans must clearly indicate which proposed trees will reach a mature height of 40 feet or greater per ECM Appendix F. This information is not provided in the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance distances are dimensioned on any submitted plans. This requirement applies only when tree clearances from electric conductors are shown with dimension lines and measurements on the plans. Since no such dimensions are provided, this deficiency cannot apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"A review of the landscape plan, electrical design plan, and grading plan shows no dimension lines or distance callouts measuring clearances from trees to electric conductors or poles.","reasoning":"This is a measurement-methodology deficiency that only applies when clearances have been dimensioned on plans. Since no clearances are shown, there is no measurement reference to evaluate.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance distances are dimensioned on any submitted plans. This requirement applies only when tree clearances are dimensioned on the plans. Since no clearances are dimensioned, this deficiency cannot apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No dimension lines or distance measurements are shown on the landscape plan for tree clearances from electric facilities.","reasoning":"This is a measurement-methodology deficiency applicable only when clearances are dimensioned. Since no clearances are shown, there is no measurement reference to evaluate.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary where overhead electric line runs and trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While trees are shown on the landscape plan and the overhead electric line is shown on the same plan, their relationship is not documented with actual clearance measurements or cross-references. The landscape plan shows tree symbols (M, P) in close proximity to or overlapping the depicted OHE line, but without dimensioned lateral distances from tree trunks to the outside conductor, and without species identification, the actual clearance relationship cannot be verified. Proposed trees and overhead facilities must be shown with sufficient clarity and documentation to verify compliance with minimum clearance requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows both trees (via symbols) and overhead electric line (labeled OHE) on the same drawing. Visually, some tree symbols appear to be very close to or overlapping the depicted OHE line. However, no dimension lines, distance callouts, or cross-reference notes clarify the actual clearances.","reasoning":"To satisfy this requirement, either the plans must clearly show (without guesswork) that trees are outside restricted clearance zones, or dimension lines must document the actual lateral distances. Graphics alone are insufficient—documented measurements are needed. The apparent proximity of trees to the OHE line, combined with the lack of dimensioning, means the relationship cannot be verified as compliant.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric line on southern boundary (M and P symbols)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed near overhead electric facilities in locations that may fall within restricted clearance zones (15 feet for distribution, 10 feet from poles, etc.). However, without species identification and dimensioned clearance measurements, it cannot be determined whether these trees comply with clearance requirements or require Austin Energy approval. No written approval letters or variance documentation from Austin Energy are included in the submitted materials. If any proposed trees will be located within the restricted clearance zones, explicit written approval from Austin Energy must be provided, or the applicant must revise the planting plan to move trees outside restricted zones and re-submit with documented clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Visually, trees marked M and P near the OHE line appear to be in close proximity, potentially within restricted clearance zones. No Austin Energy approval documentation is present in the submitted materials. Species and distances cannot be verified from the plans.","reasoning":"The burden is on the applicant to either (1) demonstrate through measured distances and identified species that all trees comply with clearance requirements, or (2) provide written Austin Energy approval authorizing any non-compliant plantings. Since clearances cannot be verified and no approval is provided, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f20ad53f-c627-448c-8c99-ee13464a7ca9"}
