{"level":30,"time":1778277697992,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y9uPtRhWdBmZXVS2PpdQRN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided electrical plan, here is the analysis regarding the electrical routing:\n\n*   **Is the routing from the transformer pads to the electrical meters and buildings shown?**\n    Yes. The routing is explicitly detailed on the plan. It is represented by the solid blue lines interspersed with the letter \"**E**\". These blue lines can be clearly seen connecting the features labeled \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\" to various \"**Electrical Pull Box**\" locations and terminating at the \"**Electrical Meters**\" mounted on or near the individual buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8).\n\n*   **Does the routing stay completely within private property or does it cross right-of-way or easements?**\n    *   **Transformer to Meters (Internal Routing):** The specific routing asked about—from the transformer pads to the electrical meters on the buildings—appears to stay **completely within the private property bounds**. These specific distribution lines route through the internal driveways and landscaped areas to reach the buildings and do not cross back into the public Right-of-Way (ROW).\n    *   **Incoming Feed (Context):** However, it should be noted that the *incoming* primary electrical supply lines that feed the site's network do cross easements and originate in the ROW. On the western side of the property along Valley View Road, the blue electrical lines originate outside the property line, crossing the ROW and a designated \"**Sidewalk Easement**\" to reach the initial transformer pads and pull boxes on the private property."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50ce05b6-fbb2-48af-b483-350129d29c8d","uuid":"5b34c800-8e6c-49c3-9901-56079a1a0039","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided electrical plan, here is the analysis regarding the electrical routing:\n\n*   **Is the routing from the transformer pads to the electrical meters and buildings shown?**\n    Yes. The routing is explicitly detailed on the plan. It is represented by the solid blue lines interspersed with the letter \"**E**\". These blue lines can be clearly seen connecting the features labeled \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\" to various \"**Electrical Pull Box**\" locations and terminating at the \"**Electrical Meters**\" mounted on or near the individual buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8).\n\n*   **Does the routing stay completely within private property or does it cross right-of-way or easements?**\n    *   **Transformer to Meters (Internal Routing):** The specific routing asked about—from the transformer pads to the electrical meters on the buildings—appears to stay **completely within the private property bounds**. These specific distribution lines route through the internal driveways and landscaped areas to reach the buildings and do not cross back into the public Right-of-Way (ROW).\n    *   **Incoming Feed (Context):** However, it should be noted that the *incoming* primary electrical supply lines that feed the site's network do cross easements and originate in the ROW. On the western side of the property along Valley View Road, the blue electrical lines originate outside the property line, crossing the ROW and a designated \"**Sidewalk Easement**\" to reach the initial transformer pads and pull boxes on the private property."}]}
