{"level":30,"time":1778277732086,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012oEVUdDWQzzkBiYuk6hAoN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CCpNSD6FhSXT2LtpzG87Ya","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad east of Building 7"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad located east of Building 7 is only 2.9 feet from the building exterior wall. Minimum 5-foot clearance from buildings is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pad east of Building 7 shows 2.9 feet distance to nearest building exterior wall.","reasoning":"The measured distance of 2.9 feet is less than the required 5-foot minimum clearance from buildings. This constitutes non-compliance with the clearance standard.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain greater than 5-foot clearance from retaining walls shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show all five transformer pads are 150+ feet from the nearest retaining wall on the east property line.","reasoning":"All measured distances exceed the 5-foot minimum requirement, so this deficiency is not present.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations adjacent to fences"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on the site plan near transformer locations, but the plans do not identify: (1) which sides of transformer pads have operators/controls versus non-operator sides, (2) access door orientation, or (3) distance dimensions to fences. Clearance verification is not possible without access door identification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows fences (wooden privacy fences noted in landscape plan) but transformer pad access door orientations are not indicated on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The requirement differentiates between operator-side clearances (5 feet) and non-operator side clearances (3 feet), but the plans do not indicate which side has the access door or operators. Without this information, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No reduced clearances (less than 5 feet) to buildings are shown on plans. However, one pad (east of Bldg 7) has only 2.9 feet clearance which would require reduced clearance documentation with Austin Energy Design written approval, 3-hour fire rating, and other conditions. Documentation of required conditions is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformer pad east of Building 7 has 2.9-foot clearance, which is less than the standard 5-foot minimum, triggering the reduced clearance exception requirements.","reasoning":"If reduced clearance is intended, specific documentation including Austin Energy Design written approval, 3-hour fire rating verification, confirmation of non-confined space status, and adequate window/door clearances must be provided. These documents are not on the plans.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations and cross-sections showing balconies, overhangs, or structures above transformer locations are not provided. Compliance with 5-foot lateral clearance from balconies and 35-foot vertical clearance to overhanging structures cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevations are not included in the site plan submittal; only 2D plan views are shown.","reasoning":"Vertical clearances and overhead structures require elevation views or cross-sections to verify. Without building elevation drawings, it is not possible to determine if any structures, balconies, or overhangs are present above or adjacent to the transformer locations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation drawings showing window, door, and ventilating duct locations relative to transformer pads are not provided. Additionally, transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. 12-foot clearance requirement for windows/doors/ducts (when lateral separation is less than 5 feet) cannot be verified without these documents.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Architectural elevations are not included in the civil site plan submittal, and transformer specifications do not identify oil-filled vs. dry-type equipment.","reasoning":"The 12-foot clearance requirement for windows/doors applies only to oil-filled equipment and only when lateral clearance is less than 5 feet. Without building elevations showing window/door locations and without equipment specifications, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations with adjacent sidewalks"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain more than 2 feet of clearance from the back of sidewalks shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show all transformer pads are 15+ feet from the back of nearest sidewalks.","reasoning":"All measured distances exceed the 2-foot minimum requirement, so this deficiency is not present.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells serving as fire exits are shown on the fire protection plan or site plan. This requirement applies only when stairwells are present adjacent to transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of fire protection plan and site plan shows no exterior stairwells or fire exit stairs identified as adjacent to proposed transformer locations.","reasoning":"This is an applicability-gated requirement triggered only by the presence of adjacent stairwells serving as fire exits. Since none are shown on the plans, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are shown on the fire protection plan. This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment when fire escapes are present. Since no fire escapes are shown, this requirement is inapplicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the fire protection plan (Sheet 10) shows no fire escapes or external stairs labeled as fire exits on any building.","reasoning":"This is an applicability-gated requirement triggered only by the presence of fire escapes. Since none are shown on the plans, the requirement does not apply regardless of equipment type.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad access door orientations are not indicated on the electrical plan. Without identification of which side is the access door, the 10-foot clearance requirement for the hot-stick use area cannot be verified. Additionally, specific clearance dimensions to open areas or structures are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer pads as simple rectangular symbols without callouts indicating access door location or orientation.","reasoning":"The 10-foot hot-stick clearance requirement applies to the 'access door side,' but the plans do not identify which side of each transformer has the access door. Without this critical information, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The site plan does not identify any transformer locations as being within niches, enclosed areas, or notched-out building configurations. However, the plans also do not explicitly confirm that none of the transformers face confined spaces. Cross-section drawings demonstrating vertical clearance in access paths are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows all transformers in open areas between buildings or adjacent to buildings, with no explicit niche or enclosed configuration noted.","reasoning":"While the visual appearance suggests none are in confined spaces, architectural cross-sections would be needed to definitively confirm absence of any confined-space configuration. Without these drawings, compliance cannot be fully verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to fire hydrants"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two proposed fire hydrants are shown on the fire protection plan (Sheet 10), located in the fire lanes at the south and east portions of the property. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads but does not overlay fire hydrant locations for cross-reference. Distance verification between transformer pads and hydrants cannot be performed without overlaying both plans or providing specific dimension callouts.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire hydrant locations are shown on Sheet 10 and transformer pad locations are shown on Sheet 21, but these plans do not reference each other with overlaid information or distance callouts.","reasoning":"While the two features are on different sheets, distance verification requires either overlaid plan information or explicit dimension callouts. Without this coordination, the 5-foot separation requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not explicitly shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). Therefore, the proximity of trees and shrubs to transformer locations cannot be determined, and utility-compatible species verification cannot be performed for trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree and planting locations but does not reference or overlay transformer pad locations from the electrical plan.","reasoning":"Without explicit transformer location callouts on the landscape plan, it is not possible to measure distances from proposed trees/shrubs to the pads or verify species compatibility. This requires plan coordination that is not present.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations with adjacent shrubs"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not explicitly located on the landscape plan. Shrub and low vegetation clearance requirements cannot be verified without knowing the access door orientation of each transformer and proximity measurements to landscape features shown on Sheet 31.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformer pad locations are identified on the electrical plan but not cross-referenced or overlaid on the landscape plan where shrub/vegetation locations are shown.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies different clearances for access door sides (10 feet) versus other sides (5 feet). Without transformer location callouts on the landscape plan and without identified access door orientations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not explicitly shown on the landscape plan. Root barrier detail specifications and installation locations relative to trees within 20 lateral feet of transformers cannot be verified without this plan coordination.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree locations and includes references to root barrier details but transformer pad locations are not marked on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates root barriers for trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment. Without transformer locations marked on the landscape plan, proximity assessment is not possible.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters are shown on the site plan. This requirement applies only when dumpsters are present. Residential trash collection appears to be handled by enclosed trash collection areas not requiring external dumpsters.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and site notes indicates trash collection requirements but no discrete dumpster locations are shown on the plan.","reasoning":"This is an applicability-gated requirement triggered only by the presence of dumpsters. Since none are shown on the plans, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bike racks are shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) with a requirement that they be placed at least 3 feet from utilities. However, transformer pad locations are not explicitly marked on the landscape plan, so the 5-foot clearance distance between bike racks and transformer pads cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows bike rack locations and includes utility clearance notes, but transformer pad locations from the electrical plan are not overlaid or cross-referenced on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"Without transformer location callouts on the landscape plan, the distance between shown bike rack locations and transformer pads cannot be measured to verify the 5-foot requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light poles are shown on the landscape plan's photometric and site design, but transformer pad locations from the electrical plan are not explicitly marked or cross-referenced on the landscape plan. Distance verification between light poles and transformer pads cannot be performed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer locations; landscape/site plan shows light pole locations; but these plans do not reference each other with specific distance callouts.","reasoning":"Without explicit transformer location callouts on the landscape plan where lighting is shown, or without distance dimensions between the plans, compliance with the 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad located near entrance roundabout/fire lane"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"One transformer pad (located south of the western entrance roundabout/near Buildings 1-2) is only 1.6 feet from the fire lane. Minimum 15-foot clearance from fire lanes is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement shows transformer pad located near the entrance roundabout is 1.6 feet from the fire lane boundary.","reasoning":"The measured distance of 1.6 feet is significantly less than the required 15-foot minimum clearance from fire lanes. This constitutes a clear violation of the spacing requirement.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Multiple transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan, but specific distance dimensions between individual pads are not provided. The 5-foot minimum clearance between transformer pads cannot be verified without explicit distance callouts or measurements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows five transformer pad locations labeled but does not include distance dimensions between the pads.","reasoning":"While the pads can be visually observed on the plan, without explicit dimension callouts or scaled measurements between each pair of pads, compliance with the 5-foot inter-pad spacing requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not explicitly shown on the utility tap plan (Sheet 19), which depicts water line locations. Therefore, distance verification between transformer pads and water service lines cannot be performed. The 5-foot horizontal clearance requirement cannot be verified without explicit plan coordination.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 19) shows water line routing but does not overlay or reference transformer pad locations from the electrical plan (Sheet 21).","reasoning":"The two plans address overlapping infrastructure but do not cross-reference each other. Without transformer locations marked on the utility plan or explicit distance callouts between plans, clearance compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not explicitly shown on the utility tap plan (Sheet 19), which depicts wastewater line locations. Therefore, distance verification between transformer pads and wastewater service lines cannot be performed. The 5-foot horizontal clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 19) shows wastewater/sewer line routing but does not overlay or reference transformer pad locations from the electrical plan (Sheet 21).","reasoning":"Without transformer locations explicitly marked on the utility plan or specific distance callouts coordinating the plans, the 5-foot separation requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not explicitly shown on the storm sewer plan (Sheet 12), which depicts storm drain line locations. The 5-foot horizontal clearance requirement between transformer pads and storm drain lines cannot be verified without explicit plan coordination showing transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Storm sewer plan (Sheet 12) shows drainage routing but transformer pad locations from the electrical plan are not overlaid or cross-referenced.","reasoning":"Without transformer locations explicitly marked on the drainage/storm sewer plan, distance verification between the pads and storm drain lines cannot be performed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service infrastructure is shown on the utility plans or project documentation. This requirement applies only when gas service is present. The project appears to be all-electric.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of utility tap plan, electrical plan, and project notes shows no gas line infrastructure proposed or mentioned.","reasoning":"This is an applicability-gated requirement triggered only by the presence of gas service. Since no gas infrastructure is shown on the plans, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not explicitly shown on the utility plan (Sheet 19) where underground utilities (electric, telecom, fuel, steam) would be referenced. The 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from other underground utilities cannot be verified without plan coordination showing transformer locations relative to all utility routing.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan shows various underground utilities but transformer pad locations are not marked or overlaid on the utility plan.","reasoning":"The 12-inch clearance requirement applies to separation from other underground utilities. Without transformer location callouts on the utility plan, this clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations and underground routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not shown on the utility plan in coordination with other utilities. Additionally, building cross-sections or elevation views are not provided. Therefore, it cannot be verified that transformer pads or AE underground facilities are not located over/under other utility lines or that customer buildings/structures are not installed over AE underground facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans do not show explicit coordination between transformer pad locations (Sheet 21) and all underground utility routing (Sheet 19) with vertical profile information.","reasoning":"This requirement requires three-dimensional analysis showing vertical relationships between utilities and structures. Without cross-section drawings and explicit plan coordination, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are not explicitly shown or labeled on the electrical site plan (Sheet 21). The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution line conductors cannot be verified without identification of overhead line locations on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan does not show overhead distribution line locations, poles, or conductor routing relative to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Without overhead line infrastructure depicted on the site plan, the 7.5-foot vertical clearance requirement cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are not shown on the electrical site plan. Without identification and location of overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors, the 15-foot radius clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan does not depict overhead distribution line infrastructure or conductor locations.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radius clearance from overhead conductors is measured from the conductors themselves. Without conductor locations shown on the plan, this clearance cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The site plan does not identify any transformer locations as niche installations (within building footprints but accessible from outside). Plans also do not include cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances through access paths with overhead structures. If any transformer is intended as a niche installation, the 35-foot vertical clearance requirement cannot be verified without cross-section drawings.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows all transformers in exterior open areas (not within building footprints), but cross-section drawings are not provided to verify vertical clearances in any configuration.","reasoning":"While the visual layout suggests no niche configurations are present, cross-sections would be needed to definitively verify this and to confirm vertical clearances in all locations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installations (transformers within building footprints but accessible from outside) are proposed on this project. This requirement applies only when niche service is specified. The site plan shows all transformers in exterior locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows all transformer pads labeled as exterior features in open areas between buildings, with no callouts indicating niche or enclosed configurations.","reasoning":"This is an applicability-gated requirement triggered only by niche service proposals. Since no niche installations are shown, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances between transformer pad locations and any overhead structures, parking garage decks, or enclosed areas above the transformer locations are not provided. Vertical clearance compliance cannot be verified without these cross-section views.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan set includes 2D plan views but does not include cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances relative to transformers and overhead features.","reasoning":"Vertical clearance verification requires cross-section or elevation views. Without these drawings, compliance with overhead structure clearance requirements cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not explicitly shown on the grading plan (Sheet 11). Additionally, transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan. Therefore, the drainage flow direction around transformer pads cannot be verified. If oil-filled transformers are proposed, drainage must flow away from buildings, which cannot be confirmed without plan coordination.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan shows overall site drainage but transformer pad locations are not marked, and electrical plan does not specify equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry).","reasoning":"The requirement for liquid flow away from buildings applies only to oil-filled equipment. Without transformer location callouts on the grading plan and without equipment type specification, drainage direction verification is not possible.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located within private property boundaries. None are shown straddling property lines or located in public right-of-way areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of electrical site plan shows all five transformer pads clearly within the heavy property boundary lines and not extending into the 60-foot right-of-way marked along Valley View Road.","reasoning":"The measured and visual assessment confirms all transformer pads are 100% on private property with adequate separation from property lines.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"One transformer pad (west of Building 8) is located within a Vault Easement as shown on the electrical plan. The grouping guidance specifies that transformers cannot be placed in electrical easements under overhead lines without Austin Energy Design written approval. The status of this vault easement relative to overhead lines and whether AE Design approval has been obtained is not documented on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis shows the transformer pad west of Building 8 is enclosed within a dashed rectangular boundary labeled 'Vault Easement' on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"While the placement may be intentional, the plans do not provide documentation of Austin Energy Design written approval for locating transformer equipment in this easement area, which is required by the regulatory framework.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown around any of the transformer pads. The electrical plan shows five transformer pads but does not depict bounded easement areas with dimensions around them. Transformer easements are required for Austin Energy accessibility and maintenance. The width of any required easements and their boundaries are not indicated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of electrical plan shows transformer pads labeled but no rectangular easement boundaries with width dimensions drawn around them, except for one 'Vault Easement' near Building 8.","reasoning":"The UCM requirements specify that transformer easements are necessary for accessibility. The absence of easement demarcations around all pads constitutes non-compliance with the documentation requirement.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformers to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformers to meters is shown on the electrical plan, but specific property ownership/boundary information for the entire routing path is not provided. Individual building plots within the development may have different ownership or legal descriptions. 100% private property routing cannot be definitively verified without explicit confirmation that all routing stays within private property owned by or under easement to the customer.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows routing lines from transformer pads to electrical meters but does not include property line demarcations or ownership callouts for each segment of the routing path.","reasoning":"While the visual appearance suggests routing is within the development property, formal verification of 100% private property routing would require property boundary callouts for each segment or explicit documentation of easement status.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions (width and length) are not shown on the electrical site plan. Additionally, no references to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided. Service type (single-phase or three-phase) is not specified. Without pad dimensions matching AE Design specifications for the specified service type, compliance with equipment sizing standards cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of electrical plan shows transformer pads as unlabeled rectangular symbols without dimension callouts or references to standard details.","reasoning":"The regulatory requirement mandates that pad dimensions match AE Design-approved specifications for the service type. The complete absence of dimensions and detail references constitutes a failure to demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Four transformer pad locations within 4 feet of parking areas or drive aisles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Four of the five transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle drive aisles. No bollards (4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts) are shown on the electrical plan protecting these pads from vehicle impact. AE Design equipment pad details showing bollard specifications and spacing are not referenced.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis identifies four transformer pads positioned immediately adjacent to drive aisles/parking curbs and confirms that no bollard symbols, details, or references are present on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The UCM standard requires bollards for pads within 4 feet of vehicle circulation. The complete absence of bollard protection on pads that clearly meet the proximity threshold constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed structures and overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution facility locations are not identified on the electrical site plan. Therefore, it cannot be verified that customer-proposed facilities (buildings, parking, light poles, signs, tanks, antennas) are not installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution lines. Plan coordination showing overhead line locations is required but not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan does not depict overhead distribution line routing or pole locations relative to proposed buildings and site structures.","reasoning":"Without overhead line infrastructure shown on the plan, compliance with the requirement that no structures be placed under overhead distribution facilities cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2170,"cache_read_input_tokens":73502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2170},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cfb3d30-a54c-43db-bd21-983850252c35","uuid":"d7976abc-33f7-4be7-bec5-dac36df0ab95"}
