{"level":30,"time":1778277746093,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017TxbpxgZbt8upPd5WDXwom","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed a comprehensive evaluation of all 39 checklist items for the Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements grouping. Here's a summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**CRITICAL FAILURES (7):**\n- **EL-13.1**: Transformer pad east of Building 7 is only 2.9 feet from building (requires 5 feet minimum)\n- **EL-13.4**: Same pad would require Austin Energy Design written approval for reduced clearance with supporting conditions\n- **EL-13.19**: Transformer pad near entrance roundabout is only 1.6 feet from fire lane (requires 15 feet)\n- **EL-13.34**: Transformer pad west of Building 8 is located in Vault Easement without documented AE Design approval\n- **EL-13.35**: No transformer easements depicted around any of the five pads\n- **EL-13.37**: Transformer pad dimensions and Austin Energy Design detail references are completely absent\n- **EL-13.38**: Four transformer pads within 4 feet of parking/drive aisles lack required bollard protection\n\n**PASSES (3):**\n- EL-13.2: All pads exceed 5-foot clearance from retaining walls\n- EL-13.7: All pads exceed 2-foot clearance from back of sidewalks  \n- EL-13.33: All pads located 100% on private property\n\n**NOT APPLICABLE (5):**\n- EL-13.8, EL-13.9: No fire escapes shown on plans\n- EL-13.16: No dumpsters on site\n- EL-13.24: No gas service (all-electric project)\n- EL-13.30: No niche service configurations proposed\n\n**NOT VERIFIABLE (23 items):**\nThe majority of not-verifiable findings result from two root causes:\n1. **Plan coordination gaps**: Transformer locations are not overlaid or cross-referenced on landscape, utility, drainage, and fire protection plans, making clearance distances unverifiable\n2. **Missing documentation**: No building elevations, cross-sections, equipment specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type, single vs. three-phase), access door orientations, or AE Design approval documents\n\nThe structured output above contains detailed analysis for each of the 39 checklist items with specific evidence and reasoning for every determination."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10866,"cache_read_input_tokens":75672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10866},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cfb3d30-a54c-43db-bd21-983850252c35","uuid":"0a669b0d-7472-43a1-ab68-ca844d45056b"}
