eAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain greater than 5-foot clearance from retaining walls shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show all five transformer pads are 150+ feet from the nearest retaining wall on the east property line.","reasoning":"All measured distances exceed the 5-foot minimum requirement, so this deficiency is not present.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations adjacent to fences"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on the site plan near transformer locations, but the plans do not identify: (1) which sides of transformer pads have operators/controls versus non-operator sides, (2) access door orientation, or (3) distance dimensions to fences. Clearance verification is not possible without access door identification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows fences (wooden privacy fences noted in landscape plan) but transformer pad access door orientations are not indicated on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The requirement differentiates between operator-side clearances (5 feet) and non-operator side clearances (3 feet), but the plans do not indicate which side has the access door or operators. Without this information, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No reduced clearances (less than 5 feet) to buildings are shown on plans. However, one pad (east of Bldg 7) has only 2.9 feet clearance which would require reduced clearance documentation with Austin Energy Design written approval, 3-hour fire rating, and other conditions. Documentation of required conditions is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformer pad east of Building 7 has 2.9-foot clearance, which is less than the standard 5-foot minimum, triggering the reduced clearance exception requirements.","reasoning":"If reduced clearance is intended, specific documentation including Austin Energy Design written approval, 3-hour fire rating verification, confirmation of non-confined space status, and adequate window/door clearances must be provided. These documents are not on the plans.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations and cross-sections showing balconies, overhangs, or structures above transformer locations are not provided. Compliance with 5-foot lateral clearance from balconies and 35-foot vertical clearance to overhanging structures cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevations are not included in the site plan submittal; only 2D plan views are shown.","reasoning":"Vertical clearances and overhead structures require elevation views or cross-sections to verify. Without building elevation drawings, it is not possible to determine if any structures, balconies, or overhangs are present above or adjacent to the transformer locations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation drawings showing window, door, and ventilating duct locations relative to transformer pads are not provided. Additionally, transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. 12-foot clearance requirement for windows/doors/ducts (when lateral separation is less than 5 feet) cannot be verified without these documents.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Architectural elevations are not included in the civil site plan submittal, and transformer specifications do not identify oil-filled vs. dry-type equipment.","reasoning":"The 12-foot clearance requirement for windows/doors applies only to oil-filled equipment and only when lateral clearance is less than 5 feet. Without building elevations showing window/door locations and without equipment specifications, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations with adjacent sidewalks"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain more than 2 feet of clearance from the back of sidewalks shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show all transformer pads are 15+ feet from the back of nearest sidewalks.","reasoning":"All measured distances exceed the 2-foot minimum requirement, so this deficiency is not present.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells serving as fire exits are shown on the fire protection plan or site plan. This requirement applies only when stairwells are present adjacent to transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of fire protection plan and site plan shows no exterior stairwells or fire exit stairs identified as adjacent to proposed transformer locations.","reasoning":"This is an applicability-gated requirement triggered only by the presence of adjacent stairwells serving as fire exits. Since none are shown on the plans, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are shown on the fire protection plan. This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment when fire escapes are present. Since no fire escapes are shown, this requirement is inapplicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the fire protection plan (Sheet 10) shows no fire escapes or external stairs labeled as fire exits on any building.","reasoning":"This is an applicability-gated requirement triggered only by the presence of fire escapes. Since none are shown on the plans, the requirement does not apply regardless of equipment type.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad access door orientations are not indicated on the electrical plan. Without identification of which side is the access door, the 10-foot clearance requirement for the hot-stick use area cannot be verified. Additionally, specific clearance dimensions to open areas or structures are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer pads as simple rectangular symbols without callouts indicating access door location or orientation.","reasoning":"The 10-foot hot-stick clearance requirement applies to the 'access door side,' but the plans do not identify which side of each transformer has the access door. Without this critical information, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The site plan does not identify any transformer locations as being within niches, enclosed areas, or notched-out building configurations. However, the plans also do not explicitly confirm that none of the transformers face confined spaces. Cross-section drawings demonstrating vertical clearance in access paths are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows all transformers in open areas between buildings or adjacent to buildings, with no explicit niche or enclosed configuration noted.","reasoning":"While the visual appearance suggests none are in confined spaces, architectural cross-sections would be needed to definitively confirm absence of any confined-space configuration. Without these drawings, compliance cannot be fully verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to fire hydrants"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two proposed fire hydrants are shown on the fire protection plan (Sheet 10), located in the fire lanes at the south and east portions o