{"level":30,"time":1778277941775,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PQq13D8j3iZUgCG97fxWFC","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 2 — Plat\n     2→\n     3→Subdivision plat map showing legal boundaries, easements, and signatures.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet displays the historical recorded plat for the Mecey Subdivision (Travis County, 1975), which serves as the base property boundary framework for the current Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to establish the legal boundary dimensions, right-of-way dedications, existing easements, and historical surveyor certifications for Lots 1 and 2 between Valley View Road and Clawson Road.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Property Recording:** Book 73, Page 76 (Filed December 11, 1975, at 2:10 PM)\n    11→*   **Original Survey Date:** August 20, 1975\n    12→*   **Base Property Reference:** Lot A, Trico Subdivision (Book 69, Page 14) / Volume 4916, Page 2385\n    13→*   **Scale:** 1\" = 100 Feet\n    14→*   **Curve Data:** Delta (Δ) = 31°25', Tangent (T) = 20.84', Radius (R) = 74.10', Long Chord (L.C.) = 39.12', Arc = 40.63'\n    15→*   **Surveyor:** Forrest B. Scott, Reg. Public Surveyor #399 (Austin, Texas)\n    16→*   **Current Project Address:** 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 1: drawing — Mecey Subdivision Plat**\n    21→    The main drawing area containing the historical plat map, legal descriptions, owner's dedication, surveyor's certification, and approval signatures. \n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of Lot 1 and Lot 2, their orientation between Valley View Road and Clawson Road, and the location of drainage easements. \n    23→    *READ the block content for* precise boundary bearings/dimensions, curve data details, historical recording information, and standard legal declarations.\n    24→\n    25→*   **Blocks 7, 18: text_block — Project Title**\n    26→    Identifies the current project name, site address, and the specific title of this sheet.\n    27→    *READ the block content for* the project address (3759 Valley View Road) and sheet title (\"Plat\").\n    28→\n    29→*   **Blocks 9, 11: table/text_block — Project Details**\n    30→    Contains the project tracking details.\n    31→    *READ the block content for* the Project No. (RJ3 70496) and the initials for Design (CS, JR), CAD (JW, CS), and Review (JKR).\n    32→\n    33→*   **Blocks 2, 13: text_block — Sheet Indexing**\n    34→    *READ the block content for* the sheet number (Sheet 2 of 39) and tracking number (SP-2025-0126C).\n    35→\n    36→*   **Blocks 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    37→    Contains standard engineering firm contact info (Bleyl Engineering), office locations, the empty revision schedule, original layout size (24x36), and CAD file path plots. These can generally be skipped during technical review unless confirming the engineer of record's contact information.\n    38→\n    39→---\n    40→\n    41→- `block-1.md` — drawing: The main content area showing the plat for the Mecey Subdivision. This includes the legal descriptio\n    42→\n    43→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    44→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50ce05b6-fbb2-48af-b483-350129d29c8d","uuid":"77343ddd-85ec-43b0-826e-0ea8c34b6ff6","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-02/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 2 — Plat\n\nSubdivision plat map showing legal boundaries, easements, and signatures.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet displays the historical recorded plat for the Mecey Subdivision (Travis County, 1975), which serves as the base property boundary framework for the current Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to establish the legal boundary dimensions, right-of-way dedications, existing easements, and historical surveyor certifications for Lots 1 and 2 between Valley View Road and Clawson Road.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Property Recording:** Book 73, Page 76 (Filed December 11, 1975, at 2:10 PM)\n*   **Original Survey Date:** August 20, 1975\n*   **Base Property Reference:** Lot A, Trico Subdivision (Book 69, Page 14) / Volume 4916, Page 2385\n*   **Scale:** 1\" = 100 Feet\n*   **Curve Data:** Delta (Δ) = 31°25', Tangent (T) = 20.84', Radius (R) = 74.10', Long Chord (L.C.) = 39.12', Arc = 40.63'\n*   **Surveyor:** Forrest B. Scott, Reg. Public Surveyor #399 (Austin, Texas)\n*   **Current Project Address:** 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Mecey Subdivision Plat**\n    The main drawing area containing the historical plat map, legal descriptions, owner's dedication, surveyor's certification, and approval signatures. \n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of Lot 1 and Lot 2, their orientation between Valley View Road and Clawson Road, and the location of drainage easements. \n    *READ the block content for* precise boundary bearings/dimensions, curve data details, historical recording information, and standard legal declarations.\n\n*   **Blocks 7, 18: text_block — Project Title**\n    Identifies the current project name, site address, and the specific title of this sheet.\n    *READ the block content for* the project address (3759 Valley View Road) and sheet title (\"Plat\").\n\n*   **Blocks 9, 11: table/text_block — Project Details**\n    Contains the project tracking details.\n    *READ the block content for* the Project No. (RJ3 70496) and the initials for Design (CS, JR), CAD (JW, CS), and Review (JKR).\n\n*   **Blocks 2, 13: text_block — Sheet Indexing**\n    *READ the block content for* the sheet number (Sheet 2 of 39) and tracking number (SP-2025-0126C).\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains standard engineering firm contact info (Bleyl Engineering), office locations, the empty revision schedule, original layout size (24x36), and CAD file path plots. These can generally be skipped during technical review unless confirming the engineer of record's contact information.\n\n---\n\n- `block-1.md` — drawing: The main content area showing the plat for the Mecey Subdivision. This includes the legal descriptio\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778277961121,"pid":56878,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AixYCVWk45MrdFiiT3fvw2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough information to compile my findings. Let me organize all the checklist items and their statuses:\n\n## PASS Items (no deficiency found):\n1. EL-13.1 - Min 5-ft clearance from buildings: PASS (all > 5 ft, measured 11.5-72.7 ft)\n2. EL-13.2 - Min 5-ft clearance from retaining walls: PASS (no adjacent retaining walls, ~20-30 ft away)\n3. EL-13.10 - 10-ft hot-stick clearance: PASS (all measurements 19.1-72.7 ft)\n4. EL-13.21 - Min 5-ft clearance from water lines: PASS (10.8-102.5 ft)\n5. EL-13.22 - Min 5-ft clearance from wastewater lines: PASS (15.9-136.5 ft)\n6. EL-13.23 - Min 5-ft clearance from storm drain lines: PASS (16.2-76.7 ft)\n7. EL-13.27 - Min 7.5-ft horizontal clearance from overhead: PASS (18.3-73.4 ft)\n8. EL-13.28 - 15-ft radius clearance from overhead: PASS (40+ ft from perimeter overhead lines)\n9. EL-13.33 - Located 100% on private property: PASS (all pads within lot boundaries)\n10. EL-13.36 - Electrical routing on private property: PASS (transformer to meter routing on private property)\n\n## N/A Items (not applicable):\n1. EL-13.3 - Fence clearances: N/A (no fences shown adjacent to pads)\n2. EL-13.4 - Reduced 3-ft clearances: N/A (no sub-5-ft clearances shown; no reduced clearance approval requested)\n\n\n3. EL-13.5 - Balconies/overhangs: N/A (building elevations don't indicate any overhangs above or near the pads)\n4. EL-13.6 - Window/door 12-ft clearance: N/A (no low windows or doors with insufficient lateral separation)\n5. EL-13.7 - Sidewalk clearance: N/A (transformer pads positioned 2+ feet from sidewalks)\n6. EL-13.8 - Stairwell clearance: N/A (no stairwells adjacent to pads)\n7. EL-13.9 - Fire escape clearance: N/A (no fire escapes identified near the pads)\n8. EL-13.11 - 15-ft confined space clearance: N/A (no niche or vault configurations present)\n9. EL-13.12 - Fire hydrant clearance: N/A (fire hydrant location not shown on electrical plan; would require cross-reference with fire protection plan)\n10. EL-13.13 - Trees within 10 ft utility-compatible: CANNOT CLEARLY VERIFY (landscape plan doesn't clearly indicate tree locations relative to transformer pads)\n11. EL-13.15 - Root barriers for trees within 20 ft: N/A (no trees identified within 20-ft radius)\n12. EL-13.16 - Dumpster clearance: N/A (no dumpsters located near pads)\n13. EL-13.17 - Bike rack clearance: N/A (no bike racks near pads)\n14. EL-13.18 - Light pole clearance: N/A (no light poles near pads)\n15. EL-13.19 - Fire lane clearance (15 ft): N/A (transformer pads not cross-referenced on fire protection plan)\n16. EL-13.20 - Multiple transformer pad separation: N/A (only one or two pads per location; cannot determine if multiple pads coexist at same site)\n17. EL-13.24 - Gas line clearance: N/A (no gas service indicated on plan)\n18. EL-13.25 - 12-inch clearance from other utilities: APPEARS TO PASS but NOT FULLY DOCUMENTED (visual spacing exceeds 12 inches but not explicitly dimensioned)\n19. EL-13.26 - No structures over/under AE facilities: CANNOT VERIFY (requires confirmation from AE Design team)\n20. EL-13.29 - Niche 35-ft vertical clearance: N/A (niche service not shown on plans)\n21. EL-13.30 - Niche fire rating/ventilation: N/A (no niche service proposed)\n22. EL-13.31 - Cross-sections showing vertical clearances: N/A or NOT PROVIDED (available cross-sections address drainage only, not pad clearances)\n23. EL-13.32 - Drainage away from oil-filled equipment: CANNOT VERIFY (transformer type not specified; drainage direction appears away from structures but not marked at pad level)\n24. EL-13.34 - Easement avoidance: CANNOT VERIFY (transformer placement relative to easement boundaries unclear; potential greenbelt and drainage easements need evaluation)\n25. EL-13.35 - Transformer easements shown: NOT PROVIDED (no transformer easements identified on plat or electrical plan)\n26. EL-13.39 - Structures over overhead facilities: N/A (no structures proposed over overhead lines)\n\n## FAIL Items (deficiency found):\n1. EL-13.37 - Pad dimensions match A\n\n/E Design details: FAIL (dimensions, specifications, service type, and AE Design detail references absent)\n2. EL-13.38 - Bollards for parking proximity: FAIL (pads located within 4 ft of vehicle circulation areas without bollard protection)\n3. EL-13.14 - Shrub clearances: FAIL (vegetation planted immediately adjacent to pads with minimal clearance; code requires 5-10 ft separation)\n\n## NOT VERIFIABLE Items (evidence absent or ambiguous):\n1. EL-13.13 - Trees within 10 ft utility-compatible: NOT VERIFIABLE (tree species and distances from transformer pads not clearly documented on landscape plan)\n2. EL-13.25 - 12-inch clearance from other underground utilities: NOT VERIFIABLE (spacing appears sufficient visually but lacks explicit dimensioning)\n3. EL-13.26 - No structures over/under AE facilities: NOT VERIFIABLE (requires AE Design coordination to confirm)\n4. EL-13.32 - Drainage away from oil-filled equipment: NOT VERIFIABLE (transformer type not specified; drainage pattern unclear)\n5. EL-13.34 - Easements conflict: NOT VERIFIABLE (transformer pad locations not clearly overlaid with easement boundaries from plat)\n\nReconsidering the evaluation criteria: items missing required information should be marked FAIL rather than NOT VERIFIABLE. For EL-13.37, the absence of dimensions is a deficiency. For EL-13.13, trees aren't shown in relation to transformer pads on the same sheet, making it impossible to verify the 10 ft requirement.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1414,"cache_read_input_tokens":87035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1414},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50ce05b6-fbb2-48af-b483-350129d29c8d","uuid":"08fabc87-54dd-4a2d-a464-06bedf52e31a"}
