 of the 5-foot clearance requirement, making this item inapplicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fences or gates are shown adjacent to transformer pads on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of electrical site plan found no fences, gates, or barriers labeled or depicted near any of the five transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Since no adjacent fences exist, the clearance requirement from fences does not apply to this project.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No reduced clearances (less than 5 feet to buildings) are shown on plans. No AE Design written approval request for reduced clearances is documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"All measured clearances from transformer pads to buildings exceed 5 feet (minimum 11.5 feet), and no architectural notes or approvals indicate reduced clearance configurations.","reasoning":"Since all clearances meet or exceed the standard 5-foot requirement, the exception for reduced clearances (requiring AE Design approval) does not apply.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevations showing balconies or overhangs are provided in the electrical plan. The 2D site plan shows no architectural projections or overhang indicators above transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical site plan (Sheet 21) is a 2D overhead drawing showing only building footprints with solid outline lines. No dashed lines, architectural projections, balconies, or overhang elements are depicted above or adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Building elevations are not included in the electrical plan document, preventing definitive assessment. However, the site plan shows no indication of overhangs. This item would require architectural elevation sheets for complete verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No windows, doors, or ventilating ducts with less than 5 feet lateral separation are identified adjacent to transformer pads on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical site plan shows transformer pads positioned at minimum 11.5 feet from buildings. No specific windows, doors, or HVAC ducts are labeled on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The visual site plan positioning and measured clearances suggest adequate separation. Detailed architectural elevations would be needed to identify low windows/doors requiring 12-foot clearance for oil-filled equipment, but none are indicated on available plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are positioned at least 2 feet from back of sidewalks based on site layout shown on electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows transformer pads positioned behind driveway curbs, maintaining separation from sidewalk edges. Scale measurement confirms adequate spacing.","reasoning":"Visual positioning on plan indicates transformer pads are set back from sidewalk areas consistent with the 2-foot minimum requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells or stairs serving as fire exits are identified adjacent to transformer pads on the electrical site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of electrical plan found no exterior stairwells, stairs serving as fire exits, or emergency exit structures labeled near any transformer pad location.","reasoning":"The absence of identified stairwell infrastructure adjacent to transformer pads indicates this requirement does not apply to the project.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or exterior stairs serving as fire escapes are shown on the electrical plan adjacent to transformer pads. Additionally, transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on plans, preventing applicability determination.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of electrical site plan found no fire escapes, exterior stairwells, or fire exit infrastructure labeled near any transformer pad location.","reasoning":"Since no fire escapes are present and transformer equipment type is not specified as oil-filled, this requirement does not apply to the project.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pad hot-stick use areas maintain minimum 10-foot clearance to open areas or adjacent buildings in all directions. Measured distances range from 11.5 to 72.7 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pads shows clearances in all directions exceed 10 feet minimum: west of Bldg 1 (21.3 ft to building), west of Bldg 2 (50.5 ft), west of Bldg 8 (53 ft), east of Bldg 5 (72.7 ft), east of Bldg 4/7 (19.1 ft). Open areas are also confirmed adjacent with no obstructions within 10 feet.","reasoning":"All measured clearances from transformer pad access door sides exceed the 10-foot minimum required clearance to buildings and open areas.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche, vault, or enclosed area configurations are indicated on the site plans. All transformer pad locations are in open areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows all transformer pads positioned in outdoor areas adjacent to driveways and landscaping, with no indication of niche installations or enclosed areas.","reasoning":"Since no confined space or niche configurations are proposed, the 15-foot confined space clearance requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire hydrant locations are not shown on the electrical plan where transformer pads are detailed. The fire protection plan does show 1 private hydrant on site but transformer pad locations are not depicted on that sheet for cross-reference measurement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) shows one private hydrant location but does not show transformer pads, preventing direct distance measurement. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads but not hydrant locations.","reasoning":"Without both transformer pads and fire hydrants shown on the same sheet, specific distance verification cannot be completed from the available documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["areas within 10 feet of transformer pads and 15 feet of overhead distribution"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not show transformer pad locations, making it impossible to determine which trees (if any) are within 10 lateral feet of pads or to verify their species designation per ECM Appendix F utility-compatible list.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows planting locations and symbols but does not include electrical transformer pad callouts or labels, preventing visual overlay of tree locations relative to transformer positions.","reasoning":"Without transformer pads clearly marked on the landscape plan, the specific distances from trees to pad locations cannot be verified from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southwest corner transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Shrubs and low-lying vegetation are shown immediately adjacent to transformer pads in the southwest corner of the site with 0 to 0.3 feet clearance. Minimum 10 feet clearance is required from access door side; 5 feet minimum from other sides.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement on landscape plan identified shrubs/low vegetation immediately adjacent to two transformer pad locations in southwest corner: northern pad at 0 feet, southern pad at 0.3 feet separation.","reasoning":"The measured clearances of 0 to 0.3 feet are substantially less than the required minimum 5-10 feet (depending on access door orientation), indicating non-compliance with vegetation clearance requirements.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No trees are identified within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment (transformer pads) on the landscape plan. Root barrier requirement therefore does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan review shows proposed planting locations but does not show trees within 20-foot radius of transformer pads where root barrier details would be required.","reasoning":"Since no trees are proposed within the 20-foot triggering distance, root barrier specifications are not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters or trash enclosures are shown near transformer pad locations on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows no dumpster or trash collection facilities positioned adjacent to any transformer pad location.","reasoning":"Since no dumpsters are present near transformer pads, this clearance requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No bike racks are positioned adjacent to transformer pads on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows bike racks located within garages and away from transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Since no bike racks are positioned near transformer pads, this clearance requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No light poles are positioned adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows exterior lighting fixtures and site lighting plan provided, with no light poles depicted immediately adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Since no light poles are positioned near transformer pads, this clearance requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not shown on the fire protection plan (Sheet 10) where fire lanes are designated. Cross-sheet verification cannot be completed, but fire lanes are shown on the fire protection plan as linear marked areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire protection plan shows designated fire lanes with red curb striping and signage requirements, but transformer pads are not depicted on this sheet for distance measurement.","reasoning":"Without both features shown on the same sheet, specific distance verification cannot be completed from available documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Only one transformer pad is shown at each location. No multiple transformer pad configurations are indicated on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan identifies individual transformer pads at each location (west of Bldg 1, 2, 8; east of Bldg 4, 7) with no notation of additional pads at the same location.","reasoning":"Since only single transformer pads are proposed at each location, separation requirements between multiple pads do not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from water lines. Measured distances range from 10.8 to 102.5 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pads to water lines (marked 'W') shows: near Bldg 1 (10.8 ft), near Bldg 2 (55.3 ft), near Bldg 8 (21 ft), near Bldg 5 (102.5 ft), near Bldg 7 (44.4 ft).","reasoning":"All measured clearances exceed the 5-foot minimum required horizontal separation from water utility lines.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from wastewater lines. Measured distances range from 15.9 to 136.5 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pads to wastewater lines (marked 'WW') shows: near Bldg 1 (51.2 ft), near Bldg 2 (35.8 ft), near Bldg 8 (136.5 ft), east of Bldg 4 (15.9 ft), east of Bldg 7 (30.5 ft).","reasoning":"All measured clearances exceed the 5-foot minimum required horizontal separation from wastewater utility lines.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from storm drain lines. Measured distances range from 16.2 to 76.7 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pads to storm drain lines (marked 'SD') shows: near Bldg 1 (76.7 ft), near Bldg 2 (51.1 ft), near Bldg 8 (19.2 ft), east of Bldg 4 (33.6 ft), east of Bldg 7 (16.2 ft).","reasoning":"All measured clearances exceed the 5-foot minimum required horizontal separation from storm drain utility lines.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas utility service is shown on the utility plans. Gas line clearance requirement does not apply to this project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of utility plan identified water, wastewater, and storm drain utilities but no gas utility lines are labeled or depicted near transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Since no gas service is proposed for the site, the gas line clearance requirement (24-36 inches depending on pressure) is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground utility lines are shown on plans and appear to maintain adequate spacing, but specific 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearances from transformer pads are not dimensionally labeled or documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan and electrical plan show underground utility locations (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric) with visual spacing that appears to exceed 12-inch minimum. However, no explicit dimension callouts or spacing table is provided for underground utility separations at transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Visual inspection suggests adequate spacing, but without explicit dimensional documentation or clearance verification notes, the 12-inch minimum clearance requirement cannot be definitively verified from submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations and underground electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Whether customer facilities (buildings, parking structures) are installed over or under Austin Energy underground electric facilities cannot be verified from submitted site plans without Austin Energy Design consultation documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows transformer pads, buildings, and underground electric lines but does not explicitly document AE Design approval for any structures positioned over underground electric conduits or vice versa.","reasoning":"This requirement requires coordination with and documentation from Austin Energy Design, which is not included in the submitted site plan package.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution line conductors. Measured distances to overhead lines range from 18.3 to 73.4 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pads to overhead electric lines (marked 'OHE') shows: Bldg 1 to north OHE (18.3 ft), Bldg 1 to west OHE (73.4 ft), Bldg 2 to west OHE (68.2 ft), Bldg 8 to west OHE (63.8 ft), Bldg 8 to south OHE (41.7 ft), Bldg 7 to south OHE (57.2 ft).","reasoning":"All measured clearances significantly exceed the 7.5-foot minimum required horizontal clearance from overhead distribution conductors.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors. Overhead lines are restricted to far outer perimeters of site; all transformer pads are interior with 40+ feet clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review confirmed overhead electric lines (OHE) are located along western, southern, and eastern property boundaries. All transformer pads are positioned in interior site areas adjacent to buildings and driveways, with visual scale measurement confirming 40+ feet minimum separation.","reasoning":"The significant separation (40+ feet) between perimeter overhead conductors and interior transformer pad locations substantially exceeds the 15-foot radius minimum requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installation is indicated on the site plans. All transformer pads are in standard outdoor ground-level configuration.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows transformer pads positioned in open outdoor areas adjacent to driveways and buildings with no notation of enclosed, notched-out, or niche-type configurations.","reasoning":"Since niche service (specialized enclosed installation within building footprint) is not proposed, the 35-foot vertical clearance requirement for niches does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installation is proposed. Fire wall ratings and ventilation specifications for niche service therefore do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan and architectural documents show no indication of niche service configuration or enclosed transformer installations within building footprints.","reasoning":"Since niche service is not proposed, architectural fire rating and ventilation requirements for niche installations do not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations with overhead structures or parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":17}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings provided are limited to drainage/conveyance profiles (Sheet 17). No cross-sections specifically demonstrating vertical clearances from transformer pad access paths to overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 17 contains six cross-sections titled 'Conveyance Cross Sections' depicting drainage channel profiles for 25-year and 100-year storm events, with no transformer pad access path clearance information.","reasoning":"While overhead structures exist at the site (buildings, parking areas), no specific cross-section drawings document the vertical clearance from transformer pad locations through access paths to overhead structures, preventing verification of this requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on electrical plan, so applicability of drainage requirement cannot be determined. Grading plan shows surface drainage slopes away from buildings generally, but specific drainage direction at transformer pad locations is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan provides no equipment specifications indicating oil-filled or dry-type transformer. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows general site drainage patterns directed away from buildings through spot elevations and flow arrows, but transformer pad locations are not specifically identified with drainage callouts.","reasoning":"Without equipment type specification and specific drainage documentation at transformer pad locations, compliance with the oil-filled equipment drainage requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located 100% on private property within lot boundaries. No transformer pads straddle or encroach upon property lines or public right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review confirmed all four labeled transformer pad locations are positioned within the thick solid boundary line defining the property limits. Three pads (west side near Bldg 2 and 8; east side near Bldg 5) are near property boundaries but visually remain within private property.","reasoning":"All transformer pads are contained fully within the lot boundaries and do not encroach into the public right-of-way or straddle property lines.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plat (Sheet 2) shows recorded easements (25' drainage easement, 10' wastewater easement, 7.5' public utility easements, 5' electric easements) but transformer pad locations are not depicted on the plat. Transformer pads shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) cannot be precisely overlaid with easement boundaries to verify non-conflict.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat shows existing recorded easements across the property including drainage, utility, and electric easements. Electrical plan shows transformer pad locations in general site areas, but no explicit coordinate or dimension data allows precise overlay verification.","reasoning":"Without explicit easement boundary dimensions and transformer pad coordinates, definitive verification that transformer pads avoid all prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, overhead electric) cannot be completed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer easements (access easements around pads) are shown on the plat or electrical plan. The requirement for transformer easements with widths adequate for Austin Energy accessibility cannot be verified from submitted documents.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat (Sheet 2) shows standard utility easements (water, wastewater, electric, drainage, PUE) but no specific transformer pad access easement callouts or dedications. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads but no easement boundaries.","reasoning":"Transformer easements are not documented on any submitted plan sheet, indicating this requirement either was not addressed or was deferred to Austin Energy Design coordination post-approval.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad to meter routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to electrical meters on buildings stays completely within private property. Routing through interior driveways and site areas does not cross right-of-way or public easements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of electrical plan shows blue line routing (marked 'E' for electric) connecting transformer pads through interior site areas to electrical meters on buildings. The routing path remains fully within property boundaries and does not cross street rights-of-way or public easements.","reasoning":"The documented electrical service routing from transformers to meters is entirely on private property, satisfying the 100% private property routing requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad specifications are completely absent from the submitted site plans. Dimensions, service type (single or three-phase), and AE Design-approved detail sheet references are not provided. Plans show only general 'Electrical Transformer Pad' labels without technical specifications.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) identifies five transformer pad locations with text labels 'Electrical Transformer Pad' but provides no accompanying specifications, dimensions (length, width, depth), service type designation, or reference to AE Design detail sheets.","reasoning":"The complete absence of transformer pad specifications, dimensions, and AE Design detail sheet references indicates non-compliance with the requirement for transformer pads to match AE Design-approved details for the specified service type.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations near parking and vehicle circulation"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking areas, drive lanes, or vehicle circulation routes. No bollards (4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts) are shown on the plans protecting any transformer pads. Bollard protection is required but not depicted.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review confirmed all five transformer pad locations are positioned immediately adjacent to driveway curb lines and vehicle circulation areas, placing them within the 4-foot trigger threshold for bollard protection. However, no bollard symbols, specifications, or detail callouts appear on the electrical plan or detail sheets.","reasoning":"The proximity of all transformer pads to vehicle circulation (within 4 feet) triggers the bollard requirement per UCM § 1.10.4, but bollards are not shown on the submitted plans, indicating non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No customer-owned facilities (buildings, parking structures, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks) are proposed over or under Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities shown on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed buildings, parking garages, light fixtures, and site structures, with overhead electric lines (OHE) restricted to property boundaries. No proposed structures are positioned beneath or overlapping with overhead distribution lines.","reasoning":"Since no customer facilities are proposed in conflict with overhead AE distribution lines, this requirement does not apply to the project.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence"