 walls are on eastern property boundary approximately 20-30 feet from nearest transformer pad.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review identified existing retaining walls only on far eastern property boundary, with transformer pads located well interior to the site. Estimated distance using scale 1\"=20' is 20-30 feet.","reasoning":"The retaining walls do not meet the adjacency threshold for application of the 5-foot clearance requirement, making this item inapplicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fences or gates are shown adjacent to transformer pads on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of electrical site plan found no fences, gates, or barriers labeled or depicted near any of the five transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Since no adjacent fences exist, the clearance requirement from fences does not apply to this project.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No reduced clearances (less than 5 feet to buildings) are shown on plans. No AE Design written approval request for reduced clearances is documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"All measured clearances from transformer pads to buildings exceed 5 feet (minimum 11.5 feet), and no architectural notes or approvals indicate reduced clearance configurations.","reasoning":"Since all clearances meet or exceed the standard 5-foot requirement, the exception for reduced clearances (requiring AE Design approval) does not apply.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevations showing balconies or overhangs are provided in the electrical plan. The 2D site plan shows no architectural projections or overhang indicators above transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical site plan (Sheet 21) is a 2D overhead drawing showing only building footprints with solid outline lines. No dashed lines, architectural projections, balconies, or overhang elements are depicted above or adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Building elevations are not included in the electrical plan document, preventing definitive assessment. However, the site plan shows no indication of overhangs. This item would require architectural elevation sheets for complete verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No windows, doors, or ventilating ducts with less than 5 feet lateral separation are identified adjacent to transformer pads on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical site plan shows transformer pads positioned at minimum 11.5 feet from buildings. No specific windows, doors, or HVAC ducts are labeled on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The visual site plan positioning and measured clearances suggest adequate separation. Detailed architectural elevations would be needed to identify low windows/doors requiring 12-foot clearance for oil-filled equipment, but none are indicated on available plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"d