roject.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pad hot-stick use areas maintain minimum 10-foot clearance to open areas or adjacent buildings in all directions. Measured distances range from 11.5 to 72.7 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pads shows clearances in all directions exceed 10 feet minimum: west of Bldg 1 (21.3 ft to building), west of Bldg 2 (50.5 ft), west of Bldg 8 (53 ft), east of Bldg 5 (72.7 ft), east of Bldg 4/7 (19.1 ft). Open areas are also confirmed adjacent with no obstructions within 10 feet.","reasoning":"All measured clearances from transformer pad access door sides exceed the 10-foot minimum required clearance to buildings and open areas.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche, vault, or enclosed area configurations are indicated on the site plans. All transformer pad locations are in open areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows all transformer pads positioned in outdoor areas adjacent to driveways and landscaping, with no indication of niche installations or enclosed areas.","reasoning":"Since no confined space or niche configurations are proposed, the 15-foot confined space clearance requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire hydrant locations are not shown on the electrical plan where transformer pads are d