ision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from storm drain lines. Measured distances range from 16.2 to 76.7 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pads to storm drain lines (marked 'SD') shows: near Bldg 1 (76.7 ft), near Bldg 2 (51.1 ft), near Bldg 8 (19.2 ft), east of Bldg 4 (33.6 ft), east of Bldg 7 (16.2 ft).","reasoning":"All measured clearances exceed the 5-foot minimum required horizontal separation from storm drain utility lines.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas utility service is shown on the utility plans. Gas line clearance requirement does not apply to this project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of utility plan identified water, wastewater, and storm drain utilities but no gas utility lines are labeled or depicted near transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Since no gas service is proposed for the site, the gas line clearance requirement (24-36 inches depending on pressure) is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground utility lines are shown on plans and appear to maintain adequate spacing, but specific 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearances from transformer pads are not dimensionally labeled or documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan and electrical plan show underground utility locations (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric) with visual spacing that appears to exceed 12-inch minimum. However, no explicit dimension callouts or spacing table is provided for underground utility separations at transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Visual inspection suggests adequate spacing, but without explicit dimensional documentation or clearance verification notes, the 12-inch minimum clearance requirement cannot be definitively verified from submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations and underground electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Whether customer facilities (buildings, parking structures) are installed over or under Austin Energy underground electric facilities cannot be verified from submitted site plans without Austin Energy Design consultation documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows transformer pads, buildings, and underground electric lines but does not explicitly document AE Design approval for any structures positioned over underground electric conduits or vice versa.","reasoning":"This requirement requires coordination with and documentation from Austin Energy Design, which is not included in the submitted site plan package.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution line conductors. Measured distances to overhead lines range from 18.3 to 73.4 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of transformer pads to overhead electric lines (marked 'OHE') shows: Bldg 1 to north OHE (18.3 ft), Bldg 1 to west OHE (73.4 ft), Bldg 2 to west OHE (68.2 ft), Bldg 8 to west OHE (63.8 ft), Bldg 8 to south OHE (41.7 ft), Bldg 7 to south OHE (57.2 ft).","reasoning":"All measured clearances significantly exceed the 7.5-foot minimum required horizontal clearance from overhead distribution conductors.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors. Overhead lines are restricted to far outer perimeters of site; all transformer pads are interior with 40+ feet clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review confirmed overhead electric lines (OHE) are located along western, southern, and eastern property boundaries. All transformer pads are positioned in interior site areas adjacent to buildings and driveways, with visual scale measurement confirming 40+ feet minimum separation.","reasoning":"The significant separation (40+ feet) between perimeter overhead conductors and interior transformer pad locations substantially exceeds the 15-foot radius minimum requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installation is indicated on the site plans. All transformer pads are in standard outdoor ground-level configuration.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows transformer pads positioned in open outdoor areas adjacent to driveways and buildings with no notation of enclosed, notched-out, or niche-type configurations.","reasoning":"Since niche service (specialized enclosed installation within building footprint) is not proposed, the 35-foot vertical clearance requirement for niches does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installation is proposed. Fire wall ratings and ventilation specifications for niche service therefore do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan and architectural documents show no indication of niche service configuration or enclosed transformer installations within building footprints.","reasoning":"Since niche service is not proposed, architectural fire rating and ventilation requirements for niche installations do not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations with overhead structures or parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":17}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings provided are limited to drainage/conveyance profiles (Sheet 17). No cross-sections specifically demonstrating vertical clearances from transformer pad access paths to overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 17 contains six cross-sections titled 'Conveyance Cross Sections' depicting drainage channel profiles for 25-year and 100-year storm events, with no transformer pad access path clearance information.","reasoning":"While overhead structures exist at the site (buildings, parking areas), no specific cross-section drawings document the vertical clearance from transformer pad locations through access paths to overhead structures, preventing verification of this requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on electrical plan, so applicability of drainage requirement cannot be determined. Grading plan shows surface drainage slopes away from buildings generally, but specific drainage direction at transformer pad locations is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan provides no equipment specifications indicating oil-filled or dry-type transformer. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows general site drainage patterns directed away from buildings through spot elevations and flow arrows, but transformer pad locations are not specifically identified with drainage callouts.","reasoning":"Without equipment type specification and specific drainage documentation at transformer pad locations, compliance with the oil-filled equipment drainage requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located 100% on private property within lot boundaries. No transformer pads straddle or encroach upon property lines or public right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review confirmed all four labeled transformer pad locations are positioned within the thick solid boundary line defining the property limits. Three pads (west side near Bldg 2 and 8; east side near Bldg 5) are near property boundaries but visually remain within private property.","reasoning":"All transformer pads are contained fully within the lot boundaries and do not encroach into the public right-of-way or straddle property lines.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plat (Sheet 2) shows recorded easements (25' drainage easement, 10' wastewater easement, 7.5' public utility easements, 5' electric easements) but transformer pad locations are not depicted on the plat. Transformer pads shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) cannot be precisely overlaid with easement boundaries to verify non-conflict.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat shows existing recorded easements across the property including drainage, utility, and electric easements. Electrical plan shows transformer pad locations in general site areas, but no explicit coordinate or dimension data allows precise overlay verification.","reasoning":"Without explicit easement boundary dimensions and transformer pad coordinates, definitive verification that transformer pads avoid all prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, overhead electric) cannot be completed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer easements (access easements around pads) are shown on the plat or electrical plan. The requirement for transformer easements with widths adequate for Austin Energy accessibility cannot be verified from submitted documents.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat (Sheet 2) shows standard utility easements (water, wastewater, electric, drainage, PUE) but no specific transformer pad access easement callouts or dedications. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads but no easement boundaries.","reasoning":"Transformer easements are not documented on any submitted plan sheet, indicating this requirement either was not addressed or was deferred to Austin Energy Design coordination post-approval.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad to meter routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to electrical meters on buildings stays completely within private property. Routing through interior driveways and site areas does not cross right-of-way or public easements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of electrical plan shows blue line routing (marked 'E' for electric) connecting transformer pads through interior site areas to electrical meters on buildings. The routing path remains fully within property boundaries and does not cross street rights-of-way or public easements.","reasoning":"The documented electrical service routing from transformers to meters is entirely on private property, satisfying the 100% private property routing requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad specifications are completely absent from the submitted site plans. Dimensions, service type (single or three-phase), and AE Design-approved detail sheet references are not provided. Plans show only general 'Electrical Transformer Pad' labels without technical specifications.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) identifies five transformer pad locations with text labels 'Electrical Transformer Pad' but provides no accompanying specifications, dimensions (length, width, depth), service type designation, or reference to AE Design detail sheets.","reasoning":"The complete absence of transformer pad specifications, dimensions, and AE Design detail sheet references indicates non-compliance with the requirement for transformer pads to match AE Design-approved details for the specified service type.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations near parking and vehicle circulation"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking areas, drive lanes, or vehicle circulation routes. No bollards (4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts) are shown on the plans protecting any transformer pads. Bollard protection is required but not depicted.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review confirmed all five transformer pad locations are positioned immediately adjacent to driveway curb lines and vehicle circulation areas, placing them within the 4-foot trigger threshold for bollard protection. However, no bollard symbols, specifications, or detail callouts appear on the electrical plan or detail sheets.","reasoning":"The proximity of all transformer pads to vehicle circulation (within 4 feet) triggers the bollard requirement per UCM § 1.10.4, but bollards are not shown on the submitted plans, indicating non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No customer-owned facilities (buildings, parking structures, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks) are proposed over or under Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities shown on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed buildings, parking garages, light fixtures, and site structures, with overhead electric lines (OHE) restricted to property boundaries. No proposed structures are positioned beneath or overlapping with overhead distribution lines.","reasoning":"Since no customer facilities are proposed in conflict with overhead AE distribution lines, this requirement does not apply to the project.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d877a97d-aa67-4bfe-b449-1c3573035d63"}
